[3143.284, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m bash submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 400 2>&1 | tail -10\r\nsubmission/testbench/sdf_checker_400.sv:82: warning: Omitting $sdf_annotate() since specify blocks are being omitted.\r\nwaves 400: first write 21250 ps, drain start 181250 ps, drain end 341250 ps\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_drainend_gate.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_drainend_rtl.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_fill_gate.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_fill_rtl.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_full_gate.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_full_rtl.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_zoom_gate.png\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/fig/wave_400_zoom_rtl.png\r\n"]
[3163.251, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -i 's|  convert $2 -crop +0+105 +repage $2      # drop the window title and toolbar|  convert $2 -crop +0+105 +repage -gravity south -chop 0x40 +repage $2   # drop title bar, toolbar, empty strip|' submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh && bash submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 400 2>&1 | grep \"^waves\" && bash submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 800 2>&1 | grep \"^waves\"\r\nwaves 400: first write 21250 ps, drain start 181250 ps, drain end 341250 ps\r\nwaves 800: first write 15625 ps, drain start 95625 ps, drain end 175625 ps\r\n"]
[3184.241, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat >> notes/WORKLOG.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n**04:35 Candidate (C), Baugh-Wooley + Dadda (subagent, `build/cand_dadda/`).**\r\n- *Best version (v6):* WNS +0.150 ns, hold +0.076 ns, 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2, 616 flops, latency 8, check/sim ALL PASS.\r\n- *Power (\u00b5W):*\r\n\r\n  | case | (C) Dadda v6 | (A) Booth/CSA |\r\n  |---|---|---|\r\n  | whole run | 3279 | 3073 |\r\n  | fill window | 5725 | 5210 |\r\n  | drain window | 2702 | 2536 |\r\n  | vectorless | 2820 | 2728 |\r\n\r\n- *Control:* it independently found the same control problem (ptr/RDY port load) and solved it with inverted twin registers and split 3-bit counters.\r\n- *Two smaller variants it rejected:* v7 drops the product register (writeMem_val comes from logic); v8 puts the PP/tree logic on the input path (0.97 ns), which is risky for the sign-off testbench.\r\n\r\n**Decision for 800 MHz: (A) Booth/CSA `z800_1101`.**\r\n- Both (A) and (C) meet the 62 ps target. (A) has 10 % less area (4755 vs 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2) and 6\u20139 % less power in every case, which SPEC Section 5 ranks after timing and area.\r\n- (C) has twice the slack margin (150 ps vs 75 ps), but the target is met by both.\r\n- (B), retiming, fails timing (\u22120.20 ns) and needs reset re-insertion; rejected.\r\n\r\n**04:40 Mutation test at 800 MHz** (`submission/scripts/mutate.sh 800`): 13/13 mutants killed. The extra mutants vs 400 are EN_writeMem one cycle early, the inverted port copy not reset, and a carry-select carry-in error in mult_pipe.\r\n\r\n**04:45 Waveform figures** (`submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 400|800`). The same gate-level checker drives the RTL and the SDF-annotated netlist, so the waves line up. GTKWave 3.3.116 runs under `xvfb-run` with `-S` Tcl scripts (`/File/Grab_To_File`), light colours set by `--rcvar`, and ImageMagick crops. Windows: first writes, transition to drain, end of drain, and a 3-cycle zoom.\r\n\r\nGate-level only effects visible in the zoom:\r\n- clock-to-output delay of 0.45\u20130.7 ns on the registered outputs at 400 MHz;\r\n- a short intermediate value on writeMem_val while bits with different clk\u2192Q settle;\r\n- EN_readMem following EN_blockRead (driven 20 ps after the edge) through one AND gate.\r\n\r\nRDY_mult is a register output in both designs, so it shows no glitch.\r\nEOF\r\ngit add -A submission notes Makefile && git status --short | grep -v \"^A\\|^M\" | head; git commit -q -m \"Checkpoint 3: 800 MHz implementation (Booth/CSA, 7 ranks), flow knobs per frequency, F14 SAT check, mutation tests, waveform figures\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126GMUJKG14LrQMZ4a6y2it\" && git push -q origin claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i 2>&1 | tail -1; git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/check/800 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline | head -2; git fetch -q origin check-results 2>&1 | tail -1\r\nremote: \r\nb6917e9 Checkpoint 3: 800 MHz implementation (Booth/CSA, 7 ranks), flow knobs per frequency, F14 SAT check, mutation tests, waveform figures\r\n60ed005 Checkpoint 2: 400 MHz implementation, checkers, synthesis, timing, gate-level checks\r\nfatal: couldn't find remote ref check-results\r\n"]
[3214.841, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m D=build/noiso400 && mkdir -p $D/rtl && cp submission/rtl_400/*.sv $D/rtl/ && grep -n \"!RST_N || !en\" $D/rtl/mult_pipe.sv | head -3 && sed -i 's/if (!RST_N || !en) begin/if (!RST_N) begin/' $D/rtl/mult_pipe.sv && sed -i 's/            end else begin\\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q/X/' $D/rtl/mult_pipe.sv && grep -n \"if (!RST_N) begin$\" $D/rtl/mult_pipe.sv | head; make synth check sim power RUN=400 RTL_DIR=$D/rtl BUILD=$D REP=$D/rep NETLIST=$D/map.v SDF=$D/map.sdf 2>&1 | grep -E \"^worst slack max|cell area|^ALL PASS|window|estimate\"\r\n49:            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n60:            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n49:            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n149:            if (!RST_N) begin\r\nworst slack max -0.146\r\ncell area 2337.874 um^2 (sequential 751.716 um^2, 1478 instances)\r\nALL PASS\r\nALL PASS\r\nsynthesis estimate (vectorless, activity 0.1)         500.68    223.19     32.01    755.88\r\nrun: window whole run                                 774.85    593.91     33.27   1402.00\r\nfill: window 521250..681250 ps                        809.52    628.31     33.31   1471.10\r\ndrain: window 688750..848750 ps                       370.78     24.49     33.37    428.64\r\n"]
[3229.95, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p submission/syn_reports/400/experiments && cp build/noiso400/rep/power_summary.txt submission/syn_reports/400/experiments/no_operand_isolation_power.txt && cp build/noiso400/rep/power.rpt submission/syn_reports/400/experiments/no_operand_isolation_power.rpt && grep -E \"^worst|cell area\" build/noiso400/rep/sta.rpt > submission/syn_reports/400/experiments/no_operand_isolation_sta_summary.txt && cat >> notes/WORKLOG.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 4: power\r\n\r\nActivity-based power uses OpenSTA `read_vcd` on the zero-delay gate-level VCD of `make sim`, which runs the full RTL-checker stimulus. It is reported for the whole run and for the two 64-cycle windows announced by the checker (`PWR_WIN`, passed as `-begin_time/-end_time`). The vectorless \"synthesis estimate\" is `report_power` with OpenSTA's default input activity of 0.1. Reports: `submission/syn_reports/<RUN>/{sta.rpt,power.rpt,power_summary.txt}`.\r\n\r\nPower in \u00b5W, slow corner (0.95 V, 125 \u00b0C):\r\n\r\n| case | 400 MHz | 800 MHz |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| vectorless estimate | 652.5 | 2727.6 |\r\n| whole run | 642.8 | 3073.1 |\r\n| fill window (64 back-to-back accepts) | 1480.1 | 5209.5 |\r\n| drain window (64 back-to-back reads, producer idle) | 430.4 | 2535.6 |\r\n\r\nIn the drain window, sequential internal (clock) power dominates: 158 flops at 400 MHz and 577 at 800 MHz, with no clock gating.\r\n\r\n**Operand-isolation experiment** (400 MHz, `build/noiso400`; operand registers load the inputs every cycle instead of zeros when nothing is accepted). Files: `submission/syn_reports/400/experiments/`.\r\n- Area: 2337.9 \u00b5m\u00b2, against 2386.6 \u00b5m\u00b2 with isolation.\r\n- Power: whole run 1402.0 \u00b5W (+118 %), fill window 1471.1 \u00b5W, drain window 428.6 \u00b5W. The windows hardly change because the checker keeps the producer quiet in the drain window. Over the whole run, the random operands presented while not ready (F5/F11 stimulus) toggle the multiplier without isolation.\r\n- Vectorless estimate: 755.9 \u00b5W.\r\n- Isolation costs about 49 \u00b5m\u00b2 of gating and removes about 54 % of the whole-run power.\r\n\r\nGlitch power is not included, because the VCD is from the zero-delay simulation that SPEC Section 7 prescribes for `sim`. This is noted in the report.\r\nEOF\r\ngit add -A submission notes && git commit -q -m \"Checkpoint 4: activity-based power at both frequencies, operand-isolation experiment\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126GMUJKG14LrQMZ4a6y2it\" && git push -q origin claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline | head -1\r\n4fe0298 Checkpoint 4: activity-based power at both frequencies, operand-isolation experiment\r\n"]
[3246.371, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m which dot rsvg-convert pandoc pdflatex xelatex lualatex; pandoc --version | head -1; kpsewhich tikz.sty listings.sty booktabs.sty longtable.sty xcolor.sty geometry.sty fancyvrb.sty 2>&1; cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open && git fetch -q origin check-results 2>&1 | tail -1; git ls-remote origin 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"pull\" | head\r\n/usr/bin/dot\r\n/usr/bin/pandoc\r\n/usr/bin/pdflatex\r\n/usr/bin/lualatex\r\npandoc 3.1.3\r\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/listings/listings.sty\r\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/booktabs/booktabs.sty\r\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/tools/longtable.sty\r\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/xcolor/xcolor.sty\r\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/geometry/geometry.sty\r\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/fancyvrb/fancyvrb.sty\r\nfatal: couldn't find remote ref check-results\r\n045bcfe98ed9069c5219ea28dd7114adf25a1fc7\tHEAD\r\n60ed0055857b5f2f41f2a12213d6ee380ae3c3e5\trefs/heads/check/400\r\nb6917e9eb1c8eacf0fcc36b69ccbf3cc0057c890\trefs/heads/check/800\r\n4fe0298b300580abf2d0cd11816712f1dc743f14\trefs/heads/claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i\r\na2d8828ede1a5d3a4cc49448cbb4ee3fae0c1451\trefs/heads/live-log\r\n045bcfe98ed9069c5219ea28dd7114adf25a1fc7\trefs/heads/main\r\n"]
[3251.856, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m for r in 400 800; do echo \"== $r\"; build/exp/path.sh submission/syn_reports/$r/sta.rpt | sed -n '3,30p' | grep -v \"data arrival\\|^ *-\" ; for k in 1; do awk '/^Startpoint/{n++} n==1' submission/syn_reports/$r/sta.rpt | grep -E \"^(Startpoint|Endpoint)|library setup|clock clk \\(rise edge\\)\" | head -6; done; done\r\n== 400\r\n_2923_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=16 d=0.658 t=0.658\r\n_2613_/ZN (AOI22_X1) fo=1 d=0.128 t=0.786\r\n_2614_/ZN (XNOR2_X1) fo=3 d=0.252 t=1.038\r\n_2635_/ZN (XNOR2_X1) fo=1 d=0.174 t=1.212\r\n_2636_/ZN (XNOR2_X1) fo=3 d=0.185 t=1.397\r\n_2671_/Z (XOR2_X1) fo=1 d=0.222 t=1.619\r\n_2672_/ZN (XNOR2_X1) fo=2 d=0.173 t=1.792\r\n_2818_/ZN (XNOR2_X1) fo=1 d=0.161 t=1.953\r\n_2819_/Z (XOR2_X1) fo=1 d=0.166 t=2.120\r\n_2820_/ZN (AND2_X1) fo=1 d=0.115 t=2.235\r\n_2821_/Z (BUF_X2) fo=1 d=0.065 t=2.300\r\nslack (MET) fo=0.152 d= t=\r\nStartpoint: _2923_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nEndpoint: _2843_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\n                   0.312    0.000    0.000   clock clk (rise edge)\r\n                   0.312    2.500    2.500   clock clk (rise edge)\r\n                           -0.048    2.452   library setup time\r\n== 800\r\n_4404_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=3 d=0.413 t=0.413\r\n_3888_/Z (XOR2_X2) fo=1 d=0.192 t=0.606\r\n_3889_/ZN (XNOR2_X2) fo=4 d=0.173 t=0.779\r\n_4003_/Z (XOR2_X2) fo=1 d=0.200 t=0.979\r\n_4004_/ZN (OAI21_X2) fo=1 d=0.055 t=1.034\r\n_4005_/ZN (AOI21_X2) fo=1 d=0.079 t=1.113\r\nslack (MET) fo=0.075 d= t=\r\nStartpoint: _4404_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nEndpoint: _4294_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\n                   0.156    0.000    0.000   clock clk (rise edge)\r\n                   0.156    1.250    1.250   clock clk (rise edge)\r\n                           -0.063    1.187   library setup time\r\n"]
[3256.616, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m for r in 400 800; do for i in _2923_ _2843_ _4404_ _4294_; do grep -A3 \" $i (\" submission/outputs/mkMultBuff_${r}_map.v | grep -o \"\\.Q([^)]*)\" ; done; done; grep -h \"F14CHECK\\|^cell area\" submission/syn_reports/*/f14.log submission/syn_reports/*/sta.rpt; for r in 400 800; do grep -E \"^worst|tns\" submission/syn_reports/$r/timing_fail/sta.rpt; grep -E \"summary|^TIMING FAIL:\" submission/syn_reports/$r/timing_fail/timing.log; done; grep -E \"^cell (DFF|FA|HA)\" submission/syn_reports/*/sta.rpt\r\n.Q(\\u_mult.a17 [8])\r\n.Q(\\u_mult.l3q [12])\r\n.Q(\\u_mult.l1q [75])\r\n.Q(\\u_mult.l3q [11])\r\nF14CHECK: flops 166, reset-gated 166 (of which reset-to-1 1), NOT reset-gated 0: \r\nF14CHECK: flops 577, reset-gated 577 (of which reset-to-1 15), NOT reset-gated 0: \r\ncell area 2386.552 um^2 (sequential 753.844 um^2, 1501 instances)\r\ncell area 4755.016 um^2 (sequential 2609.194 um^2, 2429 instances)\r\nworst slack max -1.469\r\nworst slack min 0.055\r\ntns max -23.169\r\n==== mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_400 summary: period 2.500 ns, seed 402, latency 2, 887 cycles, 384 accepted, 384 returned, 172 failure(s) ====\r\nTIMING FAIL: 172 failure(s)\r\nworst slack max -1.091\r\nworst slack min 0.073\r\ntns max -67.793\r\n==== mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_800 summary: period 1.250 ns, seed 402, latency 3, 4070 cycles, 64 accepted, 0 returned, 3 failure(s) ====\r\nTIMING FAIL: 3 failure(s)\r\nsubmission/syn_reports/400/sta.rpt:cell DFF_X1           160    723.520 um^2\r\nsubmission/syn_reports/400/sta.rpt:cell DFF_X2             6     30.324 um^2\r\nsubmission/syn_reports/800/sta.rpt:cell DFF_X1           577   2609.194 um^2\r\n"]
[3282.729, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p /home/user/elec402-p2-open/submission/pdf_report/fig /home/user/elec402-p2-open/submission/pdf_report/src && cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/submission/pdf_report/src && cat > fsm.dot <<'EOF'\r\ndigraph fsm {\r\n  rankdir=LR; bgcolor=white; fontname=\"Helvetica\";\r\n  node [shape=circle, fontname=\"Helvetica\", fontsize=11, width=1.3, fixedsize=true];\r\n  edge [fontname=\"Helvetica\", fontsize=9];\r\n  rst [shape=point, width=0.12];\r\n  FILL  [label=\"FILL\\nRDY_mult=1\\nRDY_blockRead=0\"];\r\n  WAIT  [label=\"WAIT\\nRDY_mult=0\\nRDY_blockRead=0\"];\r\n  DRAIN [label=\"DRAIN\\nRDY_mult=0\\nRDY_blockRead=1\"];\r\n  rst -> FILL [label=\"RST_N=0\\n(from any state)\"];\r\n  FILL -> FILL [label=\"accept & acc_q<63\\n/ acc_q++\"];\r\n  FILL -> WAIT [label=\"accept & acc_q=63\\n/ acc_q:=0\"];\r\n  WAIT -> WAIT [label=\"write & wp<63\"];\r\n  WAIT -> DRAIN [label=\"write & wp=63\\n(EN_writeMem, addr 63)\"];\r\n  DRAIN -> DRAIN [label=\"read & rp<63\\n/ rp++\"];\r\n  DRAIN -> FILL [label=\"read & rp=63\\n(accepted read of addr 63)\"];\r\n}\r\nEOF\r\ncat > dp400.dot <<'EOF'\r\ndigraph dp400 {\r\n  rankdir=LR; bgcolor=white; nodesep=0.25; ranksep=0.3;\r\n  node [fontname=\"Helvetica\", fontsize=10];\r\n  edge [fontname=\"Helvetica\", fontsize=9];\r\n  in [shape=plaintext, label=\"mult_input0 (a)\\nmult_input1 (b)\\nEN_mult & RDY_mult\"];\r\n  enc [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"Booth radix-4\\nrecode b\\n(one, two, neg)\\n+ operand isolation\"];\r\n  r1 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"Rank 1\\na 16b + digits 24b\\n(+ valid v[0])\"];\r\n  pp [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"select 8 PP rows\\n17b + '+1' bits\\n+ constant row K\"];\r\n  c12 [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"3:2 levels 1-2\\n9 -> 6 -> 4 rows\"];\r\n  r2 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"Rank 2\\n4 carry-save rows\\n(+ v[1])\"];\r\n  c34 [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"3:2 levels 3-4\\n4 -> 3 -> 2 rows\"];\r\n  cpa [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"32-bit\\nKogge-Stone\\nadder\"];\r\n  r3 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"Rank 3\\nproduct 32b\\n(+ v[2])\"];\r\n  out [shape=plaintext, label=\"writeMem_val\\nEN_writeMem = v[2]\\nwriteMem_addr = ptr\"];\r\n  in -> enc -> r1 -> pp -> c12 -> r2 -> c34 -> cpa -> r3 -> out;\r\n}\r\nEOF\r\ncat > dp800.dot <<'EOF'\r\ndigraph dp800 {\r\n  rankdir=LR; bgcolor=white; nodesep=0.2; ranksep=0.22;\r\n  node [fontname=\"Helvetica\", fontsize=9];\r\n  in [shape=plaintext, label=\"a, b,\\nEN_mult &\\nRDY_mult\"];\r\n  enc [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"Booth\\nrecode b\\n+ isolation\"];\r\n  r1 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R1\\na 16b\\ndigits 24b\"];\r\n  pp [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"select\\n8 PP rows\"];\r\n  r2 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R2\\n8x17b PP\\n+ 8 '+1'\"];\r\n  c1 [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"3:2 L1\\n9->6\"];\r\n  r3 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R3\\n6 rows\"];\r\n  c23 [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"3:2 L2, L3\\n6->4->3\"];\r\n  r4 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R4\\n3 rows\"];\r\n  c4 [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"3:2 L4\\n3->2\\ng=c&s\\np=c^s\"];\r\n  r5 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R5\\ng, p\\n32b+32b\"];\r\n  ca [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"4-bit block\\nprefix:\\nsums for\\ncin=0/1,\\nblock carries\"];\r\n  r6 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R6\\ns0, s1\\nco0, co1\"];\r\n  cb [shape=box, style=rounded, label=\"block-carry\\nprefix (8)\\n+ select\"];\r\n  r7 [shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#dde8f5\", label=\"R7\\nproduct\\n32b\"];\r\n  out [shape=plaintext, label=\"writeMem_val\\nEN_writeMem\\n(v[6] copy)\"];\r\n  in -> enc -> r1 -> pp -> r2 -> c1 -> r3 -> c23 -> r4 -> c4 -> r5 -> ca -> r6 -> cb -> r7 -> out;\r\n}\r\nEOF\r\nfor f in fsm dp400 dp800; do dot -Tpng -Gdpi=200 $f.dot -o ../fig/$f.png; done; ls -la ../fig/ | head -30\r\nWarning: node 'FILL', graph 'fsm' size too small for label\r\nWarning: node 'WAIT', graph 'fsm' size too small for label\r\nWarning: node 'DRAIN', graph 'fsm' size too small for label\r\ntotal 1064\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root   4096 Nov  8 03:28 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root   4096 Nov  8 03:28 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 122181 Nov  8 03:28 dp400.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 115687 Nov  8 03:28 dp800.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 144334 Nov  8 03:28 fsm.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  42381 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_drainend_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  41282 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_drainend_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  40203 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_fill_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  39527 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_fill_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  45119 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_full_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  42922 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_full_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  38455 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_zoom_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  37642 Nov  8 03:26 wave_400_zoom_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  42539 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_drainend_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  42543 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_drainend_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  43316 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_fill_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  43694 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_fill_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  42939 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_full_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  41598 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_full_rtl.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  35988 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_zoom_gate.png\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  35651 Nov  8 03:26 wave_800_zoom_rtl.png\r\n"]
[3286.165, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -i 's/width=1.3, fixedsize=true/width=1.6, fixedsize=true/' fsm.dot && dot -Tpng -Gdpi=200 fsm.dot -o ../fig/fsm.png 2>&1; echo done\r\ndone\r\n"]
[3299.078, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /tmp/claude-0/bundled-skills/2.1.319/146a918be3f9b457ebf440078c1e9589/claude-api && grep -rn -i \"1.25\\|2x\\|2\u00d7\\|multiplier\\|cache write\\|0\\.1x\\|10%\" shared/prompt-caching.md | head -15; ls ~/.claude/projects/; ls ~/.claude/projects/* | head\r\n144:**Economics:** Cache reads cost ~0.1\u00d7 base input price - **0.025\u00d7 on Claude Fable 5.1** ($0.25/MTok, on Claude Mythos 5.1 too) and 0.05\u00d7 on Claude Opus 5.5 ($0.20/MTok), which moves every break-even below proportionally. Cache writes cost **1.25\u00d7 for 5-minute TTL, 2\u00d7 for 1-hour TTL**. Break-even depends on TTL: with 5-minute TTL, two requests break even (1.25\u00d7 + 0.1\u00d7 = 1.35\u00d7 vs 2\u00d7 uncached); with 1-hour TTL, you need at least three requests (2\u00d7 + 0.2\u00d7 = 2.2\u00d7 vs 3\u00d7 uncached). The 1-hour TTL keeps entries alive across gaps in bursty traffic, but the doubled write cost means it needs more reads to pay off.\r\n153:| 5-60 minutes (a user who replies after 20 minutes; an agentic side-task or a generation that runs past 5 minutes between reads) | 1-hour - the only window where the 2\u00d7 write pays off |\r\n156:**Claude Fable 5.1 / Claude Mythos 5.1: a keep-alive is usually cheaper than the 1-hour TTL.** With cache reads at 0.025x on Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 (versus 0.05x on Claude Opus 5.5 and 0.1x elsewhere - see Economics above) a miss is much more expensive *relative to a hit*, and a read is nearly free - so for the 5-60 minute gap, instead of paying the 2x write for the 1-hour TTL, stay on the default 5-minute TTL and, while idle, re-send the previous request with `max_tokens: 0` shortly before the entry would expire. That request refreshes the entry's timer and bills only a cheap cache read (no output tokens). At Claude Fable 5.1 prices this beats the 1-hour TTL unless pauses regularly approach an hour. `max_tokens: 0` follows \u00a7 Pre-warming's rejected combinations; on these models the ones that can arise are `stream: true`, structured outputs, and Batches (forced `tool_choice` and `thinking.type: \"enabled\"` are already 400s here). Send the keep-alive with `stream` off - streaming is a transport option, not part of the cached prefix, so dropping it for this one request costs nothing - and where the request can't be reshaped that way, with structured outputs (`output_config.format`) or inside a Message Batches request, use the 1-hour TTL instead. The prompt-caching page (`shared/live-sources.md`) has a cost comparison on a sample workload and an example keep-alive request.\r\n186:| `cache_creation_input_tokens` | Tokens written to cache this request (you paid the ~1.25\u00d7 write premium) |\r\n208:**Unexplained writes:** `usage.cache_creation` breaks `cache_creation_input_tokens` down by TTL (`ephemeral_5m_input_tokens` / `ephemeral_1h_input_tokens`). Server tools such as web search automatically insert a 5-minute cache write after tool results when the request already uses caching - writes at a position you didn't mark; expected behavior, not an invalidator.\r\n271:| You'd pre-warm many distinct prefixes speculatively | Each is a ~1.25\u00d7 write; cost can exceed the latency you save |\r\n-home-user-elec402-p2-open\r\n6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca\r\n6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca.jsonl\r\nShell cwd was reset to /home/user/elec402-p2-open\r\n"]
[3307.738, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m ls -R ~/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/ | head -20; head -c 1500 ~/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca.jsonl | head -3; grep -m1 '\"usage\"' ~/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca.jsonl | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.keys()); print(d['message']['model'], d['message']['id'], d.get('requestId'), d['message']['usage'])\"\r\n/root/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/:\r\n6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca\r\n6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca.jsonl\r\n\r\n/root/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca:\r\nccr-tip.json\r\nsubagents\r\n\r\n/root/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca/subagents:\r\nagent-a6f0b6a42071b2e9a.jsonl\r\nagent-a6f0b6a42071b2e9a.meta.json\r\nagent-a6f0b6a42071b2e9a.prefix.json\r\nagent-a88f77038c8c3d60d.jsonl\r\nagent-a88f77038c8c3d60d.meta.json\r\nagent-a88f77038c8c3d60d.prefix.json\r\nagent-ac434250e4d261355.jsonl\r\nagent-ac434250e4d261355.meta.json\r\nagent-ac434250e4d261355.prefix.json\r\n{\"type\":\"queue-operation\",\"operation\":\"enqueue\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-08T02:33:34.035Z\",\"sessionId\":\"6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca\",\"content\":\"Read CLAUDE.md and SPEC.md first, then complete the project end to end. Commit and push at the end of each checkpoint, and keep notes/WORKLOG.md current as you go. The checkpoints are:\\n\\n1. Toolchain. Write the install script and the make targets from Section 7. Get Nangate45 at its slowest available corner, and Verilog cell models with timing (specify blocks) for gate-level simulation. If apt doesn't have OpenSTA or OpenROAD, use their Docker images. Find out early whether your simulator turns setup/hold violations into X, since Section 8.2 depends on it. Record every tool version. If you can't get a working toolchain, stop and tell me exactly what's missing.\\n\\n2. 400 MHz. Write the RTL and the RTL checker. Have a subagent write the checkers from SPEC.md without looking at the RTL. Get make check RUN=400 to ALL PASS. If the checker and the RTL disagree, decide from the spec which one is wrong, and never weaken a check to make it pass. Then do synthesis, timing, area and the gate-level checker, including a netlist that is guaranteed to fail. Once that is done, push a branch named check/400 for sign-off and keep working without waiting for the result.\\n\\n3. 800 MHz. Have parallel subagents evaluate two or three candidate microarchitectures, for example a deeper pipeline with retiming, or an explicit partial-product tree (Booth edict_keys(['parentUuid', 'isSidechain', 'message', 'thinkingDurationMs', 'thinkingDisplay', 'serverClassifierRequest', 'apiBlockIndex', 'requestId', 'requestedModel', 'promptCacheRequested', 'type', 'uuid', 'timestamp', 'advisorModel', 'effort', 'perTurnEffort', 'userType', 'entrypoint', 'cwd', 'sessionId', 'version', 'gitBranch'])\r\nclaude-opus-5-5 msg_011CgpgLAg1zYoqP1vbWn6dp req_011CgpgLALv2YZqZa4d1kghV {'input_tokens': 2, 'cache_creation_input_tokens': 20949, 'cache_read_input_tokens': 63062, 'output_tokens': 137, 'output_tokens_details': {'thinking_tokens': 25}, 'server_tool_use': {'web_search_requests': 0, 'web_fetch_requests': 0}, 'service_tier': 'standard', 'cache_creation': {'ephemeral_1h_input_tokens': 20949, 'ephemeral_5m_input_tokens': 0}, 'inference_geo': 'global', 'iterations': [{'input_tokens': 2, 'output_tokens': 137, 'cache_read_input_tokens': 63062, 'cache_creation_input_tokens': 20949, 'cache_creation': {'ephemeral_5m_input_tokens': 0, 'ephemeral_1h_input_tokens': 20949}, 'type': 'message'}], 'speed': 'standard', 'fallback_credit': None}\r\n"]
