[16389.677, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\np='submission/scripts/token_usage.py'\r\ns=open(p).read()\r\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    who = 'main session' if '/subagents/' not in f else 'subagent ' + os.path.basename(f)[6:-6]\"\"\",\r\n\"\"\"    who = 'main session'\r\n    if '/subagents/' in f:\r\n        try:\r\n            who = 'subagent: ' + json.load(open(f[:-6] + '.meta.json'))['description']\r\n        except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError):\r\n            who = 'subagent ' + os.path.basename(f)[6:-6]\"\"\")\r\nold=s[s.index(\"cols = ['requests'\"):]\r\nnew='''cols = ['requests', 'input', 'output', 'cache_write_5m', 'cache_write_1h', 'cache_read']\r\nheads = ['responses', 'input', 'output', 'cache write 5 min', 'cache write 1 h', 'cache read']\r\nmodels = sorted(tot)\r\nprint(f\"All responses were served by {', '.join(models)}. Token counts:\\\\n\")\r\nprint('| source | ' + ' | '.join(heads) + ' | cost (USD) |')\r\nprint('|' + '-' * 34 + '|' + '------:|' * (len(cols) + 1))\r\ngrand = 0.0\r\nfor (who, model), r in sorted(per_file.items()):\r\n    label = who if len(models) == 1 else f'{who} ({model})'\r\n    print(f'| {label} | ' + ' | '.join(f'{r[c]:,}' for c in cols) + f' | {cost(model, r):.2f} |')\r\nfor model, r in sorted(tot.items()):\r\n    c = cost(model, r)\r\n    grand += c\r\n    label = 'total' if len(models) == 1 else f'total {model}'\r\n    print(f'| **{label}** | ' + ' | '.join(f'**{r[c2]:,}**' for c2 in cols) + f' | **{c:.2f}** |')\r\nprint(f'\\\\nTotal cost at API prices: **USD {grand:.2f}** '\r\n      f'({len(files)} transcripts, {len(seen)} API responses).')\r\n'''\r\ns=s.replace(old,new)\r\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\r\nEOF\r\npython3 submission/scripts/token_usage.py\r\nAll responses were served by claude-opus-5-5. Token counts:\r\n\r\n| source | responses | input | output | cache write 5 min | cache write 1 h | cache read | cost (USD) |\r\n|----------------------------------|------:|------:|------:|------:|------:|------:|------:|\r\n| main session | 200 | 381 | 259,513 | 0 | 898,353 | 59,787,741 | 24.34 |\r\n| subagent: 800MHz candidate: Dadda tree | 52 | 104 | 97,720 | 210,726 | 0 | 7,768,398 | 4.56 |\r\n| subagent: 800MHz candidate: retimed behavioral | 44 | 88 | 44,572 | 140,455 | 0 | 5,024,137 | 2.60 |\r\n| subagent: Write spec-derived checkers | 25 | 50 | 58,794 | 145,795 | 0 | 2,756,467 | 2.46 |\r\n| **total** | **321** | **623** | **460,599** | **496,976** | **898,353** | **75,336,743** | **33.95** |\r\n\r\nTotal cost at API prices: **USD 33.95** (4 transcripts, 321 API responses).\r\n"]
[16413.045, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat >> notes/WORKLOG.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n## Report revision after sign-off (07:00\u201307:15 UTC)\r\n\r\n**Sign-off scorecards** (`git fetch origin check-results`, `results/check_{400-60ed005585,800-b6917e9eb1}/scorecard.md`).\r\n- *Correction:* the user reports that the service was online throughout the session. It did not trigger because the session environment had not been set up for it. The report's earlier wording (\"probably offline\") was wrong and has been corrected.\r\n- *Checked:* both commits at 06:37 / 06:48 UTC, after the environment fix.\r\n- *GPDK045 results:*\r\n\r\n  | | 400 MHz | 800 MHz |\r\n  |---|---|---|\r\n  | WNS (target) | 156 ps (125) | 148 ps (62) |\r\n  | Area | 2752.1 \u00b5m\u00b2 | 5674.5 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n  | Vectorless power | 224.6 \u00b5W | 1121.9 \u00b5W |\r\n  | SDF simulation | pass, 1204/1204 products, 0 timing-check messages | pass, 1249/1249 products |\r\n\r\n  Informational check: the 400 MHz netlist at 1.25 ns fails, with 0 products, 4058 timing-check messages, and F1 F4 F5 F6 F8 F9 STALL violated. This matches our own `make timing_fail RUN=800` (same netlist, same period, no product returned).\r\n- *Comparison with the open-source results:*\r\n  - functional results agree;\r\n  - GPDK045 area is 15\u201319 % larger;\r\n  - GPDK045 vectorless power is 2.4\u20132.9\u00d7 lower (different library, voltage and default activity);\r\n  - the 800 MHz design draws 4.2\u00d7 the power of the 400 MHz design in our flow and 5.0\u00d7 in GPDK045;\r\n  - 400 MHz slack is nearly equal in both flows; at 800 MHz GPDK045 has 2\u00d7 the margin (corner not stated; commercial tools spend slack on area recovery).\r\n\r\n**Report rewritten for concision.** The user asked for a results summary first, then design decisions, at about half the length. Main-text prose went from 5,650 to 2,728 words (3,805 with tables), and all ten SPEC Section 9 items are kept. Section order:\r\n1. summary;\r\n2. design decisions (control, arithmetic, 400 MHz, 800 MHz with change table and candidates);\r\n3. verification;\r\n4. area/power;\r\n5. optimisation;\r\n6. tool flow and departures;\r\n7. GPDK045 comparison;\r\n8. metrics;\r\n9. references, with the appendix after them.\r\n\r\nRTL untouched.\r\n\r\n**Build fixes.**\r\n- The first rebuild failed silently. LaTeX could not render \"\u2248\" (U+2248), and `| tail -1` hid the error, so the old PDF stayed in place. \"\u2248\" and \"\u2026\" are now declared in the header.\r\n- `token_usage.py` now labels subagents by their task description from `*.meta.json` and states the model once.\r\nEOF\r\nbash submission/scripts/build_report.sh 2>&1 | tail -2 && cp build/report/tokens.md submission/syn_reports/token_usage.md && pdftotext -l 1 submission/pdf_report/report.pdf - | sed -n 1,4p && grep \"Total cost\" submission/syn_reports/token_usage.md && git add -A submission notes && git commit -q -m \"Report revision: GPDK045 sign-off comparison, concise results-first structure, token usage update\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126GMUJKG14LrQMZ4a6y2it\" && git push -q origin claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i 2>&1 | tail -1; git status --short | wc -l; git log --oneline | head -1\r\nreport written: submission/pdf_report/report.pdf (Pages:           46)\r\nmkMultBuff: a pipelined signed 16 \u00d7 16 multiplier with a 64-entry\r\nfill/drain buffer at 400 MHz and 800 MHz\r\nDesign report, open-source flow on Nangate45 (FreePDK45), slow corner\r\nClaude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), AI agent in Claude Code\r\nTotal cost at API prices: **USD 34.11** (4 transcripts, 322 API responses).\r\n0\r\n87b9178 Report revision: GPDK045 sign-off comparison, concise results-first structure, token usage update\r\n"]
[16425.356, "o", "\u001b[2m# --- end of turn ---\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19437.088, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m git fetch -q origin main && git log --oneline -3 origin/main && git merge --no-edit origin/main 2>&1 | tail -3 && sed -n '/^## 5/,/^## 6/p' SPEC.md && sed -n '/^## 4/,/^## 5/p' CLAUDE.md\r\ne1b93d2 Judge area and power on the sign-off results; allow candidate checks\r\n045bcfe Specification, starter files and agent setup\r\n CLAUDE.md | 2 +-\r\n SPEC.md   | 2 +-\r\n 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\r\n## 5. Implementation targets\r\n\r\n| Parameter | 400 MHz implementation | 800 MHz implementation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Source directory | `submission/rtl_400/` | `submission/rtl_800/` |\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns | 1.25 ns |\r\n| Pipeline stages | 2 minimum | Implementation-defined |\r\n| Worst slack, required | \u2265 0 ps | \u2265 0 ps |\r\n| Worst slack, target | \u2265 125 ps (5 % of period) | \u2265 62 ps (5 % of period) |\r\n| Cell area | < 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2 | < 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n| Power | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity |\r\n\r\nEach implementation shall have `mkMultBuff` as its top module and shall compile from the complete set of `.sv` files in its source directory, read in any order. `` `include`` directives shall not be used. The targets apply to the results of the open-source flow in Section 7, and the slack target shall also be met in the sign-off results of Section 8.3. The slack target leaves margin for physical implementation, and slack beyond it confers no further benefit. Among implementations that meet these targets, lower area and lower power are preferred, judged on the sign-off results, since these are comparable with designs from the course's standard flow.\r\n\r\n## 6. Technology and constraints\r\n## 4. Sign-off service\r\n\r\nPushing a branch named `check/<label>` submits the RTL in `submission/rtl_400/` and `submission/rtl_800/` to the sign-off service described in `SPEC.md` Section 8.3. The scorecard appears on branch `check-results`, under `results/`, usually between five and twenty minutes later while the service is online, and can be read with `git fetch origin check-results`. Work should continue in the meantime rather than wait for the result. Candidate implementations may be submitted as well as completed ones. A check takes about three minutes once it starts, and checks run one at a time.\r\n\r\n## 5. Environment\r\n"]
[19501.499, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat > build/exp/ranks.tcl <<'EOF'\r\n# per register group: flop count and worst setup slack at D\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\narray set w {}; array set n {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n  if {![string match DFF* [get_property $inst ref_name]]} continue\r\n  set in [get_full_name $inst]\r\n  set q [get_full_name [get_nets -of_objects [get_pins $in/Q]]]\r\n  regsub {\\s*\\[[0-9]+\\]\\s*$} $q \"\" g\r\n  set s [get_property [get_pins $in/D] slack_max]\r\n  if {![info exists w($g)] || $s < $w($g)} { set w($g) $s }\r\n  if {[info exists n($g)]} { incr n($g) } else { set n($g) 1 }\r\n}\r\nforeach g [lsort [array names w]] { puts [format \"%-36s %4d %8.3f\" $g $n($g) $w($g)] }\r\nEOF\r\ndocker run --rm -v $PWD:$PWD -w $PWD -e LIB=tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib -e NETLIST=submission/outputs/mkMultBuff_800_map.v -e PERIOD=1.25 --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a -no_init -no_splash -exit build/exp/ranks.tcl 2>&1 | tail -45\r\nCannot connect to the Docker daemon at unix:///var/run/docker.sock. Is the docker daemon running?\r\n"]
