[19609.018, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cp build/exp/ranks.tcl submission/scripts/ranks.tcl && sed -i '1s/.*/# ranks.tcl -- flop count and worst setup slack at D per register group (Q-net name). env: LIB NETLIST PERIOD/' submission/scripts/ranks.tcl && grep -n '^cell DFF' submission/syn_reports/800/sta.rpt | head -2; which bc; time bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 submission/rtl_800 build/cand/base800 2>&1 | head -8\r\n175:cell DFF_X1           577   2609.194 um^2\r\n/usr/bin/bc\r\n== build/cand/base800 RUN=800\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.075 whs=0.041\r\narea=4755.016 seq=2609.194 comb=2145.8 flops=577 vectorless_uW=2727.6\r\nactivity_uW: run:=3073.10 fill:=5209.50 drain:=2535.60 \r\nper register group (flops, worst slack):\r\nVALID_memVal                            1    0.465\r\nacc_q                                   6    0.152\r\nrdy_mult_on                             1    0.203\r\n\r\nreal\t0m32.161s\r\nuser\t0m4.144s\r\nsys\t0m0.222s\r\n"]
[19664.977, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n '/^## 3/,/^## 7/p' SPEC.md | head -300; ls build/ build/cand_dadda submission/rtl_800 submission/scripts\r\n## 3. Interface\r\n\r\nThe port list is fixed and defined in `starter/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv`, with N = 32.\r\n\r\n| Port | Direction | Width | Description |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `clk` | input | 1 | Clock |\r\n| `RST_N` | input | 1 | Synchronous reset, active low |\r\n| `EN_mult` | input | 1 | The producer presents a valid operand pair |\r\n| `mult_input0`, `mult_input1` | input | 16 | Operands, two's complement |\r\n| `RDY_mult` | output | 1 | The block can accept an operand pair |\r\n| `EN_blockRead` | input | 1 | The consumer requests a product |\r\n| `RDY_blockRead` | output | 1 | The block can accept a read |\r\n| `VALID_memVal` | output | 1 | `memVal_data` carries a product |\r\n| `memVal_data` | output | N | Product returned to the consumer |\r\n| `EN_writeMem` | output | 1 | Memory write enable |\r\n| `writeMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory write address |\r\n| `writeMem_val` | output | N | Memory write data |\r\n| `EN_readMem` | output | 1 | Memory read enable |\r\n| `readMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory read address |\r\n| `readMem_val` | input | N | Memory read data |\r\n\r\nThe memory, `starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv`, is a 64 \u00d7 N two-port array instantiated in the testbench. It is not part of `mkMultBuff` and is excluded from synthesis. A write stores `writeMem_val` at a rising edge at which `EN_writeMem` = 1. A read registers the addressed word at a rising edge at which `EN_readMem` = 1, so `readMem_val` is valid in the following cycle.\r\n\r\n## 4. Functional requirements\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Datapath\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F1 | Each accepted operand pair shall produce exactly one memory write, whose data is the 32-bit two's-complement product of `mult_input0` and `mult_input1`. |\r\n| F2 | Products shall be written in acceptance order to consecutive addresses, starting at address 0 in each fill phase. |\r\n| F3 | The multiplier shall be fully pipelined and sustain a throughput of one operand pair per cycle. |\r\n| F4 | The latency is implementation-defined. `EN_writeMem` shall be asserted only in cycles in which `writeMem_addr` and `writeMem_val` carry a valid address and product. |\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Fill\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F5 | `RDY_mult` shall be 1 if and only if no drain phase is in progress and fewer than 64 operand pairs have been accepted in the current fill phase. Operand pairs in flight therefore count against the capacity of the memory. `EN_mult` shall have no effect while `RDY_mult` is 0. |\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Transition to drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F6 | `RDY_blockRead` shall be asserted in the cycle following the write to address 63 and shall remain asserted until the 64th read is accepted. |\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F7 | In each cycle in which a read is accepted, `EN_readMem` shall be 1 and `readMem_addr` shall hold the next sequential address, starting at 0. |\r\n| F8 | `VALID_memVal` shall be 1 in, and only in, the cycle following each accepted read. In that cycle `memVal_data` shall equal `readMem_val`, which shall not be registered again inside `mkMultBuff`. |\r\n| F9 | `EN_blockRead` shall have no effect while `RDY_blockRead` is 0. |\r\n| F10 | In the cycle following the accepted read of address 63, `RDY_blockRead` shall be 0 and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. |\r\n\r\n### 4.5 Flow control and invariants\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F11 | The block shall operate correctly for any sequence of `EN_mult` and `EN_blockRead`. Deasserting either signal stalls the corresponding transfer without loss or duplication of data. |\r\n| F12 | `RDY_mult` and `RDY_blockRead` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n| F13 | `EN_writeMem` and `EN_readMem` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n\r\n### 4.6 Reset\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F14 | Every register shall have a synchronous, active-low reset driven by `RST_N`. |\r\n| F15 | In the cycle following a rising edge at which `RST_N` = 0, no product shall be in flight or stored and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. `EN_writeMem`, `writeMem_addr`, `RDY_blockRead`, `EN_readMem` and `VALID_memVal` shall be 0. |\r\n\r\nFigures 1 to 4 illustrate the phases of operation for an implementation with a latency of two cycles.\r\n\r\n![Figure 1. Fill phase](docs/fig/fill.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 2. Memory full and transition to drain](docs/fig/full.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 3. Drain phase](docs/fig/drain.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 4. End of drain phase](docs/fig/drain_end.svg)\r\n\r\n## 5. Implementation targets\r\n\r\n| Parameter | 400 MHz implementation | 800 MHz implementation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Source directory | `submission/rtl_400/` | `submission/rtl_800/` |\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns | 1.25 ns |\r\n| Pipeline stages | 2 minimum | Implementation-defined |\r\n| Worst slack, required | \u2265 0 ps | \u2265 0 ps |\r\n| Worst slack, target | \u2265 125 ps (5 % of period) | \u2265 62 ps (5 % of period) |\r\n| Cell area | < 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2 | < 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n| Power | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity |\r\n\r\nEach implementation shall have `mkMultBuff` as its top module and shall compile from the complete set of `.sv` files in its source directory, read in any order. `` `include`` directives shall not be used. The targets apply to the results of the open-source flow in Section 7, and the slack target shall also be met in the sign-off results of Section 8.3. The slack target leaves margin for physical implementation, and slack beyond it confers no further benefit. Among implementations that meet these targets, lower area and lower power are preferred, judged on the sign-off results, since these are comparable with designs from the course's standard flow.\r\n\r\n## 6. Technology and constraints\r\n\r\nThe open-source flow targets the Nangate45 Open Cell Library, which is built on the FreePDK45 process, at its slowest available corner. The install script written under Section 7 shall obtain the library from a public source, which the report shall identify together with the corner used. The library is not stored in this repository.\r\n\r\nFor comparison with designs built on the GPDK045 library, the sign-off service of Section 8.3 synthesizes the submitted RTL with GPDK045 and simulates the resulting netlists. Its results are reported alongside those of the open-source flow, not in place of them.\r\n\r\n| Constraint | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns or 1.25 ns |\r\n| Input delay, all inputs except `clk` | 0 ns |\r\n| Output delay, all outputs | 0 ns |\r\n| Input drive | Output of the smallest D flip-flop in the library |\r\n| Input transition | One eighth of the clock period |\r\n| Output load | Four times the capacitance of one input of the library's X4 two-input NAND (`NAND2_X4` in Nangate45) |\r\n\r\nSynthesis may target a shorter internal clock period and may retime registers. All reported figures are evaluated at the target period.\r\n\r\n## 7. Tool flow\r\nbuild/:\r\n400\r\n800\r\ncand\r\ncand_dadda\r\ncand_retime\r\nexp\r\nfail_400\r\nfail_800\r\nh.tcl\r\nmutants_400\r\nmutants_800\r\nnoiso400\r\noutputs_cp2_backup\r\nr400new\r\nreport\r\n\r\nbuild/cand_dadda:\r\nep.sh\r\nep.tcl\r\ngen.py\r\ngen2.py\r\nio.tcl\r\npath1.sh\r\npath1.tcl\r\ntop.sv.in\r\ntop2.sv.in\r\ntop3.sv.in\r\ntop4.sv.in\r\nv1\r\nv2\r\nv3\r\nv4\r\nv5\r\nv5_abc800\r\nv5_abc900\r\nv6\r\nv6_abc1050\r\nv6_abc800\r\nv7\r\nv8\r\n\r\nsubmission/rtl_800:\r\nmkMultBuff.sv\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\n\r\nsubmission/scripts:\r\nabc_speed.script\r\nbuild_report.sh\r\nconstraints.tcl\r\neval_candidate.sh\r\nf14_check.sh\r\nf14_check.tcl\r\nfresh_clone_rerun.sh\r\ninstall.sh\r\nlib_dont_use.py\r\nmutate.sh\r\npower.sh\r\npower.tcl\r\npower_summary.py\r\nranks.tcl\r\nresize.tcl\r\nsdf_typmax.py\r\nsta.tcl\r\nsynth.tcl\r\ntoken_usage.py\r\nwaves\r\n"]
[19665.259, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n '/^## 3/,/^## 7/p' SPEC.md | head -250; wc -l submission/rtl_800/*.sv; ls build/ | head\r\n## 3. Interface\r\n\r\nThe port list is fixed and defined in `starter/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv`, with N = 32.\r\n\r\n| Port | Direction | Width | Description |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `clk` | input | 1 | Clock |\r\n| `RST_N` | input | 1 | Synchronous reset, active low |\r\n| `EN_mult` | input | 1 | The producer presents a valid operand pair |\r\n| `mult_input0`, `mult_input1` | input | 16 | Operands, two's complement |\r\n| `RDY_mult` | output | 1 | The block can accept an operand pair |\r\n| `EN_blockRead` | input | 1 | The consumer requests a product |\r\n| `RDY_blockRead` | output | 1 | The block can accept a read |\r\n| `VALID_memVal` | output | 1 | `memVal_data` carries a product |\r\n| `memVal_data` | output | N | Product returned to the consumer |\r\n| `EN_writeMem` | output | 1 | Memory write enable |\r\n| `writeMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory write address |\r\n| `writeMem_val` | output | N | Memory write data |\r\n| `EN_readMem` | output | 1 | Memory read enable |\r\n| `readMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory read address |\r\n| `readMem_val` | input | N | Memory read data |\r\n\r\nThe memory, `starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv`, is a 64 \u00d7 N two-port array instantiated in the testbench. It is not part of `mkMultBuff` and is excluded from synthesis. A write stores `writeMem_val` at a rising edge at which `EN_writeMem` = 1. A read registers the addressed word at a rising edge at which `EN_readMem` = 1, so `readMem_val` is valid in the following cycle.\r\n\r\n## 4. Functional requirements\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Datapath\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F1 | Each accepted operand pair shall produce exactly one memory write, whose data is the 32-bit two's-complement product of `mult_input0` and `mult_input1`. |\r\n| F2 | Products shall be written in acceptance order to consecutive addresses, starting at address 0 in each fill phase. |\r\n| F3 | The multiplier shall be fully pipelined and sustain a throughput of one operand pair per cycle. |\r\n| F4 | The latency is implementation-defined. `EN_writeMem` shall be asserted only in cycles in which `writeMem_addr` and `writeMem_val` carry a valid address and product. |\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Fill\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F5 | `RDY_mult` shall be 1 if and only if no drain phase is in progress and fewer than 64 operand pairs have been accepted in the current fill phase. Operand pairs in flight therefore count against the capacity of the memory. `EN_mult` shall have no effect while `RDY_mult` is 0. |\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Transition to drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F6 | `RDY_blockRead` shall be asserted in the cycle following the write to address 63 and shall remain asserted until the 64th read is accepted. |\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F7 | In each cycle in which a read is accepted, `EN_readMem` shall be 1 and `readMem_addr` shall hold the next sequential address, starting at 0. |\r\n| F8 | `VALID_memVal` shall be 1 in, and only in, the cycle following each accepted read. In that cycle `memVal_data` shall equal `readMem_val`, which shall not be registered again inside `mkMultBuff`. |\r\n| F9 | `EN_blockRead` shall have no effect while `RDY_blockRead` is 0. |\r\n| F10 | In the cycle following the accepted read of address 63, `RDY_blockRead` shall be 0 and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. |\r\n\r\n### 4.5 Flow control and invariants\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F11 | The block shall operate correctly for any sequence of `EN_mult` and `EN_blockRead`. Deasserting either signal stalls the corresponding transfer without loss or duplication of data. |\r\n| F12 | `RDY_mult` and `RDY_blockRead` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n| F13 | `EN_writeMem` and `EN_readMem` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n\r\n### 4.6 Reset\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F14 | Every register shall have a synchronous, active-low reset driven by `RST_N`. |\r\n| F15 | In the cycle following a rising edge at which `RST_N` = 0, no product shall be in flight or stored and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. `EN_writeMem`, `writeMem_addr`, `RDY_blockRead`, `EN_readMem` and `VALID_memVal` shall be 0. |\r\n\r\nFigures 1 to 4 illustrate the phases of operation for an implementation with a latency of two cycles.\r\n\r\n![Figure 1. Fill phase](docs/fig/fill.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 2. Memory full and transition to drain](docs/fig/full.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 3. Drain phase](docs/fig/drain.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 4. End of drain phase](docs/fig/drain_end.svg)\r\n\r\n## 5. Implementation targets\r\n\r\n| Parameter | 400 MHz implementation | 800 MHz implementation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Source directory | `submission/rtl_400/` | `submission/rtl_800/` |\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns | 1.25 ns |\r\n| Pipeline stages | 2 minimum | Implementation-defined |\r\n| Worst slack, required | \u2265 0 ps | \u2265 0 ps |\r\n| Worst slack, target | \u2265 125 ps (5 % of period) | \u2265 62 ps (5 % of period) |\r\n| Cell area | < 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2 | < 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n| Power | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity |\r\n\r\nEach implementation shall have `mkMultBuff` as its top module and shall compile from the complete set of `.sv` files in its source directory, read in any order. `` `include`` directives shall not be used. The targets apply to the results of the open-source flow in Section 7, and the slack target shall also be met in the sign-off results of Section 8.3. The slack target leaves margin for physical implementation, and slack beyond it confers no further benefit. Among implementations that meet these targets, lower area and lower power are preferred, judged on the sign-off results, since these are comparable with designs from the course's standard flow.\r\n\r\n## 6. Technology and constraints\r\n\r\nThe open-source flow targets the Nangate45 Open Cell Library, which is built on the FreePDK45 process, at its slowest available corner. The install script written under Section 7 shall obtain the library from a public source, which the report shall identify together with the corner used. The library is not stored in this repository.\r\n\r\nFor comparison with designs built on the GPDK045 library, the sign-off service of Section 8.3 synthesizes the submitted RTL with GPDK045 and simulates the resulting netlists. Its results are reported alongside those of the open-source flow, not in place of them.\r\n\r\n| Constraint | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns or 1.25 ns |\r\n| Input delay, all inputs except `clk` | 0 ns |\r\n| Output delay, all outputs | 0 ns |\r\n| Input drive | Output of the smallest D flip-flop in the library |\r\n| Input transition | One eighth of the clock period |\r\n| Output load | Four times the capacitance of one input of the library's X4 two-input NAND (`NAND2_X4` in Nangate45) |\r\n\r\nSynthesis may target a shorter internal clock period and may retime registers. All reported figures are evaluated at the target period.\r\n\r\n## 7. Tool flow\r\n  111 submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv\r\n  264 submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv\r\n  375 total\r\n400\r\n800\r\ncand\r\ncand_dadda\r\ncand_retime\r\nexp\r\nfail_400\r\nfail_800\r\nh.tcl\r\nmutants_400\r\n"]
[19666.798, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv; cat submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv | head -80\r\n// mult_pipe.sv -- pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier: radix-4 (modified) Booth\r\n// partial products, carry-save (3:2) reduction 9->6->4->3->2 rows and a final\r\n// carry-propagate adder. Every pipeline cut is optional (parameters).\r\n//   PRE_ENC  : Booth-recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n//   ENC_REG  : (PRE_ENC = 0 only) extra rank after the Booth recoding\r\n//   SEL_REG  : register the selected partial products (8 x 17 bits + 8 \"+1\" bits)\r\n//   CSA_REG  : bit k set -> register after carry-save level k+1 (k = 0..3)\r\n//   GP4      : the level-4 register holds generate/propagate (c&s, c^s) of the\r\n//              two final rows instead of the rows themselves (same width)\r\n//   CPA_CSEL : two-stage carry-select final adder with CSW-bit blocks and\r\n//              Kogge-Stone prefixes inside the blocks and across the blocks\r\n//   CPA_SPLIT: (alternative) low 16 bits in one stage, high 16 bits in the next\r\n// Register ranks (= latency from 'en' to 'p'): 1 (operand) + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG)\r\n//   + SEL_REG + popcount(CSA_REG) + (CPA_CSEL | CPA_SPLIT) + 1 (product)\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset. When 'en' is 0 the operand\r\n// register loads zeros (operand isolation), so an idle multiplier does not toggle.\r\n// Written for this project; the Booth recoding, the sign-extension constant and\r\n// the prefix adders follow textbook schemes (see the report's references).\r\nmodule mult_pipe #(\r\n    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n    parameter bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1000,\r\n    parameter bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter int       CSW       = 8,\r\n    parameter bit       GP4       = 1'b0\r\n) (\r\n    input  logic               clk,\r\n    input  logic               RST_N,\r\n    input  logic               en,     // accept: load operands, else load zeros\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] a,      // multiplicand (unregistered input)\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] b,      // multiplier   (unregistered input)\r\n    output logic signed [31:0] p       // product, registered\r\n);\r\n    // Booth radix-4 recoding of y: digit_i = -2 y[2i+1] + y[2i] + y[2i-1]\r\n    function automatic logic [23:0] booth_enc(input logic [15:0] y);\r\n        logic [16:0] yx;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one, two, neg;\r\n        yx = {y, 1'b0};                       // yx[k+1] = y[k], yx[0] = y[-1] = 0\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin\r\n            one[i] = yx[2*i+1] ^ yx[2*i];\r\n            two[i] = (yx[2*i+2] & ~yx[2*i+1] & ~yx[2*i]) | (~yx[2*i+2] & yx[2*i+1] & yx[2*i]);\r\n            neg[i] = yx[2*i+2];\r\n        end\r\n        booth_enc = {neg, two, one};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ---- stage 0: operand register (operand isolation: zeros when idle)\r\n    logic [7:0]  one_e, two_e, neg_e;\r\n    logic [15:0] a_e;\r\n    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\r\n        // recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_q, two_q, neg_q;\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_q, two_q, neg_q};\r\n    end else begin : g_post\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_d, two_d, neg_d;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {neg_d, two_d, one_d} = booth_enc(b_q);\r\n        if (ENC_REG) begin : g_enc\r\n            logic [7:0]  one_r, two_r, neg_r;\r\n            logic [15:0] a_r;\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n                if (!RST_N) begin a_r <= '0; one_r <= '0; two_r <= '0; neg_r <= '0; end\r\n                else begin a_r <= a_q; one_r <= one_d; two_r <= two_d; neg_r <= neg_d; end\r\n            end\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_r, one_r, two_r, neg_r};\r\n        end else begin : g_noenc\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_d, two_d, neg_d};\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    genvar i;\r\n\r\n    localparam int NB = 32 / CSW;     // carry-select blocks\r\n\r\n    // Kogge-Stone prefix over the NB block carries (generate = carry-out with\r\n    // carry-in 0, propagate = carry-out with carry-in 1)\r\n    function automatic logic [NB-1:0] bprefix(input logic [NB-1:0] g, input logic [NB-1:0] p);\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] G, P;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        for (int d = 1; d < NB; d = 2 * d)\r\n            for (int j = NB - 1; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]);\r\n                P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n            end\r\n        bprefix = G;\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // Kogge-Stone prefix over a CSW-bit block: G[j] / P[j] = group generate /\r\n    // propagate of bits j..0 of the block\r\n    function automatic logic [2*CSW-1:0] prefix(input logic [CSW-1:0] g, input logic [CSW-1:0] p);\r\n        logic [CSW-1:0] G, P;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        for (int d = 1; d < CSW; d = 2 * d)\r\n            for (int j = CSW - 1; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]);\r\n                P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n            end\r\n        prefix = {G, P};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // Partial-product rows. Sign extension is replaced by inverting each row's\r\n    // sign bit and adding the constant K = -sum(2^(16+2i)) (mod 2^32); the\r\n    // \"+1\" of each negative row is placed in the free bit of the next row.\r\n    localparam logic [31:0] K = 32'hAAAB_0000;  // -(2^16+2^18+...+2^30) mod 2^32\r\n    wire [16:0] a17 = {a_e[15], a_e};\r\n    wire [16:0] a2  = {a_e, 1'b0};\r\n    logic [31:0] r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8;\r\n    logic [16:0] pp [0:7];\r\n    logic [31:0] rw [0:7];\r\n    generate for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_pp\r\n        assign pp[i] = (({17{one_e[i]}} & a17) | ({17{two_e[i]}} & a2)) ^ {17{neg_e[i]}};\r\n        if (i == 0) begin : g_r0\r\n            assign rw[i] = {15'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0]};\r\n        end else begin : g_ri\r\n            // bits [2i+16:2i] hold the row, bit 2i-2 holds the +1 of row i-1\r\n            assign rw[i] = {13'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0], 1'b0, neg_e[i-1]} << (2*i-2);\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7} = {rw[0], rw[1], rw[2], rw[3], rw[4], rw[5], rw[6], rw[7]};\r\n    assign r8 = K | ({31'd0, neg_e[7]} << 14);\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // carry-save levels (3:2 compressors on whole rows); each optionally registered\r\n    function automatic logic [63:0] csa(input logic [31:0] x, y, z);\r\n        csa = {((x & y) | (x & z) | (y & z)) << 1, x ^ y ^ z};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // level 1: 9 -> 6, level 2: 6 -> 4, level 3: 4 -> 3, level 4: 3 -> 2\r\n    logic [6*32-1:0] l1, l1q;\r\n    logic [4*32-1:0] l2, l2q;\r\n    logic [3*32-1:0] l3, l3q;\r\n    logic [2*32-1:0] l4, l4q;\r\n    // optional register after partial-product selection (8 rows of 17 bits + the\r\n    // row +1 bits; the constant part of row 8 is re-created after the register)\r\n    logic [31:0] q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8;\r\n    generate if (SEL_REG) begin : g_sel\r\n        logic [16:0] ppq [0:7];\r\n        logic [7:0]  negq;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_q\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) ppq[i] <= RST_N ? pp[i] : 17'd0;\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) negq <= RST_N ? neg_e : 8'd0;\r\n        assign q0 = {15'd0, ~ppq[0][16], ppq[0][15:0]};\r\n        assign q1 = {13'd0, ~ppq[1][16], ppq[1][15:0], 1'b0, negq[0]} << 0;\r\n        assign q2 = {13'd0, ~ppq[2][16], ppq[2][15:0], 1'b0, negq[1]} << 2;\r\n        assign q3 = {13'd0, ~ppq[3][16], ppq[3][15:0], 1'b0, negq[2]} << 4;\r\n        assign q4 = {13'd0, ~ppq[4][16], ppq[4][15:0], 1'b0, negq[3]} << 6;\r\n        assign q5 = {13'd0, ~ppq[5][16], ppq[5][15:0], 1'b0, negq[4]} << 8;\r\n        assign q6 = {13'd0, ~ppq[6][16], ppq[6][15:0], 1'b0, negq[5]} << 10;\r\n        assign q7 = {13'd0, ~ppq[7][16], ppq[7][15:0], 1'b0, negq[6]} << 12;\r\n        assign q8 = K | ({31'd0, negq[7]} << 14);\r\n    end else begin : g_nosel\r\n        assign {q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8} = {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8};\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign l1 = {csa(q6, q7, q8), csa(q3, q4, q5), csa(q0, q1, q2)};\r\n    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    // level 4 output: the two final rows {c, s}, or (GP4) their bitwise\r\n    // generate / propagate {c & s, c ^ s}, so the adder's first gate level\r\n    // moves in front of the level-4 register\r\n    logic [63:0] l4cs;\r\n    assign l4cs = csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n    assign l4 = GP4 ? {l4cs[63:32] & l4cs[31:0], l4cs[63:32] ^ l4cs[31:0]} : l4cs;\r\n\r\n    generate\r\n        if (CSA_REG[0]) begin : g_r1\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l1q <= RST_N ? l1 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n1\r\n            assign l1q = l1;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[1]) begin : g_r2\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l2q <= RST_N ? l2 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n2\r\n            assign l2q = l2;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[2]) begin : g_r3\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l3q <= RST_N ? l3 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n3\r\n            assign l3q = l3;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[3]) begin : g_r4\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l4q <= RST_N ? l4 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n4\r\n            assign l4q = l4;\r\n        end\r\n    endgenerate\r\n    wire [31:0] sx = l4q[31:0], sy = l4q[63:32];\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // final carry-propagate adder, registered product\r\n    generate if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\r\n        // two-stage carry-select adder with CSW-bit blocks. Stage A: per block,\r\n        // bit generate/propagate and an in-block Kogge-Stone prefix give the\r\n        // block sums for carry-in 0 and carry-in 1 and the two block carry-outs.\r\n        // Stage B: the block carries are resolved and each block sum selected.\r\n        logic [31:0]   s0, s1, s0q, s1q;\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] co0, co1, co0q, co1q, cin;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_blk\r\n            logic [CSW-1:0] gg, pp_, G, P;\r\n            if (GP4) begin : g_gp\r\n                assign gg  = sy[CSW*i +: CSW];        // generate (registered)\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW];        // propagate (registered)\r\n            end else begin : g_cs\r\n                assign gg  = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] & sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            end\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(gg, pp_);\r\n            assign s0[CSW*i +: CSW] = pp_ ^ {G[CSW-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n            assign s1[CSW*i +: CSW] = pp_ ^ {G[CSW-2:0] | P[CSW-2:0], 1'b1};\r\n            assign co0[i] = G[CSW-1];\r\n            assign co1[i] = G[CSW-1] | P[CSW-1];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                s0q <= '0; s1q <= '0; co0q <= '0; co1q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                s0q <= s0; s1q <= s1; co0q <= co0; co1q <= co1;\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        // carry into block i = group generate of blocks i-1..0\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] bg;\r\n        assign bg  = bprefix(co0q, co1q);\r\n        assign cin = {bg[NB-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n        logic [31:0] psel;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_sel\r\n            assign psel[CSW*i +: CSW] = cin[i] ? s1q[CSW*i +: CSW] : s0q[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? psel : 32'd0;\r\n    end else if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n        logic [16:0] lo;\r\n        logic [15:0] lo_q, xh_q, yh_q;\r\n        logic        c_q;\r\n        assign lo = {1'b0, sx[15:0]} + {1'b0, sy[15:0]};\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                lo_q <= '0; c_q <= 1'b0; xh_q <= '0; yh_q <= '0; p <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                lo_q <= lo[15:0]; c_q <= lo[16];\r\n                xh_q <= sx[31:16]; yh_q <= sy[31:16];\r\n                p    <= {xh_q + yh_q + {15'd0, c_q}, lo_q};\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n    end else begin : g_full\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) p <= '0;\r\n            else        p <= sx + sy;\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\nendmodule : mult_pipe\r\n// mkMultBuff.sv -- 800 MHz implementation (1.25 ns clock), Nangate45 slow corner.\r\n//\r\n// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer (SPEC.md).\r\n// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, carry-select adder),\r\n// with\r\n// seven register ranks (LAT = 7):\r\n//   rank 1: operand register; mult_input1 is Booth-recoded before it\r\n//   rank 2: selected partial products (8 rows of 17 bits + 8 \"+1\" bits)\r\n//   rank 3: carry-save level 1 (9 -> 6 rows)\r\n//   rank 4: carry-save levels 2 and 3 (6 -> 4 -> 3 rows)\r\n//   rank 5: carry-save level 4 (3 -> 2 rows), stored as generate/propagate\r\n//   rank 6: carry-select adder stage A (4-bit blocks: sums for carry-in 0/1,\r\n//           block carry-outs)\r\n//   rank 7: product, after the block-carry prefix and the sum selection;\r\n//           drives writeMem_val directly\r\n// A LAT-bit valid shift register runs alongside the datapath and drives\r\n// EN_writeMem (F4).\r\n//\r\n// Control: the registered ready flags rdy_mult_q / rdy_rd_q are the fill /\r\n// drain state machine (FILL = {1,0}, WAIT = {0,0}, DRAIN = {0,1}); acc_q counts\r\n// pairs accepted in the fill phase, so pairs in flight count against the\r\n// capacity (F5); wp_q / rp_q are the write and read pointers. Changes from the\r\n// 400 MHz control for timing at 1.25 ns: separate write and read pointers, and\r\n// port-only copies of RDY_mult, RDY_blockRead, writeMem_addr, readMem_addr and\r\n// EN_writeMem, so the output load does not slow the internal handshake logic.\r\n// All outputs come from registers except EN_readMem (= EN_blockRead &\r\n// RDY_blockRead, F7) and memVal_data (= readMem_val, F8).\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (F14, F15).\r\nmodule mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (\r\n    input  logic         clk,\r\n    input  logic         RST_N,\r\n    input  logic         EN_mult,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input0,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input1,\r\n    output logic         RDY_mult,\r\n    input  logic         EN_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         RDY_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         VALID_memVal,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] memVal_data,\r\n    output logic         EN_writeMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   writeMem_addr,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] writeMem_val,\r\n    output logic         EN_readMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   readMem_addr,\r\n    input  logic [N-1:0] readMem_val\r\n);\r\n    // multiplier pipeline configuration (see mult_pipe.sv)\r\n    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1101;\r\n    localparam bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + SEL_REG + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n                                     + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3] + (CPA_SPLIT | CPA_CSEL) + 1;\r\n\r\n    logic       rdy_mult_q, rdy_rd_q, vld_q;\r\n    // copies of the two ready flags that drive only the output ports, so the\r\n    // port load does not slow the internal handshake logic (stored inverted,\r\n    // see below)\r\n    logic rdy_mult_on, rdy_rd_on;\r\n    // likewise port-only copies of the memory addresses and write enable; they\r\n    // are stored inverted (reset value all ones) so that synthesis does not\r\n    // merge them with the internal registers, which have the same next state\r\n    logic [5:0] wp_on, rp_on;\r\n    logic       wr_on;\r\n    logic [5:0] acc_q, wp_q, rp_q;\r\n    logic [LAT-1:0] v_q;                 // valid bit of each pipeline rank\r\n    logic signed [31:0] p;\r\n\r\n    wire acc = EN_mult & rdy_mult_q;\r\n    wire rd  = EN_blockRead & rdy_rd_q;\r\n    wire wr  = v_q[LAT-1];\r\n\r\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n        if (!RST_N) begin\r\n            rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; vld_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            rdy_mult_on <= 1'b0; rdy_rd_on <= 1'b1;\r\n            wp_on <= '1; rp_on <= '1; wr_on <= 1'b1;\r\n            acc_q <= '0; wp_q <= '0; rp_q <= '0; v_q <= '0;\r\n"]
[19668.356, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv\r\n// mkMultBuff.sv -- 800 MHz implementation (1.25 ns clock), Nangate45 slow corner.\r\n//\r\n// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer (SPEC.md).\r\n// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, carry-select adder),\r\n// with\r\n// seven register ranks (LAT = 7):\r\n//   rank 1: operand register; mult_input1 is Booth-recoded before it\r\n//   rank 2: selected partial products (8 rows of 17 bits + 8 \"+1\" bits)\r\n//   rank 3: carry-save level 1 (9 -> 6 rows)\r\n//   rank 4: carry-save levels 2 and 3 (6 -> 4 -> 3 rows)\r\n//   rank 5: carry-save level 4 (3 -> 2 rows), stored as generate/propagate\r\n//   rank 6: carry-select adder stage A (4-bit blocks: sums for carry-in 0/1,\r\n//           block carry-outs)\r\n//   rank 7: product, after the block-carry prefix and the sum selection;\r\n//           drives writeMem_val directly\r\n// A LAT-bit valid shift register runs alongside the datapath and drives\r\n// EN_writeMem (F4).\r\n//\r\n// Control: the registered ready flags rdy_mult_q / rdy_rd_q are the fill /\r\n// drain state machine (FILL = {1,0}, WAIT = {0,0}, DRAIN = {0,1}); acc_q counts\r\n// pairs accepted in the fill phase, so pairs in flight count against the\r\n// capacity (F5); wp_q / rp_q are the write and read pointers. Changes from the\r\n// 400 MHz control for timing at 1.25 ns: separate write and read pointers, and\r\n// port-only copies of RDY_mult, RDY_blockRead, writeMem_addr, readMem_addr and\r\n// EN_writeMem, so the output load does not slow the internal handshake logic.\r\n// All outputs come from registers except EN_readMem (= EN_blockRead &\r\n// RDY_blockRead, F7) and memVal_data (= readMem_val, F8).\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (F14, F15).\r\nmodule mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (\r\n    input  logic         clk,\r\n    input  logic         RST_N,\r\n    input  logic         EN_mult,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input0,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input1,\r\n    output logic         RDY_mult,\r\n    input  logic         EN_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         RDY_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         VALID_memVal,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] memVal_data,\r\n    output logic         EN_writeMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   writeMem_addr,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] writeMem_val,\r\n    output logic         EN_readMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   readMem_addr,\r\n    input  logic [N-1:0] readMem_val\r\n);\r\n    // multiplier pipeline configuration (see mult_pipe.sv)\r\n    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1101;\r\n    localparam bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + SEL_REG + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n                                     + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3] + (CPA_SPLIT | CPA_CSEL) + 1;\r\n\r\n    logic       rdy_mult_q, rdy_rd_q, vld_q;\r\n    // copies of the two ready flags that drive only the output ports, so the\r\n    // port load does not slow the internal handshake logic (stored inverted,\r\n    // see below)\r\n    logic rdy_mult_on, rdy_rd_on;\r\n    // likewise port-only copies of the memory addresses and write enable; they\r\n    // are stored inverted (reset value all ones) so that synthesis does not\r\n    // merge them with the internal registers, which have the same next state\r\n    logic [5:0] wp_on, rp_on;\r\n    logic       wr_on;\r\n    logic [5:0] acc_q, wp_q, rp_q;\r\n    logic [LAT-1:0] v_q;                 // valid bit of each pipeline rank\r\n    logic signed [31:0] p;\r\n\r\n    wire acc = EN_mult & rdy_mult_q;\r\n    wire rd  = EN_blockRead & rdy_rd_q;\r\n    wire wr  = v_q[LAT-1];\r\n\r\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n        if (!RST_N) begin\r\n            rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; vld_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            rdy_mult_on <= 1'b0; rdy_rd_on <= 1'b1;\r\n            wp_on <= '1; rp_on <= '1; wr_on <= 1'b1;\r\n            acc_q <= '0; wp_q <= '0; rp_q <= '0; v_q <= '0;\r\n        end else begin\r\n            v_q <= {v_q[LAT-2:0], acc};\r\n            if (acc) begin\r\n                acc_q <= acc_q + 6'd1;\r\n                if (acc_q == 6'd63) begin rdy_mult_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_on <= 1'b1; end\r\n            end\r\n            if (wr) begin wp_q <= wp_q + 6'd1; wp_on <= ~(wp_q + 6'd1); end\r\n            if (rd) begin rp_q <= rp_q + 6'd1; rp_on <= ~(rp_q + 6'd1); end\r\n            wr_on <= ~v_q[LAT-2];\r\n            if (wr && wp_q == 6'd63) begin rdy_rd_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_on <= 1'b0; end\r\n            if (rd && rp_q == 6'd63) begin\r\n                rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1;\r\n                rdy_rd_on <= 1'b1; rdy_mult_on <= 1'b0;\r\n            end\r\n            vld_q <= rd;\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .SEL_REG(SEL_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT), .CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL), .CSW(4), .GP4(1'b1))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(clk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n\r\n    assign RDY_mult      = ~rdy_mult_on;\r\n    assign RDY_blockRead = ~rdy_rd_on;\r\n    assign EN_writeMem   = ~wr_on;\r\n    assign writeMem_addr = ~wp_on;\r\n    assign writeMem_val  = p;\r\n    assign EN_readMem    = rd;\r\n    assign readMem_addr  = ~rp_on;\r\n    assign VALID_memVal  = vld_q;\r\n    assign memVal_data   = readMem_val;\r\nendmodule : mkMultBuff\r\n// mult_pipe.sv -- pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier: radix-4 (modified) Booth\r\n// partial products, carry-save (3:2) reduction 9->6->4->3->2 rows and a final\r\n// carry-propagate adder. Every pipeline cut is optional (parameters).\r\n//   PRE_ENC  : Booth-recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n//   ENC_REG  : (PRE_ENC = 0 only) extra rank after the Booth recoding\r\n//   SEL_REG  : register the selected partial products (8 x 17 bits + 8 \"+1\" bits)\r\n//   CSA_REG  : bit k set -> register after carry-save level k+1 (k = 0..3)\r\n//   GP4      : the level-4 register holds generate/propagate (c&s, c^s) of the\r\n//              two final rows instead of the rows themselves (same width)\r\n//   CPA_CSEL : two-stage carry-select final adder with CSW-bit blocks and\r\n//              Kogge-Stone prefixes inside the blocks and across the blocks\r\n//   CPA_SPLIT: (alternative) low 16 bits in one stage, high 16 bits in the next\r\n// Register ranks (= latency from 'en' to 'p'): 1 (operand) + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG)\r\n//   + SEL_REG + popcount(CSA_REG) + (CPA_CSEL | CPA_SPLIT) + 1 (product)\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset. When 'en' is 0 the operand\r\n// register loads zeros (operand isolation), so an idle multiplier does not toggle.\r\n// Written for this project; the Booth recoding, the sign-extension constant and\r\n// the prefix adders follow textbook schemes (see the report's references).\r\nmodule mult_pipe #(\r\n    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n    parameter bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1000,\r\n    parameter bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter int       CSW       = 8,\r\n    parameter bit       GP4       = 1'b0\r\n) (\r\n    input  logic               clk,\r\n    input  logic               RST_N,\r\n    input  logic               en,     // accept: load operands, else load zeros\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] a,      // multiplicand (unregistered input)\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] b,      // multiplier   (unregistered input)\r\n    output logic signed [31:0] p       // product, registered\r\n);\r\n    // Booth radix-4 recoding of y: digit_i = -2 y[2i+1] + y[2i] + y[2i-1]\r\n    function automatic logic [23:0] booth_enc(input logic [15:0] y);\r\n        logic [16:0] yx;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one, two, neg;\r\n        yx = {y, 1'b0};                       // yx[k+1] = y[k], yx[0] = y[-1] = 0\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin\r\n            one[i] = yx[2*i+1] ^ yx[2*i];\r\n            two[i] = (yx[2*i+2] & ~yx[2*i+1] & ~yx[2*i]) | (~yx[2*i+2] & yx[2*i+1] & yx[2*i]);\r\n            neg[i] = yx[2*i+2];\r\n        end\r\n        booth_enc = {neg, two, one};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ---- stage 0: operand register (operand isolation: zeros when idle)\r\n    logic [7:0]  one_e, two_e, neg_e;\r\n    logic [15:0] a_e;\r\n    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\r\n        // recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_q, two_q, neg_q;\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_q, two_q, neg_q};\r\n    end else begin : g_post\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_d, two_d, neg_d;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {neg_d, two_d, one_d} = booth_enc(b_q);\r\n        if (ENC_REG) begin : g_enc\r\n            logic [7:0]  one_r, two_r, neg_r;\r\n            logic [15:0] a_r;\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n                if (!RST_N) begin a_r <= '0; one_r <= '0; two_r <= '0; neg_r <= '0; end\r\n                else begin a_r <= a_q; one_r <= one_d; two_r <= two_d; neg_r <= neg_d; end\r\n            end\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_r, one_r, two_r, neg_r};\r\n        end else begin : g_noenc\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_d, two_d, neg_d};\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    genvar i;\r\n\r\n    localparam int NB = 32 / CSW;     // carry-select blocks\r\n\r\n    // Kogge-Stone prefix over the NB block carries (generate = carry-out with\r\n    // carry-in 0, propagate = carry-out with carry-in 1)\r\n    function automatic logic [NB-1:0] bprefix(input logic [NB-1:0] g, input logic [NB-1:0] p);\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] G, P;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        for (int d = 1; d < NB; d = 2 * d)\r\n            for (int j = NB - 1; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]);\r\n                P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n            end\r\n        bprefix = G;\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // Kogge-Stone prefix over a CSW-bit block: G[j] / P[j] = group generate /\r\n    // propagate of bits j..0 of the block\r\n    function automatic logic [2*CSW-1:0] prefix(input logic [CSW-1:0] g, input logic [CSW-1:0] p);\r\n        logic [CSW-1:0] G, P;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        for (int d = 1; d < CSW; d = 2 * d)\r\n            for (int j = CSW - 1; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]);\r\n                P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n            end\r\n        prefix = {G, P};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // Partial-product rows. Sign extension is replaced by inverting each row's\r\n    // sign bit and adding the constant K = -sum(2^(16+2i)) (mod 2^32); the\r\n    // \"+1\" of each negative row is placed in the free bit of the next row.\r\n    localparam logic [31:0] K = 32'hAAAB_0000;  // -(2^16+2^18+...+2^30) mod 2^32\r\n    wire [16:0] a17 = {a_e[15], a_e};\r\n    wire [16:0] a2  = {a_e, 1'b0};\r\n    logic [31:0] r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8;\r\n    logic [16:0] pp [0:7];\r\n    logic [31:0] rw [0:7];\r\n    generate for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_pp\r\n        assign pp[i] = (({17{one_e[i]}} & a17) | ({17{two_e[i]}} & a2)) ^ {17{neg_e[i]}};\r\n        if (i == 0) begin : g_r0\r\n            assign rw[i] = {15'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0]};\r\n        end else begin : g_ri\r\n            // bits [2i+16:2i] hold the row, bit 2i-2 holds the +1 of row i-1\r\n            assign rw[i] = {13'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0], 1'b0, neg_e[i-1]} << (2*i-2);\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7} = {rw[0], rw[1], rw[2], rw[3], rw[4], rw[5], rw[6], rw[7]};\r\n    assign r8 = K | ({31'd0, neg_e[7]} << 14);\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // carry-save levels (3:2 compressors on whole rows); each optionally registered\r\n    function automatic logic [63:0] csa(input logic [31:0] x, y, z);\r\n        csa = {((x & y) | (x & z) | (y & z)) << 1, x ^ y ^ z};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // level 1: 9 -> 6, level 2: 6 -> 4, level 3: 4 -> 3, level 4: 3 -> 2\r\n    logic [6*32-1:0] l1, l1q;\r\n    logic [4*32-1:0] l2, l2q;\r\n    logic [3*32-1:0] l3, l3q;\r\n    logic [2*32-1:0] l4, l4q;\r\n    // optional register after partial-product selection (8 rows of 17 bits + the\r\n    // row +1 bits; the constant part of row 8 is re-created after the register)\r\n    logic [31:0] q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8;\r\n    generate if (SEL_REG) begin : g_sel\r\n        logic [16:0] ppq [0:7];\r\n        logic [7:0]  negq;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_q\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) ppq[i] <= RST_N ? pp[i] : 17'd0;\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) negq <= RST_N ? neg_e : 8'd0;\r\n        assign q0 = {15'd0, ~ppq[0][16], ppq[0][15:0]};\r\n        assign q1 = {13'd0, ~ppq[1][16], ppq[1][15:0], 1'b0, negq[0]} << 0;\r\n        assign q2 = {13'd0, ~ppq[2][16], ppq[2][15:0], 1'b0, negq[1]} << 2;\r\n        assign q3 = {13'd0, ~ppq[3][16], ppq[3][15:0], 1'b0, negq[2]} << 4;\r\n        assign q4 = {13'd0, ~ppq[4][16], ppq[4][15:0], 1'b0, negq[3]} << 6;\r\n        assign q5 = {13'd0, ~ppq[5][16], ppq[5][15:0], 1'b0, negq[4]} << 8;\r\n        assign q6 = {13'd0, ~ppq[6][16], ppq[6][15:0], 1'b0, negq[5]} << 10;\r\n        assign q7 = {13'd0, ~ppq[7][16], ppq[7][15:0], 1'b0, negq[6]} << 12;\r\n        assign q8 = K | ({31'd0, negq[7]} << 14);\r\n    end else begin : g_nosel\r\n        assign {q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8} = {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8};\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign l1 = {csa(q6, q7, q8), csa(q3, q4, q5), csa(q0, q1, q2)};\r\n    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    // level 4 output: the two final rows {c, s}, or (GP4) their bitwise\r\n    // generate / propagate {c & s, c ^ s}, so the adder's first gate level\r\n    // moves in front of the level-4 register\r\n    logic [63:0] l4cs;\r\n    assign l4cs = csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n    assign l4 = GP4 ? {l4cs[63:32] & l4cs[31:0], l4cs[63:32] ^ l4cs[31:0]} : l4cs;\r\n\r\n    generate\r\n        if (CSA_REG[0]) begin : g_r1\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l1q <= RST_N ? l1 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n1\r\n            assign l1q = l1;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[1]) begin : g_r2\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l2q <= RST_N ? l2 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n2\r\n            assign l2q = l2;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[2]) begin : g_r3\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l3q <= RST_N ? l3 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n3\r\n            assign l3q = l3;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[3]) begin : g_r4\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l4q <= RST_N ? l4 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n4\r\n            assign l4q = l4;\r\n        end\r\n    endgenerate\r\n    wire [31:0] sx = l4q[31:0], sy = l4q[63:32];\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // final carry-propagate adder, registered product\r\n    generate if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\r\n        // two-stage carry-select adder with CSW-bit blocks. Stage A: per block,\r\n        // bit generate/propagate and an in-block Kogge-Stone prefix give the\r\n        // block sums for carry-in 0 and carry-in 1 and the two block carry-outs.\r\n        // Stage B: the block carries are resolved and each block sum selected.\r\n        logic [31:0]   s0, s1, s0q, s1q;\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] co0, co1, co0q, co1q, cin;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_blk\r\n            logic [CSW-1:0] gg, pp_, G, P;\r\n            if (GP4) begin : g_gp\r\n                assign gg  = sy[CSW*i +: CSW];        // generate (registered)\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW];        // propagate (registered)\r\n            end else begin : g_cs\r\n                assign gg  = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] & sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            end\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(gg, pp_);\r\n            assign s0[CSW*i +: CSW] = pp_ ^ {G[CSW-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n            assign s1[CSW*i +: CSW] = pp_ ^ {G[CSW-2:0] | P[CSW-2:0], 1'b1};\r\n            assign co0[i] = G[CSW-1];\r\n            assign co1[i] = G[CSW-1] | P[CSW-1];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                s0q <= '0; s1q <= '0; co0q <= '0; co1q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                s0q <= s0; s1q <= s1; co0q <= co0; co1q <= co1;\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        // carry into block i = group generate of blocks i-1..0\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] bg;\r\n        assign bg  = bprefix(co0q, co1q);\r\n        assign cin = {bg[NB-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n        logic [31:0] psel;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_sel\r\n            assign psel[CSW*i +: CSW] = cin[i] ? s1q[CSW*i +: CSW] : s0q[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? psel : 32'd0;\r\n    end else if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n        logic [16:0] lo;\r\n        logic [15:0] lo_q, xh_q, yh_q;\r\n        logic        c_q;\r\n        assign lo = {1'b0, sx[15:0]} + {1'b0, sy[15:0]};\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                lo_q <= '0; c_q <= 1'b0; xh_q <= '0; yh_q <= '0; p <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                lo_q <= lo[15:0]; c_q <= lo[16];\r\n                xh_q <= sx[31:16]; yh_q <= sy[31:16];\r\n                p    <= {xh_q + yh_q + {15'd0, c_q}, lo_q};\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n    end else begin : g_full\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) p <= '0;\r\n            else        p <= sx + sy;\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\nendmodule : mult_pipe\r\n"]
[19668.369, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh; grep -n \"Checkpoint 3\" -A80 notes/WORKLOG.md | head -160\r\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n# eval_candidate.sh RUN RTL_DIR WORK_DIR [make overrides...]\r\n# Runs one candidate implementation through the open-source flow (synth, RTL check,\r\n# zero-delay gate sim, activity power) and prints one summary block: slack, area\r\n# split sequential/combinational, flops, vectorless and activity power, and the flop\r\n# count and worst setup slack of every register group (Q-net name).\r\n# Example: bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 build/cand/x/rtl build/cand/x\r\nset -uo pipefail\r\nRUN=$1; RTL=$2; W=$3; shift 3\r\nmkdir -p \"$W/rep\"\r\nM=\"RUN=$RUN RTL_DIR=$RTL BUILD=$W REP=$W/rep NETLIST=$W/map.v SDF=$W/map.sdf $*\"\r\nmake -s check $M > \"$W/check.out\" 2>&1; CHK=$(grep -c \"^ALL PASS\" \"$W/rep/check.log\" 2>/dev/null)\r\nmake -s synth $M > \"$W/synth.out\" 2>&1\r\nmake -s sim $M > \"$W/sim.out\" 2>&1;   SIM=$(grep -c \"^ALL PASS\" \"$W/rep/sim.log\" 2>/dev/null)\r\nmake -s power $M > \"$W/power.out\" 2>&1\r\nPER=$([ \"$RUN\" = 400 ] && echo 2.5 || echo 1.25)\r\ndocker run --rm -v \"$PWD:$PWD\" -w \"$PWD\" -e LIB=tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib -e NETLIST=\"$W/map.v\" \\\r\n  -e PERIOD=\"$PER\" --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta \\\r\n  openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a \\\r\n  -no_init -no_splash -exit submission/scripts/ranks.tcl > \"$W/rep/ranks.rpt\" 2>&1\r\nS=\"$W/rep/sta.rpt\"\r\nWNS=$(awk '/^worst slack max/{print $NF}' \"$S\"); WHS=$(awk '/^worst slack min/{print $NF}' \"$S\")\r\nAREA=$(grep \"^cell area\" \"$S\")\r\nTOT=$(echo \"$AREA\" | sed 's/cell area \\([0-9.]*\\).*/\\1/'); SEQ=$(echo \"$AREA\" | sed 's/.*sequential \\([0-9.]*\\).*/\\1/')\r\nFF=$(awk '/^cell DFF/{n+=$3} END{print n}' \"$S\")\r\nPV=$(awk '/^Total/{print $5*1e6; exit}' \"$S\")\r\nPS=$(awk 'NR>2{printf \"%s=%s \", $1, $NF}' \"$W/rep/power_summary.txt\" 2>/dev/null)\r\necho \"== $W RUN=$RUN\"\r\necho \"check=$([ \"$CHK\" = 1 ] && echo PASS || echo FAIL) sim=$([ \"$SIM\" = 1 ] && echo PASS || echo FAIL) wns=$WNS whs=$WHS\"\r\nprintf \"area=%s seq=%s comb=%.1f flops=%s vectorless_uW=%.1f\\n\" \"$TOT\" \"$SEQ\" \"$(echo \"$TOT - $SEQ\" | bc)\" \"$FF\" \"$PV\"\r\necho \"activity_uW: $PS\"\r\necho \"per register group (flops, worst slack):\"; cat \"$W/rep/ranks.rpt\" | grep -v \"^Warning\"\r\n90:## Checkpoint 3: 800 MHz\r\n91-\r\n92-**First 800 MHz probes** (`build/exp/run.sh`, mult_pipe configurations at 1.25 ns): WNS between \u22121.1 and \u22122.8 ns. The critical path was the `RST_N` input: one DFF_X1-modelled driver into 90 to 174 synchronous-reset gates, 1.4 to 2.6 ns. The Resizer cannot buffer it without placement (RSZ-0075 makeBufferedNet failed), and ABC's `buffer -p` changed nothing (the results were bit-identical).\r\n93-- **Fix in resize.tcl:** a throw-away floorplan plus global placement, made only so the Resizer can insert buffers. Timing inside the Resizer stays on the wire-load model (no `estimate_parasitics`), so it is the same view as sign-off STA. Result at 800 MHz: \u22121.24 \u2192 \u22120.73 ns. At 400 MHz the result is identical (+0.152 ns, 2387 \u00b5m\u00b2).\r\n94-\r\n95-**Parallel candidate evaluations (two subagents) while I iterated on the Booth/CSA candidate:**\r\n96-- *(B) Behavioural `*` + R extra ranks + ABC retiming (`build/cand_retime/`):*\r\n97-  - Best result: WNS \u22120.20 ns at R=8, about 6.1k \u00b5m\u00b2. Retiming in ABC uses unit delays, so the result saturates near \u22120.2 ns.\r\n98-  - Plain retiming breaks F14: 319 of 432 flops had no reset after retiming, and ABC even moved registers onto RST_N. Keeping F14 needs a non-standard strip/re-add-reset step.\r\n99-  - Sign-off risk: the RTL alone is a one-stage multiplier followed by delay ranks, which GPDK045 sign-off would not retime. **Rejected.**\r\n100-  - Its SAT-based F14 netlist check was adopted as `make f14`.\r\n101-- *(C) Baugh-Wooley + Dadda, hand cut:* result pending at the time of writing; see below.\r\n102-- *(A) Booth/CSA mult_pipe, my own:* iterations below.\r\n103-\r\n104-**Booth/CSA iterations at 1.25 ns** (each fix found from the STA critical path; area is post-Resizer):\r\n105-\r\n106-| step | change | WNS ns | area \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n107-|---|---|---|---|\r\n108-| e800b | PRE_ENC, CS after L2 & L4, CPA split 16/16 | \u22121.136 | 3655 |\r\n109-| g800b | + placement-backed buffering | \u22120.729 | 4182 |\r\n110-| i800a | + SEL_REG (register after PP select), all 4 CSA levels registered, 2-stage carry-select adder | \u22120.610 | 5413 |\r\n111-| k800a | + ABC maps with a Liberty copy in which slow stacked cells are `dont_use` (`lib_dont_use.py`; `abc -dont_use` did not reach ABC's SCL) | \u22120.440 | 5573 |\r\n112-| m800b | carry-select adder rewritten with explicit in-block Kogge-Stone prefix computing both carry-in sums at once (Yosys had built `x+y+1` as two chained adders); 4-bit blocks | \u22120.159 | 5853 |\r\n113-| n800b | separate write and read pointers (the shared pointer drove 2 ports, 47 fF) | \u22120.090 | 5965 |\r\n114-| r800b | port-only copies of RDY_*, addresses and EN_writeMem, stored inverted so Yosys does not merge them with the internal copies (`(* keep *)` did not prevent merging) | \u22120.014 | 5786 |\r\n115-| t800b | block-carry prefix in stage B instead of a ripple | \u22120.034 | 5933 |\r\n116-| u800b | MUX2 also dont_use (MUX2_X1 0.24 ns) | +0.051 | 5893 |\r\n117-| v800b | GP4: L4 register holds generate/propagate of the final rows, moving the adder's first gate level into the L4 stage (0.36 ns slack there) | +0.136 | 5824 |\r\n118-| x800 | ABC output load 23.5 \u2192 1 fF: ABC sees every flop D pin as a primary output and had buffered each as if it drove the 23.5 fF port load | +0.150 | 5211 |\r\n119-| x800_1010 | CS registers only after L2 and L4 (473 flops instead of 577+) | \u22120.004 | 4431 |\r\n120-| y800_a | same, GP4 = 0 | +0.023 | 4465 |\r\n121-| z800_1011 | CS after L1, L2, L4 | \u22120.004 | 4973 |\r\n122-| **z800_1101** | **CS after L1, L3, L4 (L2+L3 share a stage: L3 is a single 3:2 on 3 of 4 rows)** | **+0.075** | **4755** |\r\n123-\r\n124-ABC results vary by about \u00b10.1\u20130.2 ns with small netlist-structure changes. For example, the 400 MHz RTL with the newer mult_pipe.sv (logically identical for its parameters) maps to \u22120.037 ns instead of +0.152 ns, so rtl_400 keeps its verified mult_pipe.sv. Each final configuration is deterministic, and the knobs are fixed per RUN in the Makefile (ABC_DRIVER, ABC_LOAD, DONT_USE).\r\n125-\r\n126-**rtl_800 = z800_1101** (latency 7, 577 flops; config in `submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv`). It meets the 62 ps target at the lowest area of the passing variants. The 1111 variant has more slack (+0.150 ns) but costs +456 \u00b5m\u00b2 and about +0.34 mW of vectorless power.\r\n127-\r\n128-| step | result |\r\n129-|---|---|\r\n130-| `make check RUN=800` | ALL PASS, latency 7 |\r\n131-| `make synth RUN=800` | WNS +0.075 ns, hold +0.041 ns, 4755.0 \u00b5m\u00b2, vectorless 2727.6 \u00b5W |\r\n132-| `make sim RUN=800` | ALL PASS |\r\n133-| `make timing RUN=800` | ALL PASS, 384 products |\r\n134-| `make power RUN=800` | run 3073 \u00b5W, fill window 5210 \u00b5W, drain window 2536 \u00b5W |\r\n135-| `make f14 RUN=400` | 166/166 flops reset-gated (SAT) |\r\n136-| `make f14 RUN=800` | 577/577 flops reset-gated (SAT) |\r\n137-\r\n138-`make synth RUN=400` with the final scripts and the 400 knobs reproduces the committed netlist exactly: +0.152 ns, 2386.552 \u00b5m\u00b2, and `git status` shows the netlist and SDF unchanged.\r\n139-\r\n140-**Candidate (C), Baugh-Wooley + Dadda (subagent, `build/cand_dadda/`).**\r\n141-- *Best version (v6):* WNS +0.150 ns, hold +0.076 ns, 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2, 616 flops, latency 8, check/sim ALL PASS.\r\n142-- *Power (\u00b5W):*\r\n143-\r\n144-  | case | (C) Dadda v6 | (A) Booth/CSA |\r\n145-  |---|---|---|\r\n146-  | whole run | 3279 | 3073 |\r\n147-  | fill window | 5725 | 5210 |\r\n148-  | drain window | 2702 | 2536 |\r\n149-  | vectorless | 2820 | 2728 |\r\n150-\r\n151-- *Control:* it independently found the same control problem (ptr/RDY port load) and solved it with inverted twin registers and split 3-bit counters.\r\n152-- *Two smaller variants it rejected:* v7 drops the product register (writeMem_val comes from logic); v8 puts the PP/tree logic on the input path (0.97 ns), which is risky for the sign-off testbench.\r\n153-\r\n154-**Decision for 800 MHz: (A) Booth/CSA `z800_1101`.**\r\n155-- Both (A) and (C) meet the 62 ps target. (A) has 10 % less area (4755 vs 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2) and 6\u20139 % less power in every case, which SPEC Section 5 ranks after timing and area.\r\n156-- (C) has twice the slack margin (150 ps vs 75 ps), but the target is met by both.\r\n157-- (B), retiming, fails timing (\u22120.20 ns) and needs reset re-insertion; rejected.\r\n158-\r\n159-**Mutation test at 800 MHz** (`submission/scripts/mutate.sh 800`): 13/13 mutants killed. The extra mutants vs 400 are EN_writeMem one cycle early, the inverted port copy not reset, and a carry-select carry-in error in mult_pipe.\r\n160-\r\n161-**Waveform figures** (`submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 400|800`). The same gate-level checker drives the RTL and the SDF-annotated netlist, so the waves line up. GTKWave 3.3.116 runs under `xvfb-run` with `-S` Tcl scripts (`/File/Grab_To_File`), light colours set by `--rcvar`, and ImageMagick crops. Windows: first writes, transition to drain, end of drain, and a 3-cycle zoom.\r\n162-\r\n163-Gate-level only effects visible in the zoom:\r\n164-- clock-to-output delay of 0.45\u20130.7 ns on the registered outputs at 400 MHz;\r\n165-- a short intermediate value on writeMem_val while bits with different clk\u2192Q settle;\r\n166-- EN_readMem following EN_blockRead (driven 20 ps after the edge) through one AND gate.\r\n167-\r\n168-RDY_mult is a register output in both designs, so it shows no glitch.\r\n169-\r\n170-## Checkpoint 4: power\r\n"]
[19668.576, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 80,200p submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv; cat submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh; grep -n \"Checkpoint 3\" -A80 notes/WORKLOG.md | head -150\r\n            acc_q <= '0; wp_q <= '0; rp_q <= '0; v_q <= '0;\r\n        end else begin\r\n            v_q <= {v_q[LAT-2:0], acc};\r\n            if (acc) begin\r\n                acc_q <= acc_q + 6'd1;\r\n                if (acc_q == 6'd63) begin rdy_mult_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_on <= 1'b1; end\r\n            end\r\n            if (wr) begin wp_q <= wp_q + 6'd1; wp_on <= ~(wp_q + 6'd1); end\r\n            if (rd) begin rp_q <= rp_q + 6'd1; rp_on <= ~(rp_q + 6'd1); end\r\n            wr_on <= ~v_q[LAT-2];\r\n            if (wr && wp_q == 6'd63) begin rdy_rd_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_on <= 1'b0; end\r\n            if (rd && rp_q == 6'd63) begin\r\n                rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1;\r\n                rdy_rd_on <= 1'b1; rdy_mult_on <= 1'b0;\r\n            end\r\n            vld_q <= rd;\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .SEL_REG(SEL_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT), .CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL), .CSW(4), .GP4(1'b1))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(clk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n\r\n    assign RDY_mult      = ~rdy_mult_on;\r\n    assign RDY_blockRead = ~rdy_rd_on;\r\n    assign EN_writeMem   = ~wr_on;\r\n    assign writeMem_addr = ~wp_on;\r\n    assign writeMem_val  = p;\r\n    assign EN_readMem    = rd;\r\n    assign readMem_addr  = ~rp_on;\r\n    assign VALID_memVal  = vld_q;\r\n    assign memVal_data   = readMem_val;\r\nendmodule : mkMultBuff\r\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n# eval_candidate.sh RUN RTL_DIR WORK_DIR [make overrides...]\r\n# Runs one candidate implementation through the open-source flow (synth, RTL check,\r\n# zero-delay gate sim, activity power) and prints one summary block: slack, area\r\n# split sequential/combinational, flops, vectorless and activity power, and the flop\r\n# count and worst setup slack of every register group (Q-net name).\r\n# Example: bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 build/cand/x/rtl build/cand/x\r\nset -uo pipefail\r\nRUN=$1; RTL=$2; W=$3; shift 3\r\nmkdir -p \"$W/rep\"\r\nM=\"RUN=$RUN RTL_DIR=$RTL BUILD=$W REP=$W/rep NETLIST=$W/map.v SDF=$W/map.sdf $*\"\r\nmake -s check $M > \"$W/check.out\" 2>&1; CHK=$(grep -c \"^ALL PASS\" \"$W/rep/check.log\" 2>/dev/null)\r\nmake -s synth $M > \"$W/synth.out\" 2>&1\r\nmake -s sim $M > \"$W/sim.out\" 2>&1;   SIM=$(grep -c \"^ALL PASS\" \"$W/rep/sim.log\" 2>/dev/null)\r\nmake -s power $M > \"$W/power.out\" 2>&1\r\nPER=$([ \"$RUN\" = 400 ] && echo 2.5 || echo 1.25)\r\ndocker run --rm -v \"$PWD:$PWD\" -w \"$PWD\" -e LIB=tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib -e NETLIST=\"$W/map.v\" \\\r\n  -e PERIOD=\"$PER\" --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta \\\r\n  openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a \\\r\n  -no_init -no_splash -exit submission/scripts/ranks.tcl > \"$W/rep/ranks.rpt\" 2>&1\r\nS=\"$W/rep/sta.rpt\"\r\nWNS=$(awk '/^worst slack max/{print $NF}' \"$S\"); WHS=$(awk '/^worst slack min/{print $NF}' \"$S\")\r\nAREA=$(grep \"^cell area\" \"$S\")\r\nTOT=$(echo \"$AREA\" | sed 's/cell area \\([0-9.]*\\).*/\\1/'); SEQ=$(echo \"$AREA\" | sed 's/.*sequential \\([0-9.]*\\).*/\\1/')\r\nFF=$(awk '/^cell DFF/{n+=$3} END{print n}' \"$S\")\r\nPV=$(awk '/^Total/{print $5*1e6; exit}' \"$S\")\r\nPS=$(awk 'NR>2{printf \"%s=%s \", $1, $NF}' \"$W/rep/power_summary.txt\" 2>/dev/null)\r\necho \"== $W RUN=$RUN\"\r\necho \"check=$([ \"$CHK\" = 1 ] && echo PASS || echo FAIL) sim=$([ \"$SIM\" = 1 ] && echo PASS || echo FAIL) wns=$WNS whs=$WHS\"\r\nprintf \"area=%s seq=%s comb=%.1f flops=%s vectorless_uW=%.1f\\n\" \"$TOT\" \"$SEQ\" \"$(echo \"$TOT - $SEQ\" | bc)\" \"$FF\" \"$PV\"\r\necho \"activity_uW: $PS\"\r\necho \"per register group (flops, worst slack):\"; cat \"$W/rep/ranks.rpt\" | grep -v \"^Warning\"\r\n90:## Checkpoint 3: 800 MHz\r\n91-\r\n92-**First 800 MHz probes** (`build/exp/run.sh`, mult_pipe configurations at 1.25 ns): WNS between \u22121.1 and \u22122.8 ns. The critical path was the `RST_N` input: one DFF_X1-modelled driver into 90 to 174 synchronous-reset gates, 1.4 to 2.6 ns. The Resizer cannot buffer it without placement (RSZ-0075 makeBufferedNet failed), and ABC's `buffer -p` changed nothing (the results were bit-identical).\r\n93-- **Fix in resize.tcl:** a throw-away floorplan plus global placement, made only so the Resizer can insert buffers. Timing inside the Resizer stays on the wire-load model (no `estimate_parasitics`), so it is the same view as sign-off STA. Result at 800 MHz: \u22121.24 \u2192 \u22120.73 ns. At 400 MHz the result is identical (+0.152 ns, 2387 \u00b5m\u00b2).\r\n94-\r\n95-**Parallel candidate evaluations (two subagents) while I iterated on the Booth/CSA candidate:**\r\n96-- *(B) Behavioural `*` + R extra ranks + ABC retiming (`build/cand_retime/`):*\r\n97-  - Best result: WNS \u22120.20 ns at R=8, about 6.1k \u00b5m\u00b2. Retiming in ABC uses unit delays, so the result saturates near \u22120.2 ns.\r\n98-  - Plain retiming breaks F14: 319 of 432 flops had no reset after retiming, and ABC even moved registers onto RST_N. Keeping F14 needs a non-standard strip/re-add-reset step.\r\n99-  - Sign-off risk: the RTL alone is a one-stage multiplier followed by delay ranks, which GPDK045 sign-off would not retime. **Rejected.**\r\n100-  - Its SAT-based F14 netlist check was adopted as `make f14`.\r\n101-- *(C) Baugh-Wooley + Dadda, hand cut:* result pending at the time of writing; see below.\r\n102-- *(A) Booth/CSA mult_pipe, my own:* iterations below.\r\n103-\r\n104-**Booth/CSA iterations at 1.25 ns** (each fix found from the STA critical path; area is post-Resizer):\r\n105-\r\n106-| step | change | WNS ns | area \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n107-|---|---|---|---|\r\n108-| e800b | PRE_ENC, CS after L2 & L4, CPA split 16/16 | \u22121.136 | 3655 |\r\n109-| g800b | + placement-backed buffering | \u22120.729 | 4182 |\r\n110-| i800a | + SEL_REG (register after PP select), all 4 CSA levels registered, 2-stage carry-select adder | \u22120.610 | 5413 |\r\n111-| k800a | + ABC maps with a Liberty copy in which slow stacked cells are `dont_use` (`lib_dont_use.py`; `abc -dont_use` did not reach ABC's SCL) | \u22120.440 | 5573 |\r\n112-| m800b | carry-select adder rewritten with explicit in-block Kogge-Stone prefix computing both carry-in sums at once (Yosys had built `x+y+1` as two chained adders); 4-bit blocks | \u22120.159 | 5853 |\r\n113-| n800b | separate write and read pointers (the shared pointer drove 2 ports, 47 fF) | \u22120.090 | 5965 |\r\n114-| r800b | port-only copies of RDY_*, addresses and EN_writeMem, stored inverted so Yosys does not merge them with the internal copies (`(* keep *)` did not prevent merging) | \u22120.014 | 5786 |\r\n115-| t800b | block-carry prefix in stage B instead of a ripple | \u22120.034 | 5933 |\r\n116-| u800b | MUX2 also dont_use (MUX2_X1 0.24 ns) | +0.051 | 5893 |\r\n117-| v800b | GP4: L4 register holds generate/propagate of the final rows, moving the adder's first gate level into the L4 stage (0.36 ns slack there) | +0.136 | 5824 |\r\n118-| x800 | ABC output load 23.5 \u2192 1 fF: ABC sees every flop D pin as a primary output and had buffered each as if it drove the 23.5 fF port load | +0.150 | 5211 |\r\n119-| x800_1010 | CS registers only after L2 and L4 (473 flops instead of 577+) | \u22120.004 | 4431 |\r\n120-| y800_a | same, GP4 = 0 | +0.023 | 4465 |\r\n121-| z800_1011 | CS after L1, L2, L4 | \u22120.004 | 4973 |\r\n122-| **z800_1101** | **CS after L1, L3, L4 (L2+L3 share a stage: L3 is a single 3:2 on 3 of 4 rows)** | **+0.075** | **4755** |\r\n123-\r\n124-ABC results vary by about \u00b10.1\u20130.2 ns with small netlist-structure changes. For example, the 400 MHz RTL with the newer mult_pipe.sv (logically identical for its parameters) maps to \u22120.037 ns instead of +0.152 ns, so rtl_400 keeps its verified mult_pipe.sv. Each final configuration is deterministic, and the knobs are fixed per RUN in the Makefile (ABC_DRIVER, ABC_LOAD, DONT_USE).\r\n125-\r\n126-**rtl_800 = z800_1101** (latency 7, 577 flops; config in `submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv`). It meets the 62 ps target at the lowest area of the passing variants. The 1111 variant has more slack (+0.150 ns) but costs +456 \u00b5m\u00b2 and about +0.34 mW of vectorless power.\r\n127-\r\n128-| step | result |\r\n129-|---|---|\r\n130-| `make check RUN=800` | ALL PASS, latency 7 |\r\n131-| `make synth RUN=800` | WNS +0.075 ns, hold +0.041 ns, 4755.0 \u00b5m\u00b2, vectorless 2727.6 \u00b5W |\r\n132-| `make sim RUN=800` | ALL PASS |\r\n133-| `make timing RUN=800` | ALL PASS, 384 products |\r\n134-| `make power RUN=800` | run 3073 \u00b5W, fill window 5210 \u00b5W, drain window 2536 \u00b5W |\r\n135-| `make f14 RUN=400` | 166/166 flops reset-gated (SAT) |\r\n136-| `make f14 RUN=800` | 577/577 flops reset-gated (SAT) |\r\n137-\r\n138-`make synth RUN=400` with the final scripts and the 400 knobs reproduces the committed netlist exactly: +0.152 ns, 2386.552 \u00b5m\u00b2, and `git status` shows the netlist and SDF unchanged.\r\n139-\r\n140-**Candidate (C), Baugh-Wooley + Dadda (subagent, `build/cand_dadda/`).**\r\n141-- *Best version (v6):* WNS +0.150 ns, hold +0.076 ns, 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2, 616 flops, latency 8, check/sim ALL PASS.\r\n142-- *Power (\u00b5W):*\r\n143-\r\n144-  | case | (C) Dadda v6 | (A) Booth/CSA |\r\n145-  |---|---|---|\r\n146-  | whole run | 3279 | 3073 |\r\n147-  | fill window | 5725 | 5210 |\r\n148-  | drain window | 2702 | 2536 |\r\n149-  | vectorless | 2820 | 2728 |\r\n150-\r\n151-- *Control:* it independently found the same control problem (ptr/RDY port load) and solved it with inverted twin registers and split 3-bit counters.\r\n152-- *Two smaller variants it rejected:* v7 drops the product register (writeMem_val comes from logic); v8 puts the PP/tree logic on the input path (0.97 ns), which is risky for the sign-off testbench.\r\n153-\r\n154-**Decision for 800 MHz: (A) Booth/CSA `z800_1101`.**\r\n155-- Both (A) and (C) meet the 62 ps target. (A) has 10 % less area (4755 vs 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2) and 6\u20139 % less power in every case, which SPEC Section 5 ranks after timing and area.\r\n156-- (C) has twice the slack margin (150 ps vs 75 ps), but the target is met by both.\r\n157-- (B), retiming, fails timing (\u22120.20 ns) and needs reset re-insertion; rejected.\r\n158-\r\n159-**Mutation test at 800 MHz** (`submission/scripts/mutate.sh 800`): 13/13 mutants killed. The extra mutants vs 400 are EN_writeMem one cycle early, the inverted port copy not reset, and a carry-select carry-in error in mult_pipe.\r\n160-\r\n161-**Waveform figures** (`submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 400|800`). The same gate-level checker drives the RTL and the SDF-annotated netlist, so the waves line up. GTKWave 3.3.116 runs under `xvfb-run` with `-S` Tcl scripts (`/File/Grab_To_File`), light colours set by `--rcvar`, and ImageMagick crops. Windows: first writes, transition to drain, end of drain, and a 3-cycle zoom.\r\n162-\r\n163-Gate-level only effects visible in the zoom:\r\n164-- clock-to-output delay of 0.45\u20130.7 ns on the registered outputs at 400 MHz;\r\n165-- a short intermediate value on writeMem_val while bits with different clk\u2192Q settle;\r\n166-- EN_readMem following EN_blockRead (driven 20 ps after the edge) through one AND gate.\r\n167-\r\n168-RDY_mult is a register output in both designs, so it shows no glitch.\r\n169-\r\n170-## Checkpoint 4: power\r\n"]
[19670.835, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m wc -l build/cand_dadda/gen2.py && sed -n 1,200p build/cand_dadda/gen2.py; ls build/cand_dadda/v6; ls build/cand800b 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline | head -5\r\n549 build/cand_dadda/gen2.py\r\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"gen2.py -- generator for the pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier 'mult_tree'\r\n(800 MHz candidate: explicit partial-product array + carry-save tree).\r\n\r\nDatapath, stage by stage (every stage ends in a register rank):\r\n  stage 1      operand register a_q/b_q (loads zeros when no pair is accepted)\r\n               -> Baugh-Wooley partial products (AND / NAND, constants 2^16, 2^31)\r\n               -> first carry-save reduction\r\n  stage 2..T   timing-driven column-wise carry-save reduction (3-greedy: the three\r\n               earliest bits of a column go to a full adder, the latest one on the\r\n               fast 'c' input; half adders only where a column would exceed 2 bits).\r\n               With --pg the last tree stage also forms p = x^y, g = x&y per column.\r\n  CPA          carry-select adder over blocks of K bits:\r\n               C1: per block, sum with carry-in 0, the propagate prefix AND(p) of\r\n                   each bit position, block generate G and block propagate P\r\n               C2: Kogge-Stone prefix over the blocks -> block carry-in;\r\n                   with --cpa3 the block carries are registered and the selection\r\n                   s = s0 ^ (cin & ppre) happens in C3\r\n  product      register p (drives writeMem_val)\r\nConstant bits are tracked by the generator and never registered. Every register\r\nhas a synchronous active-low reset. Each stage gets a model budget (ns of logic\r\nafter clock-to-Q) and the reduction does as much as fits.\r\n\r\nusage: gen2.py OUTDIR [--budget B] [--b1 B1] [--k K] [--pg] [--cpa3]\r\nWrites OUTDIR/rtl/mult_tree.sv and OUTDIR/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv; prints a stage summary.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse, os, sys\r\n\r\nap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\nap.add_argument(\"outdir\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--budget\", type=float, default=0.62, help=\"logic budget per tree stage (model ns)\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--b1\", type=float, default=None, help=\"budget of stage 1 (PP + reduction)\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--t-and\", type=float, default=0.22, help=\"PP AND/NAND arrival (incl. operand fanout)\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--k\", type=int, default=8, help=\"carry-select block size\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--pg\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"form p/g in the last tree stage\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--cpa3\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"register block carries (3 CPA stages)\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--dadda\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"uniform target height per stage\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--plan\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"search greedy/target mode per stage for fewest flops\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--outcomb\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"no product register: selection drives p\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--inlogic\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"no operand register: PP and stage-1 reduction from the inputs\")\r\nap.add_argument(\"--xor\", type=float, default=0.20)\r\nap.add_argument(\"--maj\", type=float, default=0.22)\r\nargs = ap.parse_args()\r\nB = args.budget\r\nB1 = args.b1 if args.b1 is not None else B\r\nDX, DM, DA = args.xor, args.maj, 0.12\r\nEPS = 1e-6\r\nW = 32\r\nONE, ZERO = \"1'b1\", \"1'b0\"\r\n\r\ndecl = []    # declarations\r\nbody = []    # combinational logic, in stage order\r\nffs = []     # (stage, comment, [(dst, src)])\r\nnid = [0]\r\n\r\ndef new(prefix):\r\n    nid[0] += 1\r\n    return f\"{prefix}{nid[0]}\"\r\n\r\ndef is_const(b):\r\n    return b[0] in (ONE, ZERO)\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n# full / half adders on bits (name, arrival)\r\ndef fa(L, col, x, y, z, st):\r\n    s = new(f\"s{st}_\")\r\n    L.append(f\"    wire {s} = {x[0]} ^ {y[0]} ^ {z[0]};\")\r\n    t_s = max(max(x[1], y[1]) + DX, z[1]) + DX\r\n    if col + 1 >= W:\r\n        return (s, t_s), None\r\n    c = new(f\"c{st}_\")\r\n    L.append(f\"    wire {c} = ({x[0]} & {y[0]}) | ({x[0]} & {z[0]}) | ({y[0]} & {z[0]});\")\r\n    return (s, t_s), (c, max(x[1], y[1], z[1]) + DM)\r\n\r\ndef fa1(L, col, x, y, st):\r\n    \"\"\"full adder with a constant-1 input: sum = ~(x ^ y), carry = x | y\"\"\"\r\n    s = new(f\"s{st}_\")\r\n    L.append(f\"    wire {s} = ~({x[0]} ^ {y[0]});\")\r\n    t = max(x[1], y[1])\r\n    if col + 1 >= W:\r\n        return (s, t + DX), None\r\n    c = new(f\"c{st}_\")\r\n    L.append(f\"    wire {c} = {x[0]} | {y[0]};\")\r\n    return (s, t + DX), (c, t + DA)\r\n\r\ndef ha(L, col, x, y, st):\r\n    s = new(f\"s{st}_\")\r\n    L.append(f\"    wire {s} = {x[0]} ^ {y[0]};\")\r\n    t = max(x[1], y[1])\r\n    if col + 1 >= W:\r\n        return (s, t + DX), None\r\n    c = new(f\"c{st}_\")\r\n    L.append(f\"    wire {c} = {x[0]} & {y[0]};\")\r\n    return (s, t + DX), (c, t + DA)\r\n\r\ndef reduce_stage(cols, st, budget):\r\n    \"\"\"timing-driven reduction of all columns (LSB first) to <= 2 bits where the\r\n    budget allows. returns (lines, new columns, #FA, #HA)\"\"\"\r\n    L = []\r\n    out = [[] for _ in range(W)]\r\n    cin = []\r\n    nfa = nha = 0\r\n    for c in range(W):\r\n        bits = list(cols[c]) + cin\r\n        cin = []\r\n        while len(bits) > 2:\r\n            consts = [b for b in bits if is_const(b)]\r\n            v = sorted([b for b in bits if not is_const(b)], key=lambda b: b[1])\r\n            r = None\r\n            if consts and len(v) >= 2 and max(v[0][1], v[1][1]) + DX <= budget + EPS:\r\n                bits.remove(consts[0]); bits.remove(v[0]); bits.remove(v[1])\r\n                r = fa1(L, c, v[0], v[1], st); nfa += 1\r\n            elif len(v) >= 3:\r\n                x, y, z = v[0], v[1], v[2]\r\n                t_s = max(max(x[1], y[1]) + DX, z[1]) + DX\r\n                t_c = max(x[1], y[1], z[1]) + DM\r\n                if t_s <= budget + EPS and (c + 1 >= W or t_c <= budget + EPS):\r\n                    for b in (x, y, z):\r\n                        bits.remove(b)\r\n                    r = fa(L, c, x, y, z, st); nfa += 1\r\n                elif len(bits) == 3 and max(x[1], y[1]) + DX <= budget + EPS:\r\n                    bits.remove(x); bits.remove(y)\r\n                    r = ha(L, c, x, y, st); nha += 1\r\n            if r is None:\r\n                break\r\n            bits.append(r[0])\r\n            if r[1] is not None:\r\n                cin.append(r[1])\r\n        out[c] = bits\r\n    return L, out, nfa, nha\r\n\r\n\r\ndef reduce_target(cols, st, budget, target):\r\n    \"\"\"reduce every column to at most 'target' bits (3-greedy FA, HA when one bit\r\n    over); returns None if this does not fit the budget\"\"\"\r\n    L = []\r\n    out = [[] for _ in range(W)]\r\n    cin = []\r\n    nfa = nha = 0\r\n    for c in range(W):\r\n        bits = list(cols[c]) + cin\r\n        cin = []\r\n        while len(bits) > target:\r\n            consts = [b for b in bits if is_const(b)]\r\n            v = sorted([b for b in bits if not is_const(b)], key=lambda b: b[1])\r\n            if consts and len(v) >= 2 and len(bits) > target + 1:\r\n                if max(v[0][1], v[1][1]) + DX > budget + EPS:\r\n                    return None\r\n                bits.remove(consts[0]); bits.remove(v[0]); bits.remove(v[1])\r\n                r = fa1(L, c, v[0], v[1], st); nfa += 1\r\n            elif len(bits) == target + 1 or len(v) < 3:\r\n                if len(v) < 2:\r\n                    return None\r\n                x, y = v[0], v[1]\r\n                if max(x[1], y[1]) + DX > budget + EPS:\r\n                    return None\r\n                bits.remove(x); bits.remove(y)\r\n                r = ha(L, c, x, y, st); nha += 1\r\n            else:\r\n                x, y, z = v[0], v[1], v[2]\r\n                t_s = max(max(x[1], y[1]) + DX, z[1]) + DX\r\n                t_c = max(x[1], y[1], z[1]) + DM\r\n                if t_s > budget + EPS or (c + 1 < W and t_c > budget + EPS):\r\n                    return None\r\n                for b in (x, y, z):\r\n                    bits.remove(b)\r\n                r = fa(L, c, x, y, z, st); nfa += 1\r\n            bits.append(r[0])\r\n            if r[1] is not None:\r\n                cin.append(r[1])\r\n        out[c] = bits\r\n    return L, out, nfa, nha\r\n\r\ndef reduce_best(cols, st, budget):\r\n    if not args.dadda:\r\n        return reduce_stage(cols, st, budget)\r\n    for t in range(2, 17):\r\n        save = nid[0]\r\n        r = reduce_target(cols, st, budget, t)\r\n        if r is not None:\r\n            return r\r\n        nid[0] = save\r\n    sys.exit(\"no feasible target\")\r\n\r\ndef nbits(out):\r\n    return sum(1 for c in out for b in c if not is_const(b))\r\n\r\ndef reg0(out):\r\n    return [[(b[0], 0.0) if not is_const(b) else b for b in c] for c in out]\r\n\r\ndef try_mode(cols, st, budget, mode):\r\n    save = nid[0]\r\n    if mode == \"g\":\r\n        r = reduce_stage(cols, st, budget)\r\n    else:\r\n        r = None\r\n        found = 0\r\n        for t in range(2, 17):\r\n            r = reduce_target(cols, st, budget, t)\r\n            if r is not None:\r\ncheck.vvp\r\nrep\r\nrtl\r\n82a3a02 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i\r\ne1b93d2 Judge area and power on the sign-off results; allow candidate checks\r\n87b9178 Report revision: GPDK045 sign-off comparison, concise results-first structure, token usage update\r\n032bfb2 Checkpoint 5: final report, fresh-clone rerun log, token usage\r\n6dc9335 Checkpoint 5: report text fixes, work-log entry for the report\r\n"]
[19671.01, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n '170,400p' notes/WORKLOG.md | head -120; ls build/cand800a 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline | head -5; cat submission/scripts/ranks.tcl | head -40\r\n## Checkpoint 4: power\r\n\r\nActivity-based power uses OpenSTA `read_vcd` on the zero-delay gate-level VCD of `make sim`, which runs the full RTL-checker stimulus. It is reported for the whole run and for the two 64-cycle windows announced by the checker (`PWR_WIN`, passed as `-begin_time/-end_time`). The vectorless \"synthesis estimate\" is `report_power` with OpenSTA's default input activity of 0.1. Reports: `submission/syn_reports/<RUN>/{sta.rpt,power.rpt,power_summary.txt}`.\r\n\r\nPower in \u00b5W, slow corner (0.95 V, 125 \u00b0C):\r\n\r\n| case | 400 MHz | 800 MHz |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| vectorless estimate | 652.5 | 2727.6 |\r\n| whole run | 642.8 | 3073.1 |\r\n| fill window (64 back-to-back accepts) | 1480.1 | 5209.5 |\r\n| drain window (64 back-to-back reads, producer idle) | 430.4 | 2535.6 |\r\n\r\nIn the drain window, sequential internal (clock) power dominates: 158 flops at 400 MHz and 577 at 800 MHz, with no clock gating.\r\n\r\n**Operand-isolation experiment** (400 MHz, `build/noiso400`; operand registers load the inputs every cycle instead of zeros when nothing is accepted). Files: `submission/syn_reports/400/experiments/`.\r\n- Area: 2337.9 \u00b5m\u00b2, against 2386.6 \u00b5m\u00b2 with isolation.\r\n- Power: whole run 1402.0 \u00b5W (+118 %), fill window 1471.1 \u00b5W, drain window 428.6 \u00b5W. The windows hardly change because the checker keeps the producer quiet in the drain window. Over the whole run, the random operands presented while not ready (F5/F11 stimulus) toggle the multiplier without isolation.\r\n- Vectorless estimate: 755.9 \u00b5W.\r\n- Isolation costs about 49 \u00b5m\u00b2 of gating and removes about 54 % of the whole-run power.\r\n\r\nGlitch power is not included, because the VCD is from the zero-delay simulation that SPEC Section 7 prescribes for `sim`. This is noted in the report.\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 5: report\r\n\r\n**Report** (`submission/pdf_report/report.pdf`). Built by `bash submission/scripts/build_report.sh`: pandoc 3.1.3 + pdflatex from `submission/pdf_report/src/report.md`. The script fills four placeholders:\r\n- the sign-off section, from `src/signoff.md`;\r\n- the token table, from `submission/scripts/token_usage.py`;\r\n- the end time;\r\n- the full source listing appendix.\r\n\r\nFigures: Graphviz state and datapath diagrams (`src/*.dot`) and the GTKWave captures. The report is marked AI-generated on its first page, with author Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic).\r\n\r\n**Token usage** (`submission/scripts/token_usage.py`). It reads every transcript under `~/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/`: the main session and the 3 subagents. Each API response is counted once (deduplicated by message id and request id), and costs use Anthropic API prices for Claude Opus 5.5:\r\n- $4 / $20 per MTok input / output;\r\n- cache reads $0.20;\r\n- cache writes 1.25\u00d7 input (5 min) or 2\u00d7 input (1 h).\r\n\r\nAt the first measurement (03:40) the total was 279 responses and $24.72. The final numbers are in the report.\r\n\r\n**Sign-off service.** `check/400` (60ed005) and `check/800` (b6917e9) were pushed at about 03:02 and 03:27. Repeated `git fetch origin check-results` returned \"couldn't find remote ref\", and `git ls-remote` shows no such branch, so no scorecard was available while the report was being built. The report states this and lists the differences to expect.\r\n\r\n**Fresh-clone rerun.** The script is in the scratchpad (`fresh.sh`). It clones the pushed branch, runs `install.sh`, `make synth check sim timing power f14` for both RUNs, `make timing_fail` for both, and the mutation tests, then reports `git status` and diffs the netlists against the committed ones. The result is recorded below.\r\n\r\n**Fresh-clone rerun result** (`submission/scripts/fresh_clone_rerun.sh`, log `submission/syn_reports/fresh_clone_rerun.log`).\r\n- *Run:* the clone of 8f205c3 ran from 03:34:16 to 03:36:14, with install.sh and the Docker images already cached.\r\n- *Both RUNs reproduce the committed results exactly:*\r\n  - 400 MHz: +0.152 ns, 2386.552 \u00b5m\u00b2, power 652.53 / 642.80 / 1480.10 / 430.37 \u00b5W;\r\n  - 800 MHz: +0.075 ns, 4755.016 \u00b5m\u00b2, 2727.60 / 3073.10 / 5209.50 / 2535.60 \u00b5W;\r\n  - check, sim and timing all ALL PASS; F14 166/166 and 577/577; timing_fail TIMING FAIL for both; mutants 11/11 and 13/13.\r\n- *`git status` after the run:* only logs changed (synth.log, resize.log and the tool_versions.txt date). Netlists, SDF and reports are byte-identical.\r\n\r\n## Report revision after sign-off (07:00\u201307:15 UTC)\r\n\r\n**Sign-off scorecards** (`git fetch origin check-results`, `results/check_{400-60ed005585,800-b6917e9eb1}/scorecard.md`).\r\n- *Correction:* the user reports that the service was online throughout the session. It did not trigger because the session environment had not been set up for it. The report's earlier wording (\"probably offline\") was wrong and has been corrected.\r\n- *Checked:* both commits at 06:37 / 06:48 UTC, after the environment fix.\r\n- *GPDK045 results:*\r\n\r\n  | | 400 MHz | 800 MHz |\r\n  |---|---|---|\r\n  | WNS (target) | 156 ps (125) | 148 ps (62) |\r\n  | Area | 2752.1 \u00b5m\u00b2 | 5674.5 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n  | Vectorless power | 224.6 \u00b5W | 1121.9 \u00b5W |\r\n  | SDF simulation | pass, 1204/1204 products, 0 timing-check messages | pass, 1249/1249 products |\r\n\r\n  Informational check: the 400 MHz netlist at 1.25 ns fails, with 0 products, 4058 timing-check messages, and F1 F4 F5 F6 F8 F9 STALL violated. This matches our own `make timing_fail RUN=800` (same netlist, same period, no product returned).\r\n- *Comparison with the open-source results:*\r\n  - functional results agree;\r\n  - GPDK045 area is 15\u201319 % larger;\r\n  - GPDK045 vectorless power is 2.4\u20132.9\u00d7 lower (different library, voltage and default activity);\r\n  - the 800 MHz design draws 4.2\u00d7 the power of the 400 MHz design in our flow and 5.0\u00d7 in GPDK045;\r\n  - 400 MHz slack is nearly equal in both flows; at 800 MHz GPDK045 has 2\u00d7 the margin (corner not stated; commercial tools spend slack on area recovery).\r\n\r\n**Report rewritten for concision.** The user asked for a results summary first, then design decisions, at about half the length. Main-text prose went from 5,650 to 2,728 words (3,805 with tables), and all ten SPEC Section 9 items are kept. Section order:\r\n1. summary;\r\n2. design decisions (control, arithmetic, 400 MHz, 800 MHz with change table and candidates);\r\n3. verification;\r\n4. area/power;\r\n5. optimisation;\r\n6. tool flow and departures;\r\n7. GPDK045 comparison;\r\n8. metrics;\r\n9. references, with the appendix after them.\r\n\r\nRTL untouched.\r\n\r\n**Build fixes.**\r\n- The first rebuild failed silently. LaTeX could not render \"\u2248\" (U+2248), and `| tail -1` hid the error, so the old PDF stayed in place. \"\u2248\" and \"\u2026\" are now declared in the header.\r\n- `token_usage.py` now labels subagents by their task description from `*.meta.json` and states the model once.\r\n82a3a02 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i\r\ne1b93d2 Judge area and power on the sign-off results; allow candidate checks\r\n87b9178 Report revision: GPDK045 sign-off comparison, concise results-first structure, token usage update\r\n032bfb2 Checkpoint 5: final report, fresh-clone rerun log, token usage\r\n6dc9335 Checkpoint 5: report text fixes, work-log entry for the report\r\n# ranks.tcl -- flop count and worst setup slack at D per register group (Q-net name). env: LIB NETLIST PERIOD\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\narray set w {}; array set n {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n  if {![string match DFF* [get_property $inst ref_name]]} continue\r\n  set in [get_full_name $inst]\r\n  set q [get_full_name [get_nets -of_objects [get_pins $in/Q]]]\r\n  regsub {\\s*\\[[0-9]+\\]\\s*$} $q \"\" g\r\n  set s [get_property [get_pins $in/D] slack_max]\r\n  if {![info exists w($g)] || $s < $w($g)} { set w($g) $s }\r\n  if {[info exists n($g)]} { incr n($g) } else { set n($g) 1 }\r\n}\r\nforeach g [lsort [array names w]] { puts [format \"%-36s %4d %8.3f\" $g $n($g) $w($g)] }\r\n"]
[19684.785, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m docker run --rm -v $PWD:$PWD -w $PWD -e LIB=tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib -e NETLIST=submission/outputs/mkMultBuff_400_map.v -e PERIOD=2.5 --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a -no_init -no_splash -exit submission/scripts/ranks.tcl 2>&1 | grep -v Warning | awk '{printf \"%s:%s:%s  \", $1,$2,$3} END{print \"\"}'; \r\nmk400() { # name PRE CSA\r\n  d=build/cand400/$1; mkdir -p $d/rtl; cp submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv $d/rtl/; sed \"s/localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;/localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b$2;/; s/localparam bit \\[3:0\\] CSA_REG   = 4'b0100;/localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b$3;/\" submission/rtl_400/mkMultBuff.sv > $d/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv; grep -c \"PRE_ENC   = 1'b$2\\|CSA_REG   = 4'b$3\" $d/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv; }\r\nmk400 p1c4 1 1000; mk400 p0c4 0 1000; mk400 p1c2 1 0100\r\nEN_writeMem:1:1.624  RDY_blockRead:1:0.709  RDY_mult:1:0.928  VALID_memVal:1:1.373  acc_q:6:0.921  readMem_addr:6:0.591  u_mult.a17:16:0.921  u_mult.g_pre.neg_q:8:1.184  u_mult.g_pre.one_q:8:1.131  u_mult.g_pre.two_q:8:1.133  u_mult.l3q:76:0.152  v_q:2:1.071  writeMem_val:32:0.220  \r\n2\r\n2\r\n2\r\n"]
[19746.806, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m export ABC_DRIVER=BUF_X1 ABC_LOAD=1.0 DONT_USE=\"OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_* MUX2_*\"; for n in p1c2 p1c4 p0c4; do bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 400 build/cand400/$n/rtl build/cand400/$n 2>&1 | sed -n 2,4p; done\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.224 whs=0.061\r\narea=2547.482 seq=750.652 comb=1796.8 flops=166 vectorless_uW=664.5\r\nactivity_uW: run:=677.48 fill:=1565.50 drain:=434.11 \r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.207 whs=0.061\r\narea=2517.956 seq=673.778 comb=1844.2 flops=149 vectorless_uW=663.2\r\nactivity_uW: run:=659.06 fill:=1606.50 drain:=398.46 \r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.110 whs=0.064\r\narea=3165.134 seq=637.602 comb=2527.5 flops=141 vectorless_uW=746.9\r\nactivity_uW: run:=765.03 fill:=2084.30 drain:=394.33\r\n"]
[19747.904, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m ls build/exp | head -50; ls build/cand | head; grep -n \"ABC\\|DONT_USE\\|800\" Makefile | head -40; nproc; uptime\r\nabc_p.script\r\ne800a\r\ne800b\r\ne800c\r\nf400\r\nf800b\r\nft\r\ng400\r\ng800b\r\ngroups.tcl\r\nh800a\r\ni800a\r\ni800b\r\ni800c\r\nj400\r\nj800a\r\nk400\r\nk400b\r\nk800a\r\nlib_du0.lib\r\nlib_du1.lib\r\nlib_du2.lib\r\nlib_du3.lib\r\nm.vvp\r\nm800a\r\nm800b\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\nn800b\r\nn800c\r\no800b\r\no800c\r\np400\r\np400a\r\np400b\r\np400c\r\np800b\r\npath.sh\r\nq400a\r\nq400b\r\nq400c\r\nq400d\r\nq800b\r\nq800c\r\nr400_1500\r\nr400_1800\r\nr400_2300\r\nr800b\r\nr800c\r\nranks.tcl\r\nrsz.tcl\r\nbase800\r\n2:# Usage: make <synth|check|sim|timing|power|all> RUN=<400|800>\r\n9:  ABC_D   ?= 2200\r\n12:  # ABC mapping knobs (see notes/WORKLOG.md): no input-driver model, the SPEC\r\n13:  # output load on every ABC output, full cell library\r\n14:  ABC_DRIVER ?= none\r\n15:  ABC_LOAD   ?= 23.5\r\n16:  DONT_USE   ?=\r\n17:else ifeq ($(RUN),800)\r\n20:  ABC_D   ?= 1050\r\n23:  # ABC mapping knobs: BUF_X1 input driver, 1 fF load (ABC outputs are mostly\r\n26:  ABC_DRIVER ?= BUF_X1\r\n27:  ABC_LOAD   ?= 1.0\r\n28:  DONT_USE   ?= OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_* MUX2_*\r\n30:  $(error RUN must be 400 or 800)\r\n51:YOSYS       := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e RTL_DIR=$(RTL_DIR) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e ABC_D=$(ABC_D) -e BOOTH=$(BOOTH) -e ADDER=$(ADDER) -e OUT=$(BUILD)/syn.v \\\r\n52:               -e ABC_DRIVER=$(ABC_DRIVER) -e ABC_LOAD=$(ABC_LOAD) -e MAPLIB=$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),$(BUILD)/maplib.lib,) \\\r\n67:\t$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),python3 submission/scripts/lib_dont_use.py $(LIB) $(BUILD)/maplib.lib $(foreach c,$(DONT_USE),'$(c)'),)\r\n109:#  RUN=800: the 400 MHz netlist, timed by STA and back-annotated at 1.25 ns\r\n118:\t$(MAKE) sta_only RUN=800 BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n4\r\n 08:02:45 up 11 min,  0 user,  load average: 0.59, 0.23, 0.08\r\n"]
[19752.854, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 1,60p Makefile; ls submission/scripts/; cat submission/scripts/synth.tcl 2>/dev/null | head -60 || ls submission/scripts/*.ys\r\n# Makefile -- open-source flow for mkMultBuff (SPEC.md Section 7).\r\n# Usage: make <synth|check|sim|timing|power|all> RUN=<400|800>\r\n# Toolchain: bash submission/scripts/install.sh\r\n\r\nRUN      ?= 400\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 2.5\r\n  HALF    := 1.25\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 2200\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\n  # ABC mapping knobs (see notes/WORKLOG.md): no input-driver model, the SPEC\r\n  # output load on every ABC output, full cell library\r\n  ABC_DRIVER ?= none\r\n  ABC_LOAD   ?= 23.5\r\n  DONT_USE   ?=\r\nelse ifeq ($(RUN),800)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 1.25\r\n  HALF    := 0.625\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 1050\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\n  # ABC mapping knobs: BUF_X1 input driver, 1 fF load (ABC outputs are mostly\r\n  # flip-flop D pins), and no cells with 3- or 4-high stacks or MUX2 (slow at\r\n  # the slow corner) during mapping\r\n  ABC_DRIVER ?= BUF_X1\r\n  ABC_LOAD   ?= 1.0\r\n  DONT_USE   ?= OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_* MUX2_*\r\nelse\r\n  $(error RUN must be 400 or 800)\r\nendif\r\n\r\nROOT     := $(CURDIR)\r\nLIB      := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib\r\nCELLS    := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary.v\r\nRTL_DIR  ?= submission/rtl_$(RUN)\r\nRTL      := $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv)\r\nMEM      := starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv starter/rtl/registerArray.sv\r\nTB       := submission/testbench\r\nOUT      := submission/outputs\r\nREP      ?= submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)\r\nBUILD    ?= build/$(RUN)\r\nNETLIST  ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.v\r\nSDF      ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.sdf\r\nSEED     ?= 402\r\nSETUP_MARGIN ?= 0.15\r\n\r\nYOSYS_IMAGE := openroad/orfs@sha256:d3505fd5f930fcd20d3d25a41f3047230b7db7b7797e3448561c9e556cca3774\r\nSTA_IMAGE   := openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a\r\nDOCKER      := docker run --rm -v $(ROOT):$(ROOT) -w $(ROOT)\r\nYOSYS       := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e RTL_DIR=$(RTL_DIR) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e ABC_D=$(ABC_D) -e BOOTH=$(BOOTH) -e ADDER=$(ADDER) -e OUT=$(BUILD)/syn.v \\\r\n               -e ABC_DRIVER=$(ABC_DRIVER) -e ABC_LOAD=$(ABC_LOAD) -e MAPLIB=$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),$(BUILD)/maplib.lib,) \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/yosys\r\nOPENROAD    := $(DOCKER) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST_IN=$(BUILD)/syn.v -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               -e SETUP_MARGIN=$(SETUP_MARGIN) -e PDK_LEF_DIR=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/nangate45/lef \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/OpenROAD/bin/openroad -no_init -exit\r\nSTA         := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e SDF=$(SDF) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta $(STA_IMAGE) -no_init -no_splash -exit\r\n\r\n.PHONY: synth check sim timing power all clean timing_fail sta_only f14\r\nabc_speed.script\r\nbuild_report.sh\r\nconstraints.tcl\r\neval_candidate.sh\r\nf14_check.sh\r\nf14_check.tcl\r\nfresh_clone_rerun.sh\r\ninstall.sh\r\nlib_dont_use.py\r\nmutate.sh\r\npower.sh\r\npower.tcl\r\npower_summary.py\r\nranks.tcl\r\nresize.tcl\r\nsdf_typmax.py\r\nsta.tcl\r\nsynth.tcl\r\ntoken_usage.py\r\nwaves\r\n# synth.tcl -- Yosys synthesis of submission/rtl_$RUN to Nangate45 (slow corner).\r\n# Invoked by the Makefile:  yosys -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl  with env\r\n#   RUN      400 | 800\r\n#   LIB      Liberty file (Nangate45 slow corner)\r\n#   ABC_D    ABC delay target in ps (may be shorter than the clock period)\r\n#   BOOTH    1 to let Yosys build a radix-4 Booth multiplier for '*'\r\n#   OUT      netlist path\r\nyosys -import\r\nset run   $::env(RUN)\r\nset lib   $::env(LIB)\r\nset abc_d $::env(ABC_D)\r\nset booth [expr {[info exists ::env(BOOTH)] ? $::env(BOOTH) : 0}]\r\nset out   $::env(OUT)\r\n# library used by ABC for mapping (may mark slow cells dont_use); everything\r\n# else (flip-flop mapping, area report) uses the original library\r\nset maplib [expr {[info exists ::env(MAPLIB)] && $::env(MAPLIB) ne \"\" ? $::env(MAPLIB) : $lib}]\r\n# final-adder architecture for $lcu (carry look-ahead unit): a Yosys parallel-prefix choice\r\nset adder [expr {[info exists ::env(ADDER)] ? $::env(ADDER) : \"sklansky\"}]\r\nset extra {}\r\nif {$adder ne \"ripple\"} { set extra [list -extra-map +/choices/${adder}.v] }\r\n\r\nread_liberty -lib $lib\r\n# read every .sv file of the source directory, in any order (SPEC Section 5)\r\nset rtl_dir [expr {[info exists ::env(RTL_DIR)] ? $::env(RTL_DIR) : \"submission/rtl_${run}\"}]\r\nforeach f [lsort [glob ${rtl_dir}/*.sv]] { read_verilog -sv $f }\r\nhierarchy -check -top mkMultBuff\r\nset sargs [list -top mkMultBuff -flatten {*}$extra]\r\nif {$booth} { lappend sargs -booth }\r\nsynth {*}$sargs\r\nopt -full\r\n# sequential mapping: Nangate has no synchronous-reset flop, so the reset is a\r\n# gate in front of D (dfflegalize keeps it synchronous)\r\ndfflibmap -liberty $lib\r\nopt\r\n# ABC: delay-oriented mapping followed by buffering and gate sizing; the\r\n# constraint file gives ABC the input drive and the output load of SPEC Section 6\r\nset cf [open [file rootname $out].abc.constr w]\r\nset drv  [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_DRIVER)] ? $::env(ABC_DRIVER) : \"BUF_X1\"}]\r\nset load [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_LOAD)] ? $::env(ABC_LOAD) : 1.0}]\r\nif {$drv ne \"\" && $drv ne \"none\"} { puts $cf \"set_driving_cell $drv\" }\r\nputs $cf \"set_load $load\"\r\nclose $cf\r\nset abc_script [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_SCRIPT)] ? $::env(ABC_SCRIPT) : \"submission/scripts/abc_speed.script\"}]\r\nif {$abc_script eq \"default\"} {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $maplib -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n} else {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $maplib -script $abc_script -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n}\r\nfile delete [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\nopt_clean\r\nsetundef -zero\r\nhilomap -singleton -hicell LOGIC1_X1 Z -locell LOGIC0_X1 Z\r\nopt_clean -purge\r\ncheck -assert\r\ntee -o [file rootname $out].stat.rpt stat -liberty $lib\r\nwrite_verilog -noattr -noexpr -nohex -nodec $out\r\n"]
[19761.618, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m for n in p1c4 p0c4; do cp -r build/cand400/$n/rtl build/cand400/${n}k; done; mv build/cand400/p1c4k build/cand400/p1c4_k4 2>/dev/null; mv build/cand400/p0c4k build/cand400/p0c4_k4; mkdir -p build/cand400/p1c4_k4/rtl; for n in p1c4_k4 p0c4_k4; do bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 400 build/cand400/$n/rtl build/cand400/$n 2>&1 | sed -n 2,4p; done\r\nawk: cannot open \"build/cand400/p1c4_k4/rep/sta.rpt\" (No such file or directory)\r\ngrep: build/cand400/p1c4_k4/rep/sta.rpt: No such file or directory\r\nawk: cannot open \"build/cand400/p1c4_k4/rep/sta.rpt\" (No such file or directory)\r\nawk: cannot open \"build/cand400/p0c4_k4/rep/sta.rpt\" (No such file or directory)\r\ngrep: build/cand400/p0c4_k4/rep/sta.rpt: No such file or directory\r\nawk: cannot open \"build/cand400/p0c4_k4/rep/sta.rpt\" (No such file or directory)\r\n"]
[19764.762, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m ls build/cand400/ build/cand400/p0c4_k4 build/cand400/p1c4_k4; tail -5 build/cand400/p0c4_k4/synth.out\r\nbuild/cand400/:\r\np0c4\r\np0c4_k4\r\np1c2\r\np1c4\r\np1c4_k4\r\n\r\nbuild/cand400/p0c4_k4:\r\ncheck.out\r\nmkMultBuff.sv\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\npower.out\r\nrep\r\nsim.out\r\nsynth.out\r\n\r\nbuild/cand400/p1c4_k4:\r\ncheck.out\r\nmkMultBuff.sv\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\npower.out\r\nrep\r\nrtl\r\nsim.out\r\nsynth.out\r\nERROR: TCL interpreter returned an error: no files matched glob pattern \"build/cand400/p0c4_k4/rtl/*.sv\"\r\nmake: *** [Makefile:68: synth] Error 1\r\n"]
[19777.926, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p build/cand800a/base/rtl && cp submission/rtl_800/*.sv build/cand800a/base/rtl/ && time bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 build/cand800a/base/rtl build/cand800a/base 2>&1 | tail -40\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].gg               3    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].gg               3    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].gg               3    0.339\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].pp_              3    0.253\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].G                1    0.422\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].P                1    0.336\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].gg               2    0.466\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].pp_              3    0.400\r\nu_mult.g_csel.psel                      8    0.370\r\nu_mult.g_csel.s0q                      24    0.203\r\nu_mult.g_csel.s1q                      24    0.150\r\nu_mult.g_pre.neg_q                      8    0.331\r\nu_mult.g_pre.one_q                      8    0.331\r\nu_mult.g_pre.two_q                      8    0.248\r\nu_mult.g_sel.negq                       8    0.376\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[0]                    17    0.164\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[1]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[2]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[3]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[4]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[5]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[6]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[7]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.l1q                            117    0.368\r\nu_mult.l3q                             76    0.075\r\nv_q                                     6    0.311\r\nwp_on                                   6    0.123\r\nwp_q                                    6    0.165\r\nwr                                      1    0.570\r\nwr_on                                   1    0.591\r\nwriteMem_val                           32    0.079\r\n\r\nreal\t0m20.891s\r\nuser\t0m4.409s\r\nsys\t0m0.300s\r\n"]
[19792.442, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 200,549p build/cand_dadda/gen2.py\r\n            if r is not None:\r\n                if found == mode:\r\n                    break\r\n                found += 1\r\n                r = None\r\n    nid[0] = save\r\n    return r\r\n\r\nmemo = {}\r\ndef search(cols, st, depth):\r\n    \"\"\"returns (total flops, [modes]) to finish the tree from stage st\"\"\"\r\n    budget = B1 if st == 1 else B\r\n    best = (10**9, None)\r\n    if depth > 7:\r\n        return best\r\n    if args.pg:\r\n        save = nid[0]\r\n        r = reduce_target(cols, st, budget - DX, 2)\r\n        nid[0] = save\r\n        if r is not None:\r\n            best = (2 * nbits(r[1]) // 2, [\"pg\"])\r\n    for mode in (\"g\", 0, 1):\r\n        r = try_mode(cols, st, budget, mode)\r\n        if r is None:\r\n            continue\r\n        out = r[1]\r\n        n = nbits(out)\r\n        if max(len(c) for c in out) <= 2 and not args.pg:\r\n            cand = (n, [mode])\r\n        else:\r\n            sub = search(reg0(out), st + 1, depth + 1)\r\n            cand = (n + sub[0], [mode] + (sub[1] or []))\r\n        if cand[0] < best[0]:\r\n            best = cand\r\n    return best\r\n\r\ndef register(items, st, comment):\r\n    \"\"\"items: list of (key, expr). registers non-constant exprs into vector r<st>.\r\n    returns dict key -> registered name (or the constant)\"\"\"\r\n    srcs = [(k, e) for (k, e) in items if e not in (ONE, ZERO)]\r\n    name = f\"r{st}\"\r\n    res = {}\r\n    if srcs:\r\n        decl.append(f\"    logic [{len(srcs)-1}:0] {name};\")\r\n    for i, (k, e) in enumerate(srcs):\r\n        res[k] = f\"{name}[{i}]\"\r\n    for (k, e) in items:\r\n        if e in (ONE, ZERO):\r\n            res[k] = e\r\n    ffs.append((st, comment, [(f\"{name}[{i}]\", e) for i, (k, e) in enumerate(srcs)], name, len(srcs)))\r\n    return res, len(srcs)\r\n\r\ndef reg_cols(cols, st):\r\n    items = []\r\n    for c in range(W):\r\n        for j, b in enumerate(cols[c]):\r\n            items.append(((c, j), b[0]))\r\n    res, n = register(items, st, \"carry-save bits\")\r\n    new_cols = [[(res[(c, j)], 0.0) for j in range(len(cols[c]))] for c in range(W)]\r\n    return new_cols, n\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n# stage 1: partial products\r\nA, Bv = ('a', 'b') if args.inlogic else ('a_q', 'b_q')\r\ncols = [[] for _ in range(W)]\r\nL = [\"    // ---- stage 1: Baugh-Wooley partial products pp_<i>_<j> = a[j] b[i] (NAND for the\"]\r\nL.append(\"    //      mixed sign-bit terms) and constants 2^16 + 2^31\")\r\nfor i in range(16):\r\n    for j in range(16):\r\n        n = f\"pp_{i}_{j}\"\r\n        if (i == 15) != (j == 15):\r\n            L.append(f\"    wire {n} = ~({A}[{j}] & {Bv}[{i}]);\")\r\n        else:\r\n            L.append(f\"    wire {n} = {A}[{j}] & {Bv}[{i}];\")\r\n        cols[i + j].append((n, args.t_and))\r\ncols[16].append((ONE, 0.0))\r\ncols[31].append((ONE, 0.0))\r\nbody.extend(L)\r\n\r\nsummary = []\r\nst = 1\r\nbudget = B1\r\npg = None   # per column (p, g_into_next) after the pg stage\r\nmodes = search(cols, 1, 0)[1] if args.plan else None\r\nprint(\"plan:\", modes)\r\nwhile True:\r\n    done = False\r\n    mode = modes[st - 1] if modes else None\r\n    if args.pg and (mode is None or mode == \"pg\"):\r\n        # try to finish the tree in this stage with room left for p/g\r\n        if mode == \"pg\":\r\n            Lt, out, nfa, nha = reduce_target(cols, st, budget - DX, 2)\r\n        else:\r\n            Lt, out, nfa, nha = reduce_best(cols, st, budget - DX)\r\n        if max(len(c) for c in out) <= 2:\r\n            body.append(f\"    // ---- stage {st}: carry-save reduction (last), then p = x ^ y, g = x & y\")\r\n            body.extend(Lt)\r\n            items = []\r\n            for c in range(W):\r\n                bs = [b[0] for b in out[c]] + [ZERO, ZERO]\r\n                x, y = bs[0], bs[1]\r\n                if ONE in (x, y):\r\n                    o = y if x == ONE else x\r\n                    if o == ONE:\r\n                        pe, ge = ZERO, ONE\r\n                    elif o == ZERO:\r\n                        pe, ge = ONE, ZERO\r\n                    else:\r\n                        pe, ge = f\"~{o}\", o\r\n                elif x == ZERO:\r\n                    pe, ge = y, ZERO\r\n                elif y == ZERO:\r\n                    pe, ge = x, ZERO\r\n                else:\r\n                    pn, gn = new(\"p_\"), new(\"g_\")\r\n                    body.append(f\"    wire {pn} = {x} ^ {y};\")\r\n                    body.append(f\"    wire {gn} = {x} & {y};\")\r\n                    pe, ge = pn, gn\r\n                items.append(((\"p\", c), pe))\r\n                if c + 1 < W:\r\n                    items.append(((\"g\", c), ge))\r\n            res, n = register(items, st, \"propagate / generate per column\")\r\n            pg = [(res[(\"p\", c)], res[(\"g\", c)] if c + 1 < W else ZERO) for c in range(W)]\r\n            summary.append(f\"stage {st}: {nfa} FA {nha} HA + p/g, {n} flops\")\r\n            st += 1\r\n            break\r\n    if mode is not None:\r\n        Lt, out, nfa, nha = try_mode(cols, st, budget, mode)\r\n    else:\r\n        Lt, out, nfa, nha = reduce_best(cols, st, budget)\r\n    body.append(f\"    // ---- stage {st}: carry-save reduction\")\r\n    body.extend(Lt)\r\n    hmax = max(len(c) for c in out)\r\n    cols, n = reg_cols(out, st)\r\n    summary.append(f\"stage {st}: {nfa} FA {nha} HA, max height {hmax}, {n} flops\")\r\n    st += 1\r\n    budget = B\r\n    if hmax <= 2 and not args.pg:\r\n        break\r\n    if st > 20:\r\n        sys.exit(\"no progress\")\r\n\r\nif pg is None:\r\n    # p/g from the two registered rows, inside C1\r\n    body.append(f\"    // ---- stage {st}: p = x ^ y, g = x & y per column\")\r\n    pg = []\r\n    for c in range(W):\r\n        bs = [b[0] for b in cols[c]] + [ZERO, ZERO]\r\n        x, y = bs[0], bs[1]\r\n        if x in (ONE, ZERO) or y in (ONE, ZERO):\r\n            if x == ZERO:\r\n                pg.append((y, ZERO))\r\n            elif y == ZERO:\r\n                pg.append((x, ZERO))\r\n            else:\r\n                o = y if x == ONE else x\r\n                pg.append((f\"~{o}\", o) if o not in (ONE, ZERO) else ((ZERO, ONE) if o == ONE else (ONE, ZERO)))\r\n        else:\r\n            pn, gn = new(\"p_\"), new(\"g_\")\r\n            body.append(f\"    wire {pn} = {x} ^ {y};\")\r\n            body.append(f\"    wire {gn} = {x} & {y};\")\r\n            pg.append((pn, gn))\r\npg = [(p, g if c + 1 < W else ZERO) for c, (p, g) in enumerate(pg)]\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n# CPA: lowest column with a possible carry into it starts block 0\r\n# columns below the first non-zero generate receive no carry: their sum is p\r\nlo = 0\r\nwhile lo < W and pg[lo][1] == ZERO:\r\n    lo += 1\r\n# columns 0..lo-1 are final (s = p); blocks start at lo\r\nK = args.k\r\nblocks = []\r\nc = lo\r\nwhile c < W:\r\n    blocks.append((c, min(c + K, W)))\r\n    c += K\r\nnb = len(blocks)\r\nsC1 = st\r\nbody.append(f\"    // ---- stage {sC1}: CPA part 1 -- per block of {K} bits: sum with carry-in 0 (s0),\")\r\nbody.append(\"    //      propagate prefix of each position (pp), block generate / propagate\")\r\n\r\ndef andp(a, b):\r\n    if ZERO in (a, b): return ZERO\r\n    if a == ONE: return b\r\n    if b == ONE: return a\r\n    n = new(\"ka_\"); body.append(f\"    wire {n} = {a} & {b};\"); return n\r\n\r\ndef orp(a, b):\r\n    if ONE in (a, b): return ONE\r\n    if a == ZERO: return b\r\n    if b == ZERO: return a\r\n    n = new(\"ko_\"); body.append(f\"    wire {n} = {a} | {b};\"); return n\r\n\r\ndef xorp(a, b):\r\n    if a == ZERO: return b\r\n    if b == ZERO: return a\r\n    if a == ONE: return f\"~{b}\" if b != ONE else ZERO\r\n    if b == ONE: return f\"~{a}\"\r\n    n = new(\"kx_\"); body.append(f\"    wire {n} = {a} ^ {b};\"); return n\r\n\r\ndef ks_prefix(G, P):\r\n    \"\"\"Kogge-Stone inclusive prefix: returns (Gpre, Ppre) with Gpre[i] = G[i:0]\"\"\"\r\n    G, P = list(G), list(P)\r\n    d = 1\r\n    while d < len(G):\r\n        G2, P2 = list(G), list(P)\r\n        for i in range(d, len(G)):\r\n            G2[i] = orp(G[i], andp(P[i], G[i - d]))\r\n            P2[i] = andp(P[i], P[i - d])\r\n        G, P = G2, P2\r\n        d *= 2\r\n    return G, P\r\n\r\nitems = []\r\nfor c in range(lo):\r\n    items.append(((\"f\", c), pg[c][0]))\r\nfor bi, (l, h) in enumerate(blocks):\r\n    gs = [pg[c][1] for c in range(l, h)]\r\n    ps = [pg[c][0] for c in range(l, h)]\r\n    Gp, Pp = ks_prefix(gs, ps)\r\n    for k, c in enumerate(range(l, h)):\r\n        s0 = ps[k] if k == 0 else xorp(ps[k], Gp[k - 1])\r\n        items.append(((\"s0\", c), s0))\r\n        if bi > 0 and k > 0:\r\n            items.append(((\"pp\", c), Pp[k - 1]))\r\n    if h < W:\r\n        items.append(((\"G\", bi), Gp[-1]))\r\n        if bi > 0:\r\n            items.append(((\"P\", bi), Pp[-1]))\r\nres1, n1 = register(items, sC1, \"CPA part 1: final low bits, block sums, prefixes, block G/P\")\r\nsummary.append(f\"stage {sC1}: CPA part 1, blocks {blocks}, {n1} flops\")\r\nst += 1\r\n\r\nsC2 = st\r\nbody.append(f\"    // ---- stage {sC2}: Kogge-Stone prefix over the {nb} blocks -> block carry-in\")\r\nGb = [res1.get((\"G\", j), ZERO) for j in range(nb)]\r\nPb = [ZERO] + [res1.get((\"P\", j), ZERO) for j in range(1, nb)]\r\nGc, _ = ks_prefix(Gb[:-1], Pb[:-1])\r\ncin = [ZERO] + Gc     # carry into block j\r\n\r\ndef select(cin_of, resx):\r\n    bits = []\r\n    for c in range(lo):\r\n        bits.append(resx[(\"f\", c)])\r\n    for bi, (l, h) in enumerate(blocks):\r\n        for k, c in enumerate(range(l, h)):\r\n            s0 = resx[(\"s0\", c)]\r\n            if bi == 0:\r\n                bits.append(s0)\r\n            elif k == 0:\r\n                bits.append(xorp(s0, cin_of[bi]))\r\n            else:\r\n                bits.append(xorp(s0, andp(cin_of[bi], resx[(\"pp\", c)])))\r\n    return bits\r\n\r\nif args.cpa3:\r\n    items = []\r\n    for c in range(lo):\r\n        items.append(((\"f\", c), res1[(\"f\", c)]))\r\n    for bi, (l, h) in enumerate(blocks):\r\n        for k, c in enumerate(range(l, h)):\r\n            items.append(((\"s0\", c), res1[(\"s0\", c)]))\r\n            if bi > 0 and k > 0:\r\n                items.append(((\"pp\", c), res1[(\"pp\", c)]))\r\n        if bi > 0:\r\n            items.append(((\"cin\", bi), cin[bi]))\r\n    res2, n2 = register(items, sC2, \"CPA part 2: block carries, delayed block sums\")\r\n    summary.append(f\"stage {sC2}: CPA part 2 (block prefix), {n2} flops\")\r\n    st += 1\r\n    body.append(f\"    // ---- stage {st}: block selection s = s0 ^ (cin & pp)\")\r\n    pbits = select([ZERO] + [res2[(\"cin\", j)] for j in range(1, nb)], res2)\r\nelse:\r\n    body.append(f\"    //      and block selection s = s0 ^ (cin & pp)\")\r\n    pbits = select(cin, res1)\r\nbody.append(\"    assign prod = {\" + \", \".join(reversed(pbits)) + \"};\")\r\nsummary.append(f\"stage {st}: selection\" + (\"\" if args.outcomb else \", product register 32 flops\"))\r\nLAT = (0 if args.inlogic else 1) + st - (1 if args.outcomb else 0)\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nout_dir = os.path.join(args.outdir, \"rtl\")\r\nos.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\r\nnff = (0 if args.inlogic else 32) + sum(f[4] for f in ffs) + (0 if args.outcomb else 32)\r\no = []\r\no.append(\"// mult_tree.sv -- GENERATED by build/cand_dadda/gen2.py; edit the generator, not this file.\")\r\no.append(f\"// generator arguments: {' '.join(sys.argv[2:])}\")\r\no.append(\"//\")\r\no.append(\"// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier: Baugh-Wooley partial products, timing-driven\")\r\no.append(\"// column-wise carry-save (full / half adder) reduction with hand-placed pipeline\")\r\no.append(\"// registers, and a pipelined carry-select final adder. Register ranks (latency\")\r\no.append(f\"// from 'en' to 'p'): {LAT}; datapath flip-flops: {nff}.\")\r\nif args.inlogic:\r\n    o.append(\"//   no operand register: stage 1 starts at the inputs; the stage-1 register loads\")\r\n    o.append(\"//   zeros when en = 0 (operand isolation)\")\r\nelse:\r\n    o.append(\"//   operand register a_q, b_q: 32 flops (zeros when en = 0: operand isolation)\")\r\nfor s in summary:\r\n    o.append(\"//   \" + s)\r\no.append(\"// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (SPEC F14).\")\r\no.append(\"module mult_tree (\")\r\no.append(\"    input  logic               clk,\")\r\no.append(\"    input  logic               RST_N,\")\r\no.append(\"    input  logic               en,     // accept: load operands, else load zeros\")\r\no.append(\"    input  logic signed [15:0] a,      // multiplicand\")\r\no.append(\"    input  logic signed [15:0] b,      // multiplier\")\r\no.append(\"    output logic signed [31:0] p       // product, registered\")\r\no.append(\");\")\r\nif not args.inlogic:\r\n    o.append(\"    logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\")\r\no.extend(decl)\r\no.append(\"    logic [31:0] prod;\")\r\no.append(\"\")\r\nif not args.inlogic:\r\n    o.append(\"    // ---- operand register\")\r\n    o.append(\"    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\")\r\n    o.append(\"        if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\")\r\n    o.append(\"        else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\")\r\n    o.append(\"    end\")\r\no.append(\"\")\r\n# interleave: body lines are in stage order; append register blocks at the end per stage\r\no.extend(body)\r\no.append(\"\")\r\nfor (s, comment, pairs, name, n) in ffs:\r\n    if not n:\r\n        continue\r\n    o.append(f\"    // stage {s} register: {comment} ({n} bits)\")\r\n    o.append(\"    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\")\r\n    rst = \"!RST_N || !en\" if (args.inlogic and s == 1) else \"!RST_N\"\r\n    o.append(f\"        if ({rst}) {name} <= '0;\")\r\n    o.append(\"        else begin\")\r\n    for (dst, src) in pairs:\r\n        o.append(f\"            {dst} <= {src};\")\r\n    o.append(\"        end\")\r\n    o.append(\"    end\")\r\nif args.outcomb:\r\n    o.append(\"    // no product register: the selection drives p (writeMem_val) directly\")\r\n    o.append(\"    assign p = prod;\")\r\nelse:\r\n    o.append(f\"    // stage {st} register: product\")\r\n    o.append(\"    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\")\r\n    o.append(\"        if (!RST_N) p <= '0;\")\r\n    o.append(\"        else        p <= prod;\")\r\n    o.append(\"    end\")\r\no.append(\"endmodule : mult_tree\")\r\nopen(os.path.join(out_dir, \"mult_tree.sv\"), \"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(o) + \"\\n\")\r\ntop = open(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), os.environ.get(\"TOP\", \"top3.sv.in\"))).read()\r\nopen(os.path.join(out_dir, \"mkMultBuff.sv\"), \"w\").write(top.replace(\"@LAT@\", str(LAT)))\r\nprint(f\"LAT={LAT} datapath flops={nff}\")\r\nfor s in summary:\r\n    print(\"  \" + s)\r\n"]
[19794.639, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m ls build/800 build/cand | head -50; find build -name ranks.rpt | head -30; nproc; uptime\r\nbuild/800:\r\ncheck.vvp\r\nf14\r\ngate.vcd\r\nmaplib.lib\r\nnetlist_sim.v\r\nsim.vvp\r\nsyn.v\r\ntiming.vvp\r\nwaves\r\n\r\nbuild/cand:\r\nbase800\r\nbuild/cand/base800/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nbuild/cand400/p1c4_k4/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nbuild/cand400/p1c4/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nbuild/cand400/p0c4_k4/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nbuild/cand400/p1c2/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nbuild/cand400/p0c4/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nbuild/cand800a/base/rep/ranks.rpt\r\n4\r\n 08:03:32 up 12 min,  0 user,  load average: 1.70, 0.56, 0.20\r\n"]
[19797.032, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat build/cand/base800/rep/ranks.rpt | grep -v ^Warning; cat submission/scripts/ranks.tcl; ls build/cand800a/ build/cand800a/base; cat build/cand800a/base/*.out 2>/dev/null | tail -5\r\nVALID_memVal                            1    0.465\r\nacc_q                                   6    0.152\r\nrdy_mult_on                             1    0.203\r\nrdy_mult_q                              1    0.243\r\nrdy_rd_on                               1    0.182\r\nrdy_rd_q                                1    0.203\r\nrp_on                                   6    0.229\r\nrp_q                                    6    0.149\r\nu_mult.a17                             16    0.222\r\nu_mult.g_csel.bg                        1    0.379\r\nu_mult.g_csel.co0q                      5    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.co1q                      5    0.211\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[0].P                1    0.570\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[0].pp_              3    0.411\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].G                1    0.543\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].P                1    0.411\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].gg               2    0.466\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].pp_              3    0.400\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].G                1    0.466\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].P                1    0.400\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].gg               3    0.340\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].pp_              3    0.258\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].G                1    0.449\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].P                1    0.362\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].gg               3    0.340\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].gg               3    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].gg               3    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[5].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].gg               3    0.339\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[6].pp_              3    0.253\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].G                1    0.422\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].P                1    0.336\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].gg               2    0.466\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[7].pp_              3    0.400\r\nu_mult.g_csel.psel                      8    0.370\r\nu_mult.g_csel.s0q                      24    0.203\r\nu_mult.g_csel.s1q                      24    0.150\r\nu_mult.g_pre.neg_q                      8    0.331\r\nu_mult.g_pre.one_q                      8    0.331\r\nu_mult.g_pre.two_q                      8    0.248\r\nu_mult.g_sel.negq                       8    0.376\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[0]                    17    0.164\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[1]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[2]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[3]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[4]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[5]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[6]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.g_sel.ppq[7]                    17    0.166\r\nu_mult.l1q                            117    0.368\r\nu_mult.l3q                             76    0.075\r\nv_q                                     6    0.311\r\nwp_on                                   6    0.123\r\nwp_q                                    6    0.165\r\nwr                                      1    0.570\r\nwr_on                                   1    0.591\r\nwriteMem_val                           32    0.079\r\n# ranks.tcl -- flop count and worst setup slack at D per register group (Q-net name). env: LIB NETLIST PERIOD\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\narray set w {}; array set n {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n  if {![string match DFF* [get_property $inst ref_name]]} continue\r\n  set in [get_full_name $inst]\r\n  set q [get_full_name [get_nets -of_objects [get_pins $in/Q]]]\r\n  regsub {\\s*\\[[0-9]+\\]\\s*$} $q \"\" g\r\n  set s [get_property [get_pins $in/D] slack_max]\r\n  if {![info exists w($g)] || $s < $w($g)} { set w($g) $s }\r\n  if {[info exists n($g)]} { incr n($g) } else { set n($g) 1 }\r\n}\r\nforeach g [lsort [array names w]] { puts [format \"%-36s %4d %8.3f\" $g $n($g) $w($g)] }\r\nbuild/cand800a/:\r\nbase\r\n\r\nbuild/cand800a/base:\r\ncheck.out\r\ncheck.vvp\r\ngate.vcd\r\nmap.sdf\r\nmap.v\r\nmaplib.lib\r\nnetlist_sim.v\r\npower.out\r\nrep\r\nrtl\r\nsim.out\r\nsim.vvp\r\nsyn.v\r\nsynth.out\r\nworst slack max 0.075\r\nworst slack min 0.041\r\ntns max 0.000\r\nTotal                2.4504e-03 2.1421e-04 6.3031e-05 2.7276e-03 100.0%\r\ncell area 4755.016 um^2 (sequential 2609.194 um^2, 2429 instances)\r\n"]
[19802.813, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m bash -c 'W=build/cand800a/base; head -5 <(bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 $W/rtl $W 2>&1)'; cat build/cand800a/base/rep/ranks.rpt | grep -v Warning | head -30; cat submission/scripts/sta.tcl | head -40\r\n== build/cand800a/base RUN=800\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.075 whs=0.041\r\narea=4755.016 seq=2609.194 comb=2145.8 flops=577 vectorless_uW=2727.6\r\nactivity_uW: run:=3073.10 fill:=5209.50 drain:=2535.60 \r\nper register group (flops, worst slack):\r\nVALID_memVal                            1    0.465\r\nacc_q                                   6    0.152\r\nrdy_mult_on                             1    0.203\r\nrdy_mult_q                              1    0.243\r\nrdy_rd_on                               1    0.182\r\nrdy_rd_q                                1    0.203\r\nrp_on                                   6    0.229\r\nrp_q                                    6    0.149\r\nu_mult.a17                             16    0.222\r\nu_mult.g_csel.bg                        1    0.379\r\nu_mult.g_csel.co0q                      5    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.co1q                      5    0.211\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[0].P                1    0.570\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[0].pp_              3    0.411\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].G                1    0.543\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].P                1    0.411\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].gg               2    0.466\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[1].pp_              3    0.400\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].G                1    0.466\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].P                1    0.400\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].gg               3    0.340\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[2].pp_              3    0.258\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].G                1    0.449\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].P                1    0.362\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].gg               3    0.340\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[3].pp_              3    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].G                1    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].P                1    0.254\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].gg               3    0.341\r\nu_mult.g_csel.g_blk[4].pp_              3    0.254\r\n# sta.tcl -- OpenSTA timing at the target period; writes the SDF for gate-level sim.\r\n# env: RUN, LIB, NETLIST, SDF, PERIOD (ns)\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nputs \"== constraints: period $period ns, clock/input transition [expr {$period/8.0}] ns, output load [expr {4.0*$c_nand}] fF\"\r\nreport_checks -path_delay max -group_path_count 3 -format full_clock_expanded \\\r\n    -fields {slew cap input_pins fanout} -digits 3\r\nreport_checks -path_delay min -format full_clock_expanded -fields {slew cap input_pins} -digits 3\r\nputs \"== summary\"\r\nreport_worst_slack -max -digits 3\r\nreport_worst_slack -min -digits 3\r\nreport_tns -digits 3\r\nreport_check_types -max_slew -max_capacitance -max_fanout -violators\r\nreport_power -digits 4\r\n# cell area of the final netlist, from the Liberty areas\r\nset area 0.0\r\narray set hist {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n    set lc [get_property $inst ref_name]\r\n    set a [get_property [get_lib_cells */$lc] area]\r\n    set area [expr {$area + $a}]\r\n    if {[info exists hist($lc)]} { incr hist($lc) } else { set hist($lc) 1 }\r\n}\r\nset seq 0.0\r\nforeach lc [lsort [array names hist]] {\r\n    set a [get_property [get_lib_cells */$lc] area]\r\n    if {[string match DFF* $lc]} { set seq [expr {$seq + $a * $hist($lc)}] }\r\n    puts [format \"cell %-14s %5d  %9.3f um^2\" $lc $hist($lc) [expr {$a * $hist($lc)}]]\r\n}\r\nputs [format \"cell area %.3f um^2 (sequential %.3f um^2, %d instances)\" $area $seq [llength [get_cells *]]]\r\nwrite_sdf -include_typ -digits 4 -no_timestamp $::env(SDF).sta\r\nputs \"SDF written to $::env(SDF)\"\r\n"]
[19806.306, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m awk '/^Startpoint/{n++} n==1' build/cand800a/base/rep/sta.rpt | head -80\r\nStartpoint: _4404_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nEndpoint: _4294_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nPath Group: clk\r\nPath Type: max\r\n\r\nFanout      Cap     Slew    Delay     Time   Description\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n                   0.156    0.000    0.000   clock clk (rise edge)\r\n                            0.000    0.000   clock network delay (ideal)\r\n                   0.156    0.000    0.000 ^ _4404_/CK (DFF_X1)\r\n     3    8.737    0.080    0.413    0.413 ^ _4404_/Q (DFF_X1)\r\n                   0.080    0.000    0.414 ^ _3888_/A (XOR2_X2)\r\n     1    4.317    0.091    0.192    0.606 ^ _3888_/Z (XOR2_X2)\r\n                   0.091    0.000    0.606 ^ _3889_/A (XNOR2_X2)\r\n     4   12.110    0.148    0.173    0.779 ^ _3889_/ZN (XNOR2_X2)\r\n                   0.148    0.000    0.779 ^ _4003_/A (XOR2_X2)\r\n     1    3.320    0.082    0.200    0.979 ^ _4003_/Z (XOR2_X2)\r\n                   0.082    0.000    0.979 ^ _4004_/B1 (OAI21_X2)\r\n     1    2.956    0.028    0.055    1.034 v _4004_/ZN (OAI21_X2)\r\n                   0.028    0.000    1.034 v _4005_/B1 (AOI21_X2)\r\n     1    1.419    0.063    0.079    1.113 ^ _4005_/ZN (AOI21_X2)\r\n                   0.063    0.000    1.113 ^ _4294_/D (DFF_X1)\r\n                                     1.113   data arrival time\r\n\r\n                   0.156    1.250    1.250   clock clk (rise edge)\r\n                            0.000    1.250   clock network delay (ideal)\r\n                            0.000    1.250   clock reconvergence pessimism\r\n                                     1.250 ^ _4294_/CK (DFF_X1)\r\n                           -0.063    1.187   library setup time\r\n                                     1.187   data required time\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n                                     1.187   data required time\r\n                                    -1.113   data arrival time\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n                                     0.075   slack (MET)\r\n"]
[19816.031, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m for n in p1c4_k4 p0c4_k4; do mkdir -p build/cand400/$n/rtl; mv build/cand400/$n/*.sv build/cand400/$n/rtl/; bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 400 build/cand400/$n/rtl build/cand400/$n 2>&1 | sed -n 2,4p; done\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-0.035 whs=0.055\r\narea=2341.066 seq=695.058 comb=1646.0 flops=149 vectorless_uW=635.5\r\nactivity_uW: run:=614.53 fill:=1465.30 drain:=393.45 \r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-0.269 whs=0.053\r\narea=3550.036 seq=651.966 comb=2898.1 flops=141 vectorless_uW=836.0\r\nactivity_uW: run:=845.16 fill:=2434.00 drain:=404.18\r\n"]
[19824.747, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m grep -n \"PRE_ENC\\|g_pre\\|g_post\\|a_q <= \\|always_ff @(posedge clk) begin$\" submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv | head -20; sed -n 55,75p submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv\r\n4://   PRE_ENC  : Booth-recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n5://   ENC_REG  : (PRE_ENC = 0 only) extra rank after the Booth recoding\r\n13:// Register ranks (= latency from 'en' to 'p'): 1 (operand) + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG)\r\n20:    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n52:    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\r\n56:        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n58:                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n60:                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n64:    end else begin : g_post\r\n67:        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n68:            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n69:            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n75:            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n228:        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n249:        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n259:        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_q, two_q, neg_q};\r\n    end else begin : g_post\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_d, two_d, neg_d;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {neg_d, two_d, one_d} = booth_enc(b_q);\r\n        if (ENC_REG) begin : g_enc\r\n            logic [7:0]  one_r, two_r, neg_r;\r\n            logic [15:0] a_r;\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n"]
[19884.15, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800a/src && cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800a/src && cp ../base/rtl/*.sv . && ls\r\nmkMultBuff.sv\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\n"]
[19887.866, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m d=build/cand400/r2c2; mkdir -p $d/rtl && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\nsrc='submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv'\r\ns=open(src).read()\r\ns=s.replace(\"    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\",\"    parameter bit       OPREG     = 1'b1,   // 0: no operand register (inputs gated by en feed the logic)\\n    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\")\r\ns=s.replace(\"    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\",\"\"\"    generate if (!OPREG) begin : g_noop\r\n        // no operand register: operand isolation by gating the inputs with en\r\n        wire [15:0] ag = en ? a : 16'd0;\r\n        wire [15:0] bg = en ? b : 16'd0;\r\n        assign a_e = ag;\r\n        assign {neg_e, two_e, one_e} = booth_enc(bg);\r\n    end else if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\"\"\")\r\nopen('build/cand400/r2c2/rtl/mult_pipe.sv','w').write(s)\r\nt=open('submission/rtl_400/mkMultBuff.sv').read()\r\nt=t.replace(\"localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\",\"localparam bit       OPREG     = 1'b0;\\n    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\")\r\nt=t.replace(\"localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC\",\"localparam int       LAT       = OPREG + (PRE_ENC\")\r\nt=t.replace(\"mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC),\",\"mult_pipe #(.OPREG(OPREG), .PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC),\")\r\nopen('build/cand400/r2c2/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv','w').write(t)\r\nEOF\r\ngrep -n \"OPREG\\|LAT  \" $d/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv | head; for c in 0100 0010; do n=r2c$c; mkdir -p build/cand400/$n/rtl; cp $d/rtl/mult_pipe.sv build/cand400/$n/rtl/; sed \"s/CSA_REG   = 4'b0100;/CSA_REG   = 4'b$c;/\" $d/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv > build/cand400/$n/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv; bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 400 build/cand400/$n/rtl build/cand400/$n 2>&1 | sed -n 2,4p; done\r\n42:    localparam bit       OPREG     = 1'b0;\r\n47:    localparam int       LAT       = OPREG + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n78:    mult_pipe #(.OPREG(OPREG), .PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-0.314 whs=0.055\r\narea=2736.608 seq=565.782 comb=2170.8 flops=125 vectorless_uW=800.0\r\nactivity_uW: run:=882.31 fill:=1628.80 drain:=348.98 \r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-1.100 whs=0.055\r\narea=2843.540 seq=628.558 comb=2215.0 flops=139 vectorless_uW=814.4\r\nactivity_uW: run:=991.47 fill:=1717.50 drain:=380.53\r\n"]
[19894.751, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m build/exp/path.sh build/cand400/r2c0100/rep/sta.rpt | sed -n '1,8p'; grep -B2 -A3 \"^Startpoint\" build/cand400/r2c0100/rep/sta.rpt | head -5; sort -k3 -n build/cand400/r2c0100/rep/ranks.rpt | head -4\r\nby clk) fo=Startpoint: d=port t=clocked\r\nby clk) fo=Endpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\nmult_input1[1] (in) fo=37 d=0.833 t=0.833\r\n_1979_/ZN (XNOR2_X1) fo=3 d=0.213 t=1.046\r\n_1980_/ZN (NOR2_X2) fo=6 d=0.292 t=1.338\r\n_2141_/ZN (AOI22_X1) fo=1 d=0.111 t=1.449\r\n_2142_/ZN (AOI21_X2) fo=3 d=0.201 t=1.650\r\n_2148_/ZN (NOR2_X1) fo=1 d=0.038 t=1.687\r\n== constraints: period 2.5 ns, clock/input transition 0.3125 ns, output load 23.536888 fF\r\nStartpoint: mult_input1[1] (input port clocked by clk)\r\nEndpoint: _3277_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nPath Group: clk\r\nPath Type: max\r\nu_mult.l3q                             76   -0.314\r\nwriteMem_val                           32   -0.155\r\nRDY_mult                                1    0.328\r\nacc_q                                   6    0.332\r\n"]
[19909.922, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sort -k3 -n build/cand400/p1c4/rep/ranks.rpt | grep -v Warn | awk '{printf \"%s:%s:%s  \", $1,$2,$3} END{print \"\"}'\r\nwriteMem_val:32:0.207  u_mult.l4q:59:0.268  readMem_addr:6:0.602  acc_q:6:0.802  RDY_mult:1:0.944  RDY_blockRead:1:0.989  u_mult.a17:16:1.070  v_q:2:1.162  u_mult.g_pre.two_q:8:1.174  u_mult.g_pre.neg_q:8:1.263  u_mult.g_pre.one_q:8:1.274  VALID_memVal:1:1.309  EN_writeMem:1:1.966\r\n"]
[19931.45, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800a/src && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\nsrc = open('mult_pipe.sv').read()\r\n# 1. header params\r\nsrc = src.replace(\"\"\"    parameter int       CSW       = 8,\r\n    parameter bit       GP4       = 1'b0\r\n) (\"\"\", \"\"\"    parameter int       CSW       = 8,\r\n    parameter bit       GP4       = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       GT        = 1'b0,  // with GP4: store generate / transmit (c|s) instead of propagate\r\n    parameter bit       ORD       = 1'b0,  // arrival-aware 3:2 input order\r\n    parameter int       CPA       = 0,     // 0: per CPA_CSEL/CPA_SPLIT, 1: 2-stage carry-increment, 2: 1-stage prefix, 3: 1-stage '+'\r\n    parameter int       PFX       = 0      // CPA=2: 0 Kogge-Stone, 1 Sklansky, 2 Brent-Kung, 3 Han-Carlson\r\n) (\"\"\")\r\n# 2. csa levels with ordering\r\nold_l = \"\"\"    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\"\"\"\r\nnew_l = \"\"\"    // csa3: z is the late input: sum = (x ^ y) ^ z, carry = x&y | z&(x|y)\r\n    function automatic logic [63:0] csa3(input logic [31:0] x, y, z);\r\n        logic [31:0] t;\r\n        t = x ^ y;\r\n        csa3 = {((x & y) | (z & (x | y))) << 1, t ^ z};\r\n    endfunction\r\n    // l1 = {c678, s678, c345, s345, c012, s012}\r\n    generate if (ORD) begin : g_ord\r\n        assign l2 = {csa3(l1q[5*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32]),    // c678, s678, s345\r\n                     csa3(l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[0*32 +: 32])};   // c012, c345, s012\r\n        // l2 = {cB, sB, cA, sA}; l3 = {sB, c3, s3}\r\n        assign l3 = {l2q[2*32 +: 32], csa3(l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[3*32 +: 32], l2q[0*32 +: 32])};\r\n    end else begin : g_nord\r\n    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    end endgenerate\"\"\"\r\nassert old_l in src; src = src.replace(old_l, new_l)\r\nold4 = \"\"\"    assign l4cs = csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n    assign l4 = GP4 ? {l4cs[63:32] & l4cs[31:0], l4cs[63:32] ^ l4cs[31:0]} : l4cs;\"\"\"\r\nnew4 = \"\"\"    assign l4cs = ORD ? csa3(l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32], l3q[0*32 +: 32])\r\n                      : csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n    assign l4 = !GP4 ? l4cs\r\n              : GT   ? {l4cs[63:32] & l4cs[31:0], l4cs[63:32] | l4cs[31:0]}\r\n              :        {l4cs[63:32] & l4cs[31:0], l4cs[63:32] ^ l4cs[31:0]};\"\"\"\r\nassert old4 in src; src = src.replace(old4, new4)\r\n# 3. adder: insert new modes before g_csel\r\nold_a = \"    generate if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\"\r\nnew_a = \"\"\"    // bitwise generate, carry-transmit (for the carry network) and propagate (for the sum)\r\n    logic [31:0] bg_, bt_, bp_;\r\n    assign bg_ = GP4 ? sy : (sx & sy);\r\n    assign bt_ = GP4 ? sx : (GT ? (sx | sy) : (sx ^ sy));\r\n    assign bp_ = GP4 ? (GT ? (sx & ~sy) : sx) : (sx ^ sy);\r\n\r\n    // 32-bit parallel-prefix carry network; returns group generate G[j] = bits j..0\r\n    function automatic logic [31:0] pfx32(input logic [31:0] g, input logic [31:0] p, input int kind);\r\n        logic [31:0] G, P;\r\n        int s;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        if (kind == 0) begin                       // Kogge-Stone\r\n            for (int d = 1; d < 32; d = 2 * d)\r\n                for (int j = 31; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                    G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]); P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n                end\r\n        end else if (kind == 1) begin              // Sklansky\r\n            for (int l = 0; l < 5; l++)\r\n                for (int j = 0; j < 32; j++)\r\n                    if ((j >> l) & 1) begin\r\n                        s = ((j >> (l + 1)) << (l + 1)) + (1 << l) - 1;\r\n                        G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[s]); P[j] = P[j] & P[s];\r\n                    end\r\n        end else if (kind == 2) begin              // Brent-Kung\r\n            for (int d = 1; d < 32; d = 2 * d)\r\n                for (int j = 2 * d - 1; j < 32; j = j + 2 * d) begin\r\n                    G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]); P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n                end\r\n            for (int d = 8; d >= 1; d = d / 2)\r\n                for (int j = 3 * d - 1; j < 32; j = j + 2 * d) begin\r\n                    G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]); P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n                end\r\n        end else begin                             // Han-Carlson\r\n            for (int j = 31; j >= 1; j = j - 2) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-1]); P[j] = P[j] & P[j-1];\r\n            end\r\n            for (int d = 2; d < 32; d = 2 * d)\r\n                for (int j = 31; j >= d + 1; j = j - 2) begin\r\n                    G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]); P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n                end\r\n            for (int j = 2; j < 32; j = j + 2) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-1]); P[j] = P[j] & P[j-1];\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        pfx32 = G;\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    generate if (CPA == 2) begin : g_pfx\r\n        logic [31:0] Gc;\r\n        assign Gc = pfx32(bg_, bt_, PFX);\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? (bp_ ^ {Gc[30:0], 1'b0}) : 32'd0;\r\n    end else if (CPA == 3) begin : g_beh\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? (sx + sy) : 32'd0;\r\n    end else if (CPA == 1) begin : g_cinc\r\n        // two-stage carry-increment adder: stage A gives each CSW-bit block's\r\n        // sum and carry-out for carry-in 0; stage B resolves the block carries\r\n        // (block propagate = block sum all ones) and increments the blocks\r\n        logic [31:0]   s0, s0q;\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] co0, co0q, bpq, cin;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_blk\r\n            logic [CSW-1:0] G, P;\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(bg_[CSW*i +: CSW], bt_[CSW*i +: CSW]);\r\n            assign s0[CSW*i +: CSW] = bp_[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ {G[CSW-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n            assign co0[i] = G[CSW-1];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin s0q <= '0; co0q <= '0; end\r\n            else        begin s0q <= s0; co0q <= co0; end\r\n        end\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] bgg;\r\n        logic [31:0]   inc;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_bp\r\n            assign bpq[i] = &s0q[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            for (genvar k = 0; k < CSW; k++) begin : g_k\r\n                if (k == 0) begin : g_k0\r\n                    assign inc[CSW*i] = 1'b1;\r\n                end else begin : g_kn\r\n                    assign inc[CSW*i + k] = &s0q[CSW*i +: k];\r\n                end\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign bgg = bprefix(co0q, bpq);\r\n        assign cin = {bgg[NB-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n        logic [31:0] psum;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_inc\r\n            assign psum[CSW*i +: CSW] = s0q[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ (inc[CSW*i +: CSW] & {CSW{cin[i]}});\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? psum : 32'd0;\r\n    end else if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\"\"\"\r\nassert old_a in src; src = src.replace(old_a, new_a)\r\n# csel uses gg/pp_ from GP; with GT the propagate for sums needs bp_. patch csel block to use bg_/bt_/bp_\r\nold_c = \"\"\"            if (GP4) begin : g_gp\r\n                assign gg  = sy[CSW*i +: CSW];        // generate (registered)\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW];        // propagate (registered)\r\n            end else begin : g_cs\r\n                assign gg  = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] & sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            end\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(gg, pp_);\"\"\"\r\nnew_c = \"\"\"            logic [CSW-1:0] tt;\r\n            assign gg  = bg_[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            assign tt  = bt_[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            assign pp_ = bp_[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(gg, tt);\"\"\"\r\nassert old_c in src; src = src.replace(old_c, new_c)\r\nopen('mult_pipe.sv','w').write(src)\r\nEOF\r\ngrep -n \"g_csel\\|end else if (CPA_SPLIT)\\|end endgenerate\" mult_pipe.sv | tail -5\r\n172:    end endgenerate\r\n190:    end endgenerate\r\n315:    end else if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\r\n350:    end else if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n369:    end endgenerate\r\n"]
[19945.015, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800a/src && sed -i 's/for (genvar k = 0; k < CSW; k++)/for (k = 0; k < CSW; k++)/; s/^    genvar i;$/    genvar i, k;/' mult_pipe.sv && grep -n \"genvar\" mult_pipe.sv && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\ns = open('mkMultBuff.sv').read()\r\nold = s[s.index(\"    localparam bit       PRE_ENC\"):s.index(\"    logic       rdy_mult_q\")]\r\nnew = \"\"\"    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1101;\r\n    localparam bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam int       CPA       = 0;\r\n    localparam int       PFX       = 0;\r\n    localparam int       CSW       = 4;\r\n    localparam bit       GP4       = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       GT        = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit       ORD       = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + SEL_REG + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n                                     + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3]\r\n                                     + ((CPA == 1 || (CPA == 0 && (CPA_SPLIT | CPA_CSEL))) ? 1 : 0) + 1;\r\n\r\n\"\"\"\r\ns = s.replace(old, new)\r\ns = s.replace(\".CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL), .CSW(4), .GP4(1'b1))\", \".CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL), .CSW(CSW), .GP4(GP4), .GT(GT), .ORD(ORD), .CPA(CPA), .PFX(PFX))\")\r\nopen('mkMultBuff.sv','w').write(s)\r\nEOF\r\ngrep -n \"u_mult\\|localparam\" mkMultBuff.sv\r\ncat > ../mk.sh <<'EOF'\r\n#!/bin/bash\r\n# mk.sh NAME KEY=VAL ... : create build/cand800a/NAME/rtl from src with localparams overridden, then evaluate\r\nset -e\r\ncd /home/user/elec402-p2-open\r\nN=$1; shift\r\nD=build/cand800a/$N\r\nmkdir -p $D/rtl\r\ncp build/cand800a/src/mult_pipe.sv $D/rtl/\r\ncp build/cand800a/src/mkMultBuff.sv $D/rtl/\r\nfor kv in \"$@\"; do k=${kv%%=*}; v=${kv#*=}\r\n  sed -i -E \"s/(localparam [a-z]+( \\[3:0\\])? +$k +=) [^;]*;/\\1 $v;/\" $D/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv\r\ndone\r\ngrep -E \"localparam\" $D/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv | grep -v LAT | tr -s ' ' | tr '\\n' ' '; echo\r\nbash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 $D/rtl $D > $D/summary.txt 2>&1\r\nhead -4 $D/summary.txt\r\nEOF\r\nchmod +x ../mk.sh\r\n88:    genvar i, k;\r\n48:    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n49:    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n50:    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1101;\r\n51:    localparam bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b1;\r\n52:    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n53:    localparam bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b1;\r\n54:    localparam int       CPA       = 0;\r\n55:    localparam int       PFX       = 0;\r\n56:    localparam int       CSW       = 4;\r\n57:    localparam bit       GP4       = 1'b1;\r\n58:    localparam bit       GT        = 1'b0;\r\n59:    localparam bit       ORD       = 1'b0;\r\n60:    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + SEL_REG + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n107:        u_mult (.clk(clk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n"]
[19957.087, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat > /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800a/rk.py <<'EOF'\r\nimport sys, re\r\n# summarise ranks.rpt per pipeline rank: flops, worst slack\r\nb = {}\r\norder = ['R1op','PP','L1','L2','L3','GP','ADD','PROD','CTRL']\r\nfor line in open(sys.argv[1]):\r\n    f = line.split()\r\n    if len(f) != 3 or line.startswith('Warning'): continue\r\n    g, n, s = f[0], int(f[1]), float(f[2])\r\n    if re.search(r'a17|g_pre|g_post|a_q|b_q|g_enc', g): k = 'R1op'\r\n    elif 'g_sel.' in g: k = 'PP'\r\n    elif 'l1q' in g: k = 'L1'\r\n    elif 'l2q' in g: k = 'L2'\r\n    elif 'l3q' in g: k = 'L3'\r\n    elif re.search(r'l4q|\\.gg|\\.pp_|\\.tt|\\]\\.G|\\]\\.P|bg_|bt_|bp_|\\.sx|\\.sy|g_blk', g): k = 'GP'\r\n    elif re.search(r's0q|s1q|co0q|co1q|g_csel\\.bg|bpq|bgg|\\.inc|g_cinc', g): k = 'ADD'\r\n    elif re.search(r'writeMem_val|psel|psum|u_mult\\.p\\b|Gc', g): k = 'PROD'\r\n    else: k = 'CTRL'\r\n    c = b.setdefault(k, [0, 9.9]); c[0] += n; c[1] = min(c[1], s)\r\nprint(' '.join(f\"{k}:{b[k][0]}({b[k][1]:.3f})\" for k in order if k in b))\r\nEOF\r\ncd /home/user/elec402-p2-open && python3 build/cand800a/rk.py build/cand800a/base/rep/ranks.rpt\r\nR1op:40(0.222) PP:144(0.164) L1:117(0.368) L3:76(0.075) GP:58(0.253) ADD:59(0.150) PROD:40(0.079) CTRL:43(0.123)\r\n"]
[19961.267, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m export ABC_DRIVER=BUF_X1 ABC_LOAD=1.0; for v in \"m25|OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_* MUX2_*|0.25\" \"du2|OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_*|0.15\"; do IFS='|' read -r tag du m <<< \"$v\"; n=p0c4_$tag; mkdir -p build/cand400/$n/rtl; cp build/cand400/p0c4/rtl/*.sv build/cand400/$n/rtl/; DONT_USE=\"$du\" SETUP_MARGIN=$m bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 400 build/cand400/$n/rtl build/cand400/$n 2>&1 | sed -n 2,3p; done\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.083 whs=0.064\r\narea=3320.478 seq=637.602 comb=2682.9 flops=141 vectorless_uW=782.2\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=0.073 whs=0.064\r\narea=3139.066 seq=637.602 comb=2501.5 flops=141 vectorless_uW=746.2\r\n"]
[19989.704, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m echo 'python3 build/cand800a/rk.py $D/rep/ranks.rpt | tee -a $D/summary.txt' >> build/cand800a/mk.sh && build/cand800a/mk.sh e1_ks1 CPA=2 PFX=0 GT=1\"'\"b1\r\n localparam bit PRE_ENC = 1'b1;  localparam bit ENC_REG = 1'b0;  localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG = 4'b1101;  localparam bit SEL_REG = 1'b1;  localparam bit CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;  localparam bit CPA_CSEL = 1'b1;  localparam int CPA = 2;  localparam int PFX = 0;  localparam int CSW = 4;  localparam bit GP4 = 1'b1;  localparam bit GT = 1'b1;  localparam bit ORD = 1'b0; \r\n== build/cand800a/e1_ks1 RUN=800\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-0.246 whs=0.020\r\narea=4348.568 seq=2306.220 comb=2042.3 flops=510 vectorless_uW=2432.4\r\nactivity_uW: run:=2755.50 fill:=4809.90 drain:=2246.50 \r\nR1op:40(0.154) PP:144(0.159) L1:117(0.309) L3:76(0.060) GP:59(0.327) PROD:32(-0.246) CTRL:42(0.054)\r\n"]
[19993.409, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m awk '/^Startpoint/{n++} n==1' build/cand800a/e1_ks1/rep/sta.rpt | grep -E \"\\^|v \" | head -30\r\n                   0.156    0.000    0.000 ^ _3917_/CK (DFF_X1)\r\n     3   11.957    0.106    0.439    0.439 ^ _3917_/Q (DFF_X1)\r\n                   0.106    0.000    0.439 ^ _2238_/A1 (NAND2_X2)\r\n     1    5.676    0.037    0.069    0.508 v _2238_/ZN (NAND2_X2)\r\n                   0.037    0.000    0.508 v _2240_/B1 (OAI21_X4)\r\n     4   14.742    0.103    0.145    0.653 ^ _2240_/ZN (OAI21_X4)\r\n                   0.103    0.000    0.653 ^ _2241_/B1 (AOI21_X4)\r\n     2    7.556    0.034    0.064    0.717 v _2241_/ZN (AOI21_X4)\r\n                   0.034    0.000    0.717 v _2242_/B1 (OAI21_X4)\r\n     2    7.833    0.074    0.109    0.827 ^ _2242_/ZN (OAI21_X4)\r\n                   0.074    0.000    0.827 ^ _2291_/A1 (AND2_X1)\r\n     2    4.536    0.049    0.138    0.964 ^ _2291_/ZN (AND2_X1)\r\n                   0.049    0.000    0.964 ^ _2292_/A2 (NAND2_X1)\r\n     2    4.744    0.031    0.062    1.027 v _2292_/ZN (NAND2_X1)\r\n                   0.031    0.000    1.027 v _2294_/B1 (OAI21_X2)\r\n     2    5.963    0.093    0.128    1.155 ^ _2294_/ZN (OAI21_X2)\r\n                   0.093    0.000    1.155 ^ _2295_/B1 (AOI21_X2)\r\n     1    2.399    0.029    0.055    1.210 v _2295_/ZN (AOI21_X2)\r\n                   0.029    0.000    1.210 v _2298_/A (XNOR2_X1)\r\n     1    1.802    0.027    0.124    1.334 v _2298_/ZN (XNOR2_X1)\r\n                   0.027    0.000    1.334 v _2299_/A2 (NOR2_X1)\r\n     1    1.419    0.059    0.101    1.435 ^ _2299_/ZN (NOR2_X1)\r\n                   0.059    0.000    1.435 ^ _4260_/D (DFF_X1)\r\n                                     1.250 ^ _4260_/CK (DFF_X1)\r\n"]
[20025.163, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 1,205p SPEC.md\r\n# mkMultBuff Design Specification\r\n\r\nPipelined signed 16 \u00d7 16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer\r\n\r\n## 1. Scope\r\n\r\nThis document specifies `mkMultBuff`, a pipelined multiplier for 16-bit two's-complement operands. Its 32-bit products are stored in an external 64-entry memory and returned to a consumer in the order in which they were produced. Two implementations of the same interface are required, one closing timing at 400 MHz and one at 800 MHz.\r\n\r\n## 2. Conventions\r\n\r\nAll registers are clocked on the rising edge of `clk`, and every cycle-level statement refers to signal values sampled at a rising edge. Requirements use \"shall\" and carry an identifier for traceability.\r\n\r\n| Term | Definition |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Accepted operand pair | Operands present in a cycle in which `EN_mult` = 1 and `RDY_mult` = 1 |\r\n| Accepted read | A read request in a cycle in which `EN_blockRead` = 1 and `RDY_blockRead` = 1 |\r\n| Fill phase | The interval from reset, or from the end of a drain phase, to the write of the 64th product |\r\n| Drain phase | The interval from the assertion of `RDY_blockRead` to the acceptance of the 64th read |\r\n| Latency | The number of cycles from the acceptance of an operand pair to the write of its product |\r\n\r\n## 3. Interface\r\n\r\nThe port list is fixed and defined in `starter/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv`, with N = 32.\r\n\r\n| Port | Direction | Width | Description |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `clk` | input | 1 | Clock |\r\n| `RST_N` | input | 1 | Synchronous reset, active low |\r\n| `EN_mult` | input | 1 | The producer presents a valid operand pair |\r\n| `mult_input0`, `mult_input1` | input | 16 | Operands, two's complement |\r\n| `RDY_mult` | output | 1 | The block can accept an operand pair |\r\n| `EN_blockRead` | input | 1 | The consumer requests a product |\r\n| `RDY_blockRead` | output | 1 | The block can accept a read |\r\n| `VALID_memVal` | output | 1 | `memVal_data` carries a product |\r\n| `memVal_data` | output | N | Product returned to the consumer |\r\n| `EN_writeMem` | output | 1 | Memory write enable |\r\n| `writeMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory write address |\r\n| `writeMem_val` | output | N | Memory write data |\r\n| `EN_readMem` | output | 1 | Memory read enable |\r\n| `readMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory read address |\r\n| `readMem_val` | input | N | Memory read data |\r\n\r\nThe memory, `starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv`, is a 64 \u00d7 N two-port array instantiated in the testbench. It is not part of `mkMultBuff` and is excluded from synthesis. A write stores `writeMem_val` at a rising edge at which `EN_writeMem` = 1. A read registers the addressed word at a rising edge at which `EN_readMem` = 1, so `readMem_val` is valid in the following cycle.\r\n\r\n## 4. Functional requirements\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Datapath\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F1 | Each accepted operand pair shall produce exactly one memory write, whose data is the 32-bit two's-complement product of `mult_input0` and `mult_input1`. |\r\n| F2 | Products shall be written in acceptance order to consecutive addresses, starting at address 0 in each fill phase. |\r\n| F3 | The multiplier shall be fully pipelined and sustain a throughput of one operand pair per cycle. |\r\n| F4 | The latency is implementation-defined. `EN_writeMem` shall be asserted only in cycles in which `writeMem_addr` and `writeMem_val` carry a valid address and product. |\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Fill\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F5 | `RDY_mult` shall be 1 if and only if no drain phase is in progress and fewer than 64 operand pairs have been accepted in the current fill phase. Operand pairs in flight therefore count against the capacity of the memory. `EN_mult` shall have no effect while `RDY_mult` is 0. |\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Transition to drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F6 | `RDY_blockRead` shall be asserted in the cycle following the write to address 63 and shall remain asserted until the 64th read is accepted. |\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F7 | In each cycle in which a read is accepted, `EN_readMem` shall be 1 and `readMem_addr` shall hold the next sequential address, starting at 0. |\r\n| F8 | `VALID_memVal` shall be 1 in, and only in, the cycle following each accepted read. In that cycle `memVal_data` shall equal `readMem_val`, which shall not be registered again inside `mkMultBuff`. |\r\n| F9 | `EN_blockRead` shall have no effect while `RDY_blockRead` is 0. |\r\n| F10 | In the cycle following the accepted read of address 63, `RDY_blockRead` shall be 0 and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. |\r\n\r\n### 4.5 Flow control and invariants\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F11 | The block shall operate correctly for any sequence of `EN_mult` and `EN_blockRead`. Deasserting either signal stalls the corresponding transfer without loss or duplication of data. |\r\n| F12 | `RDY_mult` and `RDY_blockRead` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n| F13 | `EN_writeMem` and `EN_readMem` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n\r\n### 4.6 Reset\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F14 | Every register shall have a synchronous, active-low reset driven by `RST_N`. |\r\n| F15 | In the cycle following a rising edge at which `RST_N` = 0, no product shall be in flight or stored and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. `EN_writeMem`, `writeMem_addr`, `RDY_blockRead`, `EN_readMem` and `VALID_memVal` shall be 0. |\r\n\r\nFigures 1 to 4 illustrate the phases of operation for an implementation with a latency of two cycles.\r\n\r\n![Figure 1. Fill phase](docs/fig/fill.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 2. Memory full and transition to drain](docs/fig/full.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 3. Drain phase](docs/fig/drain.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 4. End of drain phase](docs/fig/drain_end.svg)\r\n\r\n## 5. Implementation targets\r\n\r\n| Parameter | 400 MHz implementation | 800 MHz implementation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Source directory | `submission/rtl_400/` | `submission/rtl_800/` |\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns | 1.25 ns |\r\n| Pipeline stages | 2 minimum | Implementation-defined |\r\n| Worst slack, required | \u2265 0 ps | \u2265 0 ps |\r\n| Worst slack, target | \u2265 125 ps (5 % of period) | \u2265 62 ps (5 % of period) |\r\n| Cell area | < 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2 | < 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n| Power | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity |\r\n\r\nEach implementation shall have `mkMultBuff` as its top module and shall compile from the complete set of `.sv` files in its source directory, read in any order. `` `include`` directives shall not be used. The targets apply to the results of the open-source flow in Section 7, and the slack target shall also be met in the sign-off results of Section 8.3. The slack target leaves margin for physical implementation, and slack beyond it confers no further benefit. Among implementations that meet these targets, lower area and lower power are preferred, judged on the sign-off results, since these are comparable with designs from the course's standard flow.\r\n\r\n## 6. Technology and constraints\r\n\r\nThe open-source flow targets the Nangate45 Open Cell Library, which is built on the FreePDK45 process, at its slowest available corner. The install script written under Section 7 shall obtain the library from a public source, which the report shall identify together with the corner used. The library is not stored in this repository.\r\n\r\nFor comparison with designs built on the GPDK045 library, the sign-off service of Section 8.3 synthesizes the submitted RTL with GPDK045 and simulates the resulting netlists. Its results are reported alongside those of the open-source flow, not in place of them.\r\n\r\n| Constraint | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns or 1.25 ns |\r\n| Input delay, all inputs except `clk` | 0 ns |\r\n| Output delay, all outputs | 0 ns |\r\n| Input drive | Output of the smallest D flip-flop in the library |\r\n| Input transition | One eighth of the clock period |\r\n| Output load | Four times the capacitance of one input of the library's X4 two-input NAND (`NAND2_X4` in Nangate45) |\r\n\r\nSynthesis may target a shorter internal clock period and may retime registers. All reported figures are evaluated at the target period.\r\n\r\n## 7. Tool flow\r\n\r\nThe flow shall use open-source tools only and shall be reproducible on a clean Linux host through an install script in the repository. Each step is invoked from the repository root as `make <step> RUN=<400|800>`.\r\n\r\n| Step | Function | Output |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `synth` | Synthesis of `submission/rtl_<RUN>/` to the target library | Netlist and SDF in `submission/outputs/`; reports in `submission/syn_reports/` |\r\n| `check` | RTL simulation with the RTL checker | Simulation log ending in `ALL PASS` |\r\n| `sim` | Gate-level simulation of the netlist with the RTL checker, without back-annotation | Value change dump (VCD) |\r\n| `timing` | Gate-level simulation with SDF back-annotation and the gate-level checker | Simulation log reporting `ALL PASS` or `TIMING FAIL` |\r\n| `power` | Activity-based power analysis from the VCD | Power report |\r\n\r\nOpen-source code and optimization techniques may be used where their licenses permit, with each source cited in the report. Complete implementations of this specification from other sources shall not be used.\r\n\r\n## 8. Verification requirements\r\n\r\nThe harnesses in `starter/tb/` instantiate the design and the memory and generate the clock.\r\n\r\n### 8.1 RTL checker\r\n\r\nThe RTL checker, `submission/testbench/rtl_checker.sv` with top module `mkMultBuff_tb`, shall\r\n\r\n- run at least eight complete fill and drain phases\r\n- drive operands from a random source, in addition to the directed pairs (\u221232768, \u221232768), (\u22121, 1), (0, 32767), (32767, 32767) and (\u22121, \u22121)\r\n- deassert `EN_mult` within a fill phase and `EN_blockRead` within a drain phase\r\n- compare every product returned on `memVal_data` with an independent reference model\r\n- check every observable requirement of Section 4\r\n- print `ALL PASS` if and only if no check has failed\r\n\r\nThe stimulus shall also contain one fill phase with `EN_mult` held at 1 for 64 consecutive cycles and one drain phase with `EN_blockRead` held at 1 for 64 consecutive cycles. These windows are used for power analysis.\r\n\r\n### 8.2 Gate-level checkers\r\n\r\nThe gate-level checkers, `submission/testbench/sdf_checker_400.sv` and `sdf_checker_800.sv` with top modules `mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_400` and `mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_800`, simulate the synthesized netlist with SDF back-annotation at fixed clock periods of 2.5 ns and 1.25 ns. The SDF file is supplied as `+sdf_file=<path>`. Each checker shall\r\n\r\n- drive inputs after the rising edge and sample outputs at the falling edge\r\n- apply random operands over multiple fill and drain phases\r\n- report `TIMING FAIL` for any unknown (X) or incorrect value on `memVal_data` while `VALID_memVal` is 1\r\n- print `ALL PASS` if and only if no failure has occurred\r\n\r\nEach checker shall pass a netlist that meets timing and fail a netlist that violates it. Both outcomes shall be demonstrated and their logs retained. Where the available cell models or simulator do not turn a timing violation into an unknown value, the checker shall detect the violation through the resulting incorrect values, and the report shall describe the limitation.\r\n\r\n### 8.3 Sign-off service\r\n\r\nPushing a branch named `check/<label>` submits the RTL in `submission/rtl_400/` and `submission/rtl_800/` to an independent sign-off service. The latest commit on the branch is checked after each push. The service synthesizes each implementation with GPDK045 under the constraints of Section 6 and simulates the resulting netlists with SDF back-annotation against an independent testbench. Its scorecard is published on branch `check-results`.\r\n\r\n## 9. Deliverables\r\n\r\n```\r\nsubmission/\r\n  rtl_400/       400 MHz implementation\r\n  rtl_800/       800 MHz implementation\r\n  scripts/       synthesis and flow scripts\r\n  testbench/     rtl_checker.sv, sdf_checker_400.sv, sdf_checker_800.sv\r\n  outputs/       synthesis outputs\r\n  syn_reports/   synthesis and power reports\r\n  pdf_report/    report.pdf\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe report shall contain\r\n\r\n1. area and power at both frequencies, as a synthesis estimate and from activity-based analysis\r\n2. the pipeline depth and the critical path at each frequency\r\n3. the changes made to meet 800 MHz\r\n4. a state diagram of every state machine and a datapath diagram showing each pipeline stage and its registers\r\n5. a description of each checker, comparing RTL and gate-level waveforms and identifying effects that appear only at gate level, such as clock-to-output delay and glitches on `RDY_mult`\r\n6. the optimization techniques applied and their measured effect\r\n7. a description of the tool flow and of any departure from the constraints of Section 6\r\n8. a comparison of the open-source results with the GPDK045 sign-off results\r\n9. the external sources used, with citations\r\n10. the source listing, as an appendix\r\n\r\nThe report is generated by the implementing agent and shall be identified as AI-generated on its first page.\r\n"]
[20025.17, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat notes/WORKLOG.md\r\n# Work log: mkMultBuff (400 MHz and 800 MHz)\r\n\r\nEntries are in chronological order on 2026-11-08 (UTC). An earlier draft of this log carried clock times on each entry that were estimates rather than readings, and they were wrong, so they were removed. The reliable times come from git and from file timestamps:\r\n- session start 02:33\r\n- checkpoints 1 and 2 committed 03:01, with check/400 pushed right after\r\n- 800 MHz iterations 03:02\u201303:20 (`build/exp/*/sta.rpt`)\r\n- checkpoint 3 committed 03:26, with check/800 pushed right after\r\n- checkpoint 4 committed 03:27\r\n\r\nEach entry gives what was done, why, the commands and the results. Tool logs that support reported numbers are kept under `submission/syn_reports/`.\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 1: toolchain\r\n\r\n**Environment survey.** Ubuntu 24.04 x86-64, 4 cores, 15 GB RAM. Preinstalled: Icarus Verilog 12.0, Yosys 0.33 (apt), Verilator 5.020, GTKWave, Xvfb, pdflatex, pandoc. Docker CLI was present, but the daemon was not running; it was started with `dockerd &`. OpenSTA and OpenROAD are not in apt (`apt-cache policy opensta` gives no candidate).\r\n\r\n**Nangate45 slow corner.** OpenROAD-flow-scripts ships only `NangateOpenCellLibrary_typical.lib`. The public mirror `mflowgen/freepdk-45nm`, at commit d3be42a7, holds `stdcells-wc.lib`. That file is the Nangate Open Cell Library's slow corner: `operating_conditions (slow)`, process 1.0, 0.95 V, 125 \u00b0C, default wire load `5K_hvratio_1_1`. The repository also has the typical and best-case libraries, so the worst-case file is the slowest corner available. Its `stdcells.v` is the Nangate Verilog cell library, with `specify` blocks, `$setuphold`/`$width` checks and notifier UDPs (250 specify blocks, 196 `$setuphold`). Both files are fetched by `submission/scripts/install.sh` and checked by sha256.\r\n\r\n**OpenSTA / Yosys images.** Docker Hub has `openroad/opensta` (OpenSTA 3.1.0, f8e13cbf) and `openroad/orfs` (Yosys 0.68, OpenROAD). Both are pinned by digest in `install.sh` and in the `Makefile`. Yosys 0.68 was chosen over apt's 0.33 because it has `synth -booth` and the parallel-prefix `$lcu` maps (`+/choices/kogge-stone.v`). OpenROAD, from the same image, is used only for the Resizer (gate sizing).\r\n\r\n**Does the simulator turn timing violations into X?** No. A test of `DFF_X1` with D changing 50 ps before CK (setup 100 ps), under `iverilog -gspecify`, captured the new value with no X (`/tmp/claude-0/probe/tc/t.v`). Icarus 12 parses `$setuphold` but does not evaluate it, so the notifier never toggles. OSS CVC, an open-source simulator that does evaluate timing checks, would have to be built from source, and building it was blocked by this session's permission policy (external code). Decision: use Icarus. Under SPEC 8.2's fallback, the gate-level checkers detect violations through incorrect values; Icarus does apply SDF IOPATH and INTERCONNECT delays, so a late D is captured stale. The report describes this limitation.\r\n\r\n**install.sh.** It installs the apt packages, starts dockerd if needed, pulls both images by digest, fetches and checksums the library, and writes `submission/syn_reports/tool_versions.txt`. Run: `bash submission/scripts/install.sh` gave \"install complete\".\r\n\r\n**Make targets.** `synth`, `check`, `sim`, `timing` and `power` take `RUN=400|800`; `timing_fail` and `all` are extra.\r\n\r\n**SDF and Icarus.** Icarus annotates the *typ* entry of an SDF triple. This was checked on a single `BUF_X1` with `(0.1:0.5:0.9)`, which gave a 0.5 ns delay. OpenSTA's `-include_typ` writes typ as the mean of min and max, so `sdf_typmax.py` rewrites every triple as `(min:max:max)`, so the gate-level sims use the setup-pessimistic delays. Icarus also ignores the extra arguments of `$sdf_annotate` (such as \"MAXIMUM\") and warns about them.\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 2: 400 MHz\r\n\r\n**Checkers delegated.** A subagent wrote `rtl_checker.sv`, `sdf_checker_400.sv` and `sdf_checker_800.sv` from SPEC.md, without access to `submission/rtl_*`. It smoke-tested them against its own throwaway behavioural model and 12 broken models; all were caught.\r\n- *Reference model:* cycle-accurate, it learns the latency L from the first write, then checks every cycle for F1\u2013F15, data and X/Z, and prints `ALL PASS` iff there are 0 failures.\r\n- *Stimulus:* 14 fill/drain phases with densities from 10 to 100 %, the 5 directed pairs plus extra corners, junk EN_mult/EN_blockRead while not ready, and 4 resets (power-on, mid-fill, pipeline full, mid-drain).\r\n- *Power windows:* a 64-cycle back-to-back fill and drain, announced as `PWR_WIN` lines.\r\n- *Interpretations it recorded:* EN_readMem=0 outside accepted reads; outputs are not checked while RST_N=0; memVal_data is X-checked only while VALID.\r\n- *Gate-level checkers:* 6 phases, inputs driven 20 ps after the rising edge, outputs sampled at the falling edge, and TIMING FAIL on any X or wrong memVal_data, or on missing products.\r\n\r\n**First synthesis.** Yosys default (`synth`, `abc -D`) on the simple 2-stage RTL (operand register, then the whole multiply, then the product register): 1772 \u00b5m\u00b2, but WNS \u22125.6 ns. The critical path was 8 ns: a ripple-like final adder, plus a DFF_X1 at fanout 29 with 0.99 ns clk\u2192Q. At this corner (SS, 0.95 V, 125 \u00b0C, 5K wire load) a gate costs 0.1\u20130.5 ns.\r\n\r\n**Flow improvements, measured on the same RTL.**\r\n- *Parallel-prefix adder maps* (`-extra-map +/choices/{sklansky,kogge-stone}.v`) plus an ABC script with buffering and sizing, after ORFS `abc_speed.script` (BSD-3): WNS \u22123.8 to \u22124.1 ns.\r\n- *OpenROAD Resizer without placement* (`repair_design`, `repair_timing`; wire-load parasitics; `setRC.tcl` from ORFS nangate45): \u22123.83 \u2192 \u22121.92 ns. Buffer insertion fails without placement (RSZ-0075), so only sizing and pin swapping take effect.\r\n- *Conclusion:* a one-stage 16\u00d716 multiply needs about 4.4 ns at this corner. 400 MHz needs the multiply split over two stages, and 800 MHz over about four.\r\n\r\n**Own multiplier `mult_pipe.sv`.** It uses radix-4 modified Booth with 8 partial products. Sign extension is replaced by inverted sign bits plus the constant 0xAAAB0000, and each row's +1 sits in the free bit of the next row. Carry-save 3:2 levels go 9\u21926\u21924\u21923\u21922, then a final adder. Every pipeline cut is a parameter (PRE_ENC, ENC_REG, CSA_REG[3:0], CPA_SPLIT). Verified standalone against `a*b` over 200k random and corner pairs in several configurations (0 errors), and inside mkMultBuff with the independent RTL checker in 4 configurations (all ALL PASS).\r\n\r\n**Sweep of the 400 MHz cut** (`build/exp/run.sh`; Yosys + Resizer + OpenSTA; area is post-Resizer):\r\n\r\n| config | latency | area \u00b5m\u00b2 | WNS ns |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| operand reg, CS reg after L4 (CSA_REG=1000) | 3 | 3146 | \u22120.202 |\r\n| + Booth-encoded rank (ENC_REG) | 4 | 2820 | +0.001 |\r\n| CS reg after L2 | 3 | 2871 | +0.004 |\r\n| CS reg after L3 | 3 | 2903 | \u22120.170 |\r\n| Booth recoding before the operand reg (PRE_ENC), CS after L4, sklansky | 3 | 2311 | \u22120.354 |\r\n| PRE_ENC, CS after L4, kogge-stone | 3 | 2347 | +0.045 |\r\n| **PRE_ENC, CS after L2, kogge-stone** | **3** | **2387** | **+0.152** |\r\n| PRE_ENC, CS after L2/L4, Resizer margin 0.3 | 3 | same | no change (sizing saturates) |\r\n\r\n- *PRE_ENC:* recoding the multiplier (one/two/neg, 24 bits) before the operand register saved about 500 \u00b5m\u00b2. The recoding logic is small, and it removes the recoder from the multiply stage and the fan-out of the b bits.\r\n- *Adders:* Kogge-Stone was consistently better than Sklansky and Han-Carlson for the final adder. ABC's `-D` has no effect with this script.\r\n- *Choice:* PRE_ENC, CS register after L2, Kogge-Stone, Resizer setup margin 0.15 ns. This is the only configuration that meets the 125 ps target.\r\n\r\n**Full 400 MHz flow (`make synth|check|sim|timing|power RUN=400`).**\r\n- *synth:* WNS +0.152 ns, hold WNS +0.053 ns, TNS 0, area 2386.6 \u00b5m\u00b2 (sequential 753.8 \u00b5m\u00b2); vectorless power estimate 652.5 \u00b5W.\r\n- *check:* ALL PASS, 14 phases, about 5900 cycles, latency 3.\r\n- *sim (zero delay):* ALL PASS.\r\n- *timing (SDF, typ=max):* ALL PASS, 384 products.\r\n- *Netlist parameter:* the netlist has no parameter N, but the harness instantiates `mkMultBuff #(.N(N))`. The sim targets therefore use `build/<RUN>/netlist_sim.v`, which adds an unused `parameter N = 32`; the official netlist is unchanged.\r\n\r\n**Netlists that must fail (`make timing_fail RUN=400|800`).**\r\n- *400:* the variant with no carry-save register (`submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage`), synthesized with the same flow at 2.5 ns, has WNS \u22121.469 ns. The checker printed `TIMING FAIL: 172 failure(s)`; the first was `memVal_data=87fc0013 expected 00000013`.\r\n- *800:* the 400 MHz netlist, timed and back-annotated at 1.25 ns, has WNS \u22121.091 ns. The checker reports TIMING FAIL: the drain never starts, because the control path fails.\r\n- *Logs:* `submission/syn_reports/{400,800}/timing_fail/`.\r\n\r\n**Power (`make power RUN=400`).** OpenSTA `read_vcd -scope mkMultBuff_tb/DUT -begin_time/-end_time` on the zero-delay gate-level VCD:\r\n\r\n| case | power \u00b5W |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| whole run | 642.8 |\r\n| 64-cycle fill window | 1480.1 |\r\n| 64-cycle drain window | 430.4 |\r\n| vectorless estimate | 652.5 |\r\n\r\nIn the drain window the internal power of the 158 flip-flops' clock pins dominates. Operand isolation (zeros loaded when idle) keeps the datapath quiet.\r\n\r\n**Mutation test of the RTL checker (`submission/scripts/mutate.sh 400`).** 11 one-line mutants of the real RTL, covering ready/valid off-by-ones, missing resets, ignored enables and wrong data source. All 11 were killed (`submission/syn_reports/400/mutation.log`).\r\n\r\n**check/400 pushed** (`git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/check/400`, commit 60ed005). Work continued without waiting. Note: `rtl_800/` was still empty at that point, so the 800 part of that scorecard is expected to fail.\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 3: 800 MHz\r\n\r\n**First 800 MHz probes** (`build/exp/run.sh`, mult_pipe configurations at 1.25 ns): WNS between \u22121.1 and \u22122.8 ns. The critical path was the `RST_N` input: one DFF_X1-modelled driver into 90 to 174 synchronous-reset gates, 1.4 to 2.6 ns. The Resizer cannot buffer it without placement (RSZ-0075 makeBufferedNet failed), and ABC's `buffer -p` changed nothing (the results were bit-identical).\r\n- **Fix in resize.tcl:** a throw-away floorplan plus global placement, made only so the Resizer can insert buffers. Timing inside the Resizer stays on the wire-load model (no `estimate_parasitics`), so it is the same view as sign-off STA. Result at 800 MHz: \u22121.24 \u2192 \u22120.73 ns. At 400 MHz the result is identical (+0.152 ns, 2387 \u00b5m\u00b2).\r\n\r\n**Parallel candidate evaluations (two subagents) while I iterated on the Booth/CSA candidate:**\r\n- *(B) Behavioural `*` + R extra ranks + ABC retiming (`build/cand_retime/`):*\r\n  - Best result: WNS \u22120.20 ns at R=8, about 6.1k \u00b5m\u00b2. Retiming in ABC uses unit delays, so the result saturates near \u22120.2 ns.\r\n  - Plain retiming breaks F14: 319 of 432 flops had no reset after retiming, and ABC even moved registers onto RST_N. Keeping F14 needs a non-standard strip/re-add-reset step.\r\n  - Sign-off risk: the RTL alone is a one-stage multiplier followed by delay ranks, which GPDK045 sign-off would not retime. **Rejected.**\r\n  - Its SAT-based F14 netlist check was adopted as `make f14`.\r\n- *(C) Baugh-Wooley + Dadda, hand cut:* result pending at the time of writing; see below.\r\n- *(A) Booth/CSA mult_pipe, my own:* iterations below.\r\n\r\n**Booth/CSA iterations at 1.25 ns** (each fix found from the STA critical path; area is post-Resizer):\r\n\r\n| step | change | WNS ns | area \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| e800b | PRE_ENC, CS after L2 & L4, CPA split 16/16 | \u22121.136 | 3655 |\r\n| g800b | + placement-backed buffering | \u22120.729 | 4182 |\r\n| i800a | + SEL_REG (register after PP select), all 4 CSA levels registered, 2-stage carry-select adder | \u22120.610 | 5413 |\r\n| k800a | + ABC maps with a Liberty copy in which slow stacked cells are `dont_use` (`lib_dont_use.py`; `abc -dont_use` did not reach ABC's SCL) | \u22120.440 | 5573 |\r\n| m800b | carry-select adder rewritten with explicit in-block Kogge-Stone prefix computing both carry-in sums at once (Yosys had built `x+y+1` as two chained adders); 4-bit blocks | \u22120.159 | 5853 |\r\n| n800b | separate write and read pointers (the shared pointer drove 2 ports, 47 fF) | \u22120.090 | 5965 |\r\n| r800b | port-only copies of RDY_*, addresses and EN_writeMem, stored inverted so Yosys does not merge them with the internal copies (`(* keep *)` did not prevent merging) | \u22120.014 | 5786 |\r\n| t800b | block-carry prefix in stage B instead of a ripple | \u22120.034 | 5933 |\r\n| u800b | MUX2 also dont_use (MUX2_X1 0.24 ns) | +0.051 | 5893 |\r\n| v800b | GP4: L4 register holds generate/propagate of the final rows, moving the adder's first gate level into the L4 stage (0.36 ns slack there) | +0.136 | 5824 |\r\n| x800 | ABC output load 23.5 \u2192 1 fF: ABC sees every flop D pin as a primary output and had buffered each as if it drove the 23.5 fF port load | +0.150 | 5211 |\r\n| x800_1010 | CS registers only after L2 and L4 (473 flops instead of 577+) | \u22120.004 | 4431 |\r\n| y800_a | same, GP4 = 0 | +0.023 | 4465 |\r\n| z800_1011 | CS after L1, L2, L4 | \u22120.004 | 4973 |\r\n| **z800_1101** | **CS after L1, L3, L4 (L2+L3 share a stage: L3 is a single 3:2 on 3 of 4 rows)** | **+0.075** | **4755** |\r\n\r\nABC results vary by about \u00b10.1\u20130.2 ns with small netlist-structure changes. For example, the 400 MHz RTL with the newer mult_pipe.sv (logically identical for its parameters) maps to \u22120.037 ns instead of +0.152 ns, so rtl_400 keeps its verified mult_pipe.sv. Each final configuration is deterministic, and the knobs are fixed per RUN in the Makefile (ABC_DRIVER, ABC_LOAD, DONT_USE).\r\n\r\n**rtl_800 = z800_1101** (latency 7, 577 flops; config in `submission/rtl_800/mkMultBuff.sv`). It meets the 62 ps target at the lowest area of the passing variants. The 1111 variant has more slack (+0.150 ns) but costs +456 \u00b5m\u00b2 and about +0.34 mW of vectorless power.\r\n\r\n| step | result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `make check RUN=800` | ALL PASS, latency 7 |\r\n| `make synth RUN=800` | WNS +0.075 ns, hold +0.041 ns, 4755.0 \u00b5m\u00b2, vectorless 2727.6 \u00b5W |\r\n| `make sim RUN=800` | ALL PASS |\r\n| `make timing RUN=800` | ALL PASS, 384 products |\r\n| `make power RUN=800` | run 3073 \u00b5W, fill window 5210 \u00b5W, drain window 2536 \u00b5W |\r\n| `make f14 RUN=400` | 166/166 flops reset-gated (SAT) |\r\n| `make f14 RUN=800` | 577/577 flops reset-gated (SAT) |\r\n\r\n`make synth RUN=400` with the final scripts and the 400 knobs reproduces the committed netlist exactly: +0.152 ns, 2386.552 \u00b5m\u00b2, and `git status` shows the netlist and SDF unchanged.\r\n\r\n**Candidate (C), Baugh-Wooley + Dadda (subagent, `build/cand_dadda/`).**\r\n- *Best version (v6):* WNS +0.150 ns, hold +0.076 ns, 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2, 616 flops, latency 8, check/sim ALL PASS.\r\n- *Power (\u00b5W):*\r\n\r\n  | case | (C) Dadda v6 | (A) Booth/CSA |\r\n  |---|---|---|\r\n  | whole run | 3279 | 3073 |\r\n  | fill window | 5725 | 5210 |\r\n  | drain window | 2702 | 2536 |\r\n  | vectorless | 2820 | 2728 |\r\n\r\n- *Control:* it independently found the same control problem (ptr/RDY port load) and solved it with inverted twin registers and split 3-bit counters.\r\n- *Two smaller variants it rejected:* v7 drops the product register (writeMem_val comes from logic); v8 puts the PP/tree logic on the input path (0.97 ns), which is risky for the sign-off testbench.\r\n\r\n**Decision for 800 MHz: (A) Booth/CSA `z800_1101`.**\r\n- Both (A) and (C) meet the 62 ps target. (A) has 10 % less area (4755 vs 5278 \u00b5m\u00b2) and 6\u20139 % less power in every case, which SPEC Section 5 ranks after timing and area.\r\n- (C) has twice the slack margin (150 ps vs 75 ps), but the target is met by both.\r\n- (B), retiming, fails timing (\u22120.20 ns) and needs reset re-insertion; rejected.\r\n\r\n**Mutation test at 800 MHz** (`submission/scripts/mutate.sh 800`): 13/13 mutants killed. The extra mutants vs 400 are EN_writeMem one cycle early, the inverted port copy not reset, and a carry-select carry-in error in mult_pipe.\r\n\r\n**Waveform figures** (`submission/scripts/waves/waves.sh 400|800`). The same gate-level checker drives the RTL and the SDF-annotated netlist, so the waves line up. GTKWave 3.3.116 runs under `xvfb-run` with `-S` Tcl scripts (`/File/Grab_To_File`), light colours set by `--rcvar`, and ImageMagick crops. Windows: first writes, transition to drain, end of drain, and a 3-cycle zoom.\r\n\r\nGate-level only effects visible in the zoom:\r\n- clock-to-output delay of 0.45\u20130.7 ns on the registered outputs at 400 MHz;\r\n- a short intermediate value on writeMem_val while bits with different clk\u2192Q settle;\r\n- EN_readMem following EN_blockRead (driven 20 ps after the edge) through one AND gate.\r\n\r\nRDY_mult is a register output in both designs, so it shows no glitch.\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 4: power\r\n\r\nActivity-based power uses OpenSTA `read_vcd` on the zero-delay gate-level VCD of `make sim`, which runs the full RTL-checker stimulus. It is reported for the whole run and for the two 64-cycle windows announced by the checker (`PWR_WIN`, passed as `-begin_time/-end_time`). The vectorless \"synthesis estimate\" is `report_power` with OpenSTA's default input activity of 0.1. Reports: `submission/syn_reports/<RUN>/{sta.rpt,power.rpt,power_summary.txt}`.\r\n\r\nPower in \u00b5W, slow corner (0.95 V, 125 \u00b0C):\r\n\r\n| case | 400 MHz | 800 MHz |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| vectorless estimate | 652.5 | 2727.6 |\r\n| whole run | 642.8 | 3073.1 |\r\n| fill window (64 back-to-back accepts) | 1480.1 | 5209.5 |\r\n| drain window (64 back-to-back reads, producer idle) | 430.4 | 2535.6 |\r\n\r\nIn the drain window, sequential internal (clock) power dominates: 158 flops at 400 MHz and 577 at 800 MHz, with no clock gating.\r\n\r\n**Operand-isolation experiment** (400 MHz, `build/noiso400`; operand registers load the inputs every cycle instead of zeros when nothing is accepted). Files: `submission/syn_reports/400/experiments/`.\r\n- Area: 2337.9 \u00b5m\u00b2, against 2386.6 \u00b5m\u00b2 with isolation.\r\n- Power: whole run 1402.0 \u00b5W (+118 %), fill window 1471.1 \u00b5W, drain window 428.6 \u00b5W. The windows hardly change because the checker keeps the producer quiet in the drain window. Over the whole run, the random operands presented while not ready (F5/F11 stimulus) toggle the multiplier without isolation.\r\n- Vectorless estimate: 755.9 \u00b5W.\r\n- Isolation costs about 49 \u00b5m\u00b2 of gating and removes about 54 % of the whole-run power.\r\n\r\nGlitch power is not included, because the VCD is from the zero-delay simulation that SPEC Section 7 prescribes for `sim`. This is noted in the report.\r\n\r\n## Checkpoint 5: report\r\n\r\n**Report** (`submission/pdf_report/report.pdf`). Built by `bash submission/scripts/build_report.sh`: pandoc 3.1.3 + pdflatex from `submission/pdf_report/src/report.md`. The script fills four placeholders:\r\n- the sign-off section, from `src/signoff.md`;\r\n- the token table, from `submission/scripts/token_usage.py`;\r\n- the end time;\r\n- the full source listing appendix.\r\n\r\nFigures: Graphviz state and datapath diagrams (`src/*.dot`) and the GTKWave captures. The report is marked AI-generated on its first page, with author Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic).\r\n\r\n**Token usage** (`submission/scripts/token_usage.py`). It reads every transcript under `~/.claude/projects/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/`: the main session and the 3 subagents. Each API response is counted once (deduplicated by message id and request id), and costs use Anthropic API prices for Claude Opus 5.5:\r\n- $4 / $20 per MTok input / output;\r\n- cache reads $0.20;\r\n- cache writes 1.25\u00d7 input (5 min) or 2\u00d7 input (1 h).\r\n\r\nAt the first measurement (03:40) the total was 279 responses and $24.72. The final numbers are in the report.\r\n\r\n**Sign-off service.** `check/400` (60ed005) and `check/800` (b6917e9) were pushed at about 03:02 and 03:27. Repeated `git fetch origin check-results` returned \"couldn't find remote ref\", and `git ls-remote` shows no such branch, so no scorecard was available while the report was being built. The report states this and lists the differences to expect.\r\n\r\n**Fresh-clone rerun.** The script is in the scratchpad (`fresh.sh`). It clones the pushed branch, runs `install.sh`, `make synth check sim timing power f14` for both RUNs, `make timing_fail` for both, and the mutation tests, then reports `git status` and diffs the netlists against the committed ones. The result is recorde\r\n... (output truncated)\r\n"]
[20027.423, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat build/cand400/p1c4/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv; cat build/cand400/p1c4/rtl/mult_pipe.sv; cat submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh\r\n// mkMultBuff.sv -- 400 MHz implementation (2.5 ns clock), Nangate45 slow corner.\r\n//\r\n// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer (SPEC.md).\r\n// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, final adder), with\r\n// // three register ranks (LAT = 3):\r\n//   rank 1: operand register; the multiplier mult_input1 is Booth-recoded\r\n//           before it (one/two/neg digits), the multiplicand is stored as is\r\n//   rank 2: four carry-save rows after partial-product selection and two\r\n//           3:2 levels (9 -> 6 -> 4 rows)\r\n//   rank 3: product, after two more 3:2 levels (4 -> 3 -> 2) and a 32-bit\r\n//           Kogge-Stone adder; drives writeMem_val directly\r\n// Latency (accept -> EN_writeMem) = LAT cycles; a LAT-bit valid shift register\r\n// runs alongside the datapath and drives EN_writeMem (F4).\r\n//\r\n// Control: the two registered ready flags RDY_mult / RDY_blockRead are the\r\n// fill / drain state machine (states FILL = {1,0}, WAIT = {0,0}, DRAIN = {0,1});\r\n// acc_q counts operand pairs accepted in the fill phase, so pairs still in the\r\n// pipeline count against the capacity (F5); ptr_q is the memory address, shared\r\n// by the write pointer (fill) and the read pointer (drain), which never run in\r\n// the same cycle (F13). All outputs come from registers except EN_readMem\r\n// (= EN_blockRead & RDY_blockRead, F7) and memVal_data (= readMem_val, F8).\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (F14, F15).\r\nmodule mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (\r\n    input  logic         clk,\r\n    input  logic         RST_N,\r\n    input  logic         EN_mult,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input0,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input1,\r\n    output logic         RDY_mult,\r\n    input  logic         EN_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         RDY_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         VALID_memVal,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] memVal_data,\r\n    output logic         EN_writeMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   writeMem_addr,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] writeMem_val,\r\n    output logic         EN_readMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   readMem_addr,\r\n    input  logic [N-1:0] readMem_val\r\n);\r\n    // multiplier pipeline configuration (see mult_pipe.sv)\r\n    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1000;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n                                     + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3] + CPA_SPLIT + 1;\r\n\r\n    logic       rdy_mult_q, rdy_rd_q, vld_q;\r\n    logic [5:0] acc_q, ptr_q;\r\n    logic [LAT-1:0] v_q;                 // valid bit of each pipeline rank\r\n    logic signed [31:0] p;\r\n\r\n    wire acc = EN_mult & rdy_mult_q;\r\n    wire rd  = EN_blockRead & rdy_rd_q;\r\n    wire wr  = v_q[LAT-1];\r\n\r\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n        if (!RST_N) begin\r\n            rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; vld_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            acc_q <= '0; ptr_q <= '0; v_q <= '0;\r\n        end else begin\r\n            v_q <= {v_q[LAT-2:0], acc};\r\n            if (acc) begin\r\n                acc_q <= acc_q + 6'd1;\r\n                if (acc_q == 6'd63) rdy_mult_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            end\r\n            if (wr | rd) ptr_q <= ptr_q + 6'd1;\r\n            if (wr && ptr_q == 6'd63) rdy_rd_q <= 1'b1;\r\n            if (rd && ptr_q == 6'd63) begin\r\n                rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1;\r\n            end\r\n            vld_q <= rd;\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(clk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n\r\n    assign RDY_mult      = rdy_mult_q;\r\n    assign RDY_blockRead = rdy_rd_q;\r\n    assign EN_writeMem   = wr;\r\n    assign writeMem_addr = ptr_q;\r\n    assign writeMem_val  = p;\r\n    assign EN_readMem    = rd;\r\n    assign readMem_addr  = ptr_q;\r\n    assign VALID_memVal  = vld_q;\r\n    assign memVal_data   = readMem_val;\r\nendmodule : mkMultBuff\r\n// mult_pipe.sv -- pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier: radix-4 (modified) Booth\r\n// partial products, carry-save (3:2) reduction 9->6->4->3->2 rows and a final\r\n// carry-propagate adder. Every pipeline cut is optional (parameters).\r\n//   PRE_ENC  : Booth-recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n//   ENC_REG  : (PRE_ENC = 0 only) extra rank after the Booth recoding\r\n//   SEL_REG  : register the selected partial products (8 x 17 bits + 8 \"+1\" bits)\r\n//   CSA_REG  : bit k set -> register after carry-save level k+1 (k = 0..3)\r\n//   GP4      : the level-4 register holds generate/propagate (c&s, c^s) of the\r\n//              two final rows instead of the rows themselves (same width)\r\n//   CPA_CSEL : two-stage carry-select final adder with CSW-bit blocks and\r\n//              Kogge-Stone prefixes inside the blocks and across the blocks\r\n//   CPA_SPLIT: (alternative) low 16 bits in one stage, high 16 bits in the next\r\n// Register ranks (= latency from 'en' to 'p'): 1 (operand) + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG)\r\n//   + SEL_REG + popcount(CSA_REG) + (CPA_CSEL | CPA_SPLIT) + 1 (product)\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset. When 'en' is 0 the operand\r\n// register loads zeros (operand isolation), so an idle multiplier does not toggle.\r\n// Written for this project; the Booth recoding, the sign-extension constant and\r\n// the prefix adders follow textbook schemes (see the report's references).\r\nmodule mult_pipe #(\r\n    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n    parameter bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1000,\r\n    parameter bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter int       CSW       = 8,\r\n    parameter bit       GP4       = 1'b0\r\n) (\r\n    input  logic               clk,\r\n    input  logic               RST_N,\r\n    input  logic               en,     // accept: load operands, else load zeros\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] a,      // multiplicand (unregistered input)\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] b,      // multiplier   (unregistered input)\r\n    output logic signed [31:0] p       // product, registered\r\n);\r\n    // Booth radix-4 recoding of y: digit_i = -2 y[2i+1] + y[2i] + y[2i-1]\r\n    function automatic logic [23:0] booth_enc(input logic [15:0] y);\r\n        logic [16:0] yx;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one, two, neg;\r\n        yx = {y, 1'b0};                       // yx[k+1] = y[k], yx[0] = y[-1] = 0\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin\r\n            one[i] = yx[2*i+1] ^ yx[2*i];\r\n            two[i] = (yx[2*i+2] & ~yx[2*i+1] & ~yx[2*i]) | (~yx[2*i+2] & yx[2*i+1] & yx[2*i]);\r\n            neg[i] = yx[2*i+2];\r\n        end\r\n        booth_enc = {neg, two, one};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ---- stage 0: operand register (operand isolation: zeros when idle)\r\n    logic [7:0]  one_e, two_e, neg_e;\r\n    logic [15:0] a_e;\r\n    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\r\n        // recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_q, two_q, neg_q;\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_q, two_q, neg_q};\r\n    end else begin : g_post\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_d, two_d, neg_d;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {neg_d, two_d, one_d} = booth_enc(b_q);\r\n        if (ENC_REG) begin : g_enc\r\n            logic [7:0]  one_r, two_r, neg_r;\r\n            logic [15:0] a_r;\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n                if (!RST_N) begin a_r <= '0; one_r <= '0; two_r <= '0; neg_r <= '0; end\r\n                else begin a_r <= a_q; one_r <= one_d; two_r <= two_d; neg_r <= neg_d; end\r\n            end\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_r, one_r, two_r, neg_r};\r\n        end else begin : g_noenc\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_d, two_d, neg_d};\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    genvar i;\r\n\r\n    localparam int NB = 32 / CSW;     // carry-select blocks\r\n\r\n    // Kogge-Stone prefix over the NB block carries (generate = carry-out with\r\n    // carry-in 0, propagate = carry-out with carry-in 1)\r\n    function automatic logic [NB-1:0] bprefix(input logic [NB-1:0] g, input logic [NB-1:0] p);\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] G, P;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        for (int d = 1; d < NB; d = 2 * d)\r\n            for (int j = NB - 1; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]);\r\n                P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n            end\r\n        bprefix = G;\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // Kogge-Stone prefix over a CSW-bit block: G[j] / P[j] = group generate /\r\n    // propagate of bits j..0 of the block\r\n    function automatic logic [2*CSW-1:0] prefix(input logic [CSW-1:0] g, input logic [CSW-1:0] p);\r\n        logic [CSW-1:0] G, P;\r\n        G = g; P = p;\r\n        for (int d = 1; d < CSW; d = 2 * d)\r\n            for (int j = CSW - 1; j >= d; j--) begin\r\n                G[j] = G[j] | (P[j] & G[j-d]);\r\n                P[j] = P[j] & P[j-d];\r\n            end\r\n        prefix = {G, P};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // Partial-product rows. Sign extension is replaced by inverting each row's\r\n    // sign bit and adding the constant K = -sum(2^(16+2i)) (mod 2^32); the\r\n    // \"+1\" of each negative row is placed in the free bit of the next row.\r\n    localparam logic [31:0] K = 32'hAAAB_0000;  // -(2^16+2^18+...+2^30) mod 2^32\r\n    wire [16:0] a17 = {a_e[15], a_e};\r\n    wire [16:0] a2  = {a_e, 1'b0};\r\n    logic [31:0] r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8;\r\n    logic [16:0] pp [0:7];\r\n    logic [31:0] rw [0:7];\r\n    generate for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_pp\r\n        assign pp[i] = (({17{one_e[i]}} & a17) | ({17{two_e[i]}} & a2)) ^ {17{neg_e[i]}};\r\n        if (i == 0) begin : g_r0\r\n            assign rw[i] = {15'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0]};\r\n        end else begin : g_ri\r\n            // bits [2i+16:2i] hold the row, bit 2i-2 holds the +1 of row i-1\r\n            assign rw[i] = {13'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0], 1'b0, neg_e[i-1]} << (2*i-2);\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7} = {rw[0], rw[1], rw[2], rw[3], rw[4], rw[5], rw[6], rw[7]};\r\n    assign r8 = K | ({31'd0, neg_e[7]} << 14);\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // carry-save levels (3:2 compressors on whole rows); each optionally registered\r\n    function automatic logic [63:0] csa(input logic [31:0] x, y, z);\r\n        csa = {((x & y) | (x & z) | (y & z)) << 1, x ^ y ^ z};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // level 1: 9 -> 6, level 2: 6 -> 4, level 3: 4 -> 3, level 4: 3 -> 2\r\n    logic [6*32-1:0] l1, l1q;\r\n    logic [4*32-1:0] l2, l2q;\r\n    logic [3*32-1:0] l3, l3q;\r\n    logic [2*32-1:0] l4, l4q;\r\n    // optional register after partial-product selection (8 rows of 17 bits + the\r\n    // row +1 bits; the constant part of row 8 is re-created after the register)\r\n    logic [31:0] q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8;\r\n    generate if (SEL_REG) begin : g_sel\r\n        logic [16:0] ppq [0:7];\r\n        logic [7:0]  negq;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_q\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) ppq[i] <= RST_N ? pp[i] : 17'd0;\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) negq <= RST_N ? neg_e : 8'd0;\r\n        assign q0 = {15'd0, ~ppq[0][16], ppq[0][15:0]};\r\n        assign q1 = {13'd0, ~ppq[1][16], ppq[1][15:0], 1'b0, negq[0]} << 0;\r\n        assign q2 = {13'd0, ~ppq[2][16], ppq[2][15:0], 1'b0, negq[1]} << 2;\r\n        assign q3 = {13'd0, ~ppq[3][16], ppq[3][15:0], 1'b0, negq[2]} << 4;\r\n        assign q4 = {13'd0, ~ppq[4][16], ppq[4][15:0], 1'b0, negq[3]} << 6;\r\n        assign q5 = {13'd0, ~ppq[5][16], ppq[5][15:0], 1'b0, negq[4]} << 8;\r\n        assign q6 = {13'd0, ~ppq[6][16], ppq[6][15:0], 1'b0, negq[5]} << 10;\r\n        assign q7 = {13'd0, ~ppq[7][16], ppq[7][15:0], 1'b0, negq[6]} << 12;\r\n        assign q8 = K | ({31'd0, negq[7]} << 14);\r\n    end else begin : g_nosel\r\n        assign {q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8} = {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8};\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign l1 = {csa(q6, q7, q8), csa(q3, q4, q5), csa(q0, q1, q2)};\r\n    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    // level 4 output: the two final rows {c, s}, or (GP4) their bitwise\r\n    // generate / propagate {c & s, c ^ s}, so the adder's first gate level\r\n    // moves in front of the level-4 register\r\n    logic [63:0] l4cs;\r\n    assign l4cs = csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n    assign l4 = GP4 ? {l4cs[63:32] & l4cs[31:0], l4cs[63:32] ^ l4cs[31:0]} : l4cs;\r\n\r\n    generate\r\n        if (CSA_REG[0]) begin : g_r1\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l1q <= RST_N ? l1 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n1\r\n            assign l1q = l1;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[1]) begin : g_r2\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l2q <= RST_N ? l2 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n2\r\n            assign l2q = l2;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[2]) begin : g_r3\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l3q <= RST_N ? l3 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n3\r\n            assign l3q = l3;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[3]) begin : g_r4\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l4q <= RST_N ? l4 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n4\r\n            assign l4q = l4;\r\n        end\r\n    endgenerate\r\n    wire [31:0] sx = l4q[31:0], sy = l4q[63:32];\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // final carry-propagate adder, registered product\r\n    generate if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\r\n        // two-stage carry-select adder with CSW-bit blocks. Stage A: per block,\r\n        // bit generate/propagate and an in-block Kogge-Stone prefix give the\r\n        // block sums for carry-in 0 and carry-in 1 and the two block carry-outs.\r\n        // Stage B: the block carries are resolved and each block sum selected.\r\n        logic [31:0]   s0, s1, s0q, s1q;\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] co0, co1, co0q, co1q, cin;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_blk\r\n            logic [CSW-1:0] gg, pp_, G, P;\r\n            if (GP4) begin : g_gp\r\n                assign gg  = sy[CSW*i +: CSW];        // generate (registered)\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW];        // propagate (registered)\r\n            end else begin : g_cs\r\n                assign gg  = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] & sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n                assign pp_ = sx[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ sy[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            end\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(gg, pp_);\r\n            assign s0[CSW*i +: CSW] = pp_ ^ {G[CSW-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n            assign s1[CSW*i +: CSW] = pp_ ^ {G[CSW-2:0] | P[CSW-2:0], 1'b1};\r\n            assign co0[i] = G[CSW-1];\r\n            assign co1[i] = G[CSW-1] | P[CSW-1];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                s0q <= '0; s1q <= '0; co0q <= '0; co1q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                s0q <= s0; s1q <= s1; co0q <= co0; co1q <= co1;\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        // carry into block i = group generate of blocks i-1..0\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] bg;\r\n        assign bg  = bprefix(co0q, co1q);\r\n        assign cin = {bg[NB-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n        logic [31:0] psel;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_sel\r\n            assign psel[CSW*i +: CSW] = cin[i] ? s1q[CSW*i +: CSW] : s0q[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? psel : 32'd0;\r\n    end else if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n        logic [16:0] lo;\r\n        logic [15:0] lo_q, xh_q, yh_q;\r\n        logic        c_q;\r\n        assign lo = {1'b0, sx[15:0]} + {1'b0, sy[15:0]};\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                lo_q <= '0; c_q <= 1'b0; xh_q <= '0; yh_q <= '0; p <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                lo_q <= lo[15:0]; c_q <= lo[16];\r\n                xh_q <= sx[31:16]; yh_q <= sy[31:16];\r\n                p    <= {xh_q + yh_q + {15'd0, c_q}, lo_q};\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n    end else begin : g_full\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) p <= '0;\r\n            else        p <= sx + sy;\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\nendmodule : mult_pipe\r\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n# eval_candidate.sh RUN RTL_DIR WORK_DIR [make overrides...]\r\n# Runs one candidate implementation through the open-source flow (synth, RTL check,\r\n# zero-delay gate sim, activity power) and prints one summary block: slack, area\r\n# split sequential/combinational, flops, vectorless and activity power, and the flop\r\n# count and worst setup slack of every register group (Q-net name).\r\n# Example: bash submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh 800 build/cand/x/rtl build/cand/x\r\nset -uo pipefail\r\nRUN=$1; RTL=$2; W=$3; shift 3\r\nmkdir -p \"$W/rep\"\r\nM=\"RUN=$RUN RTL_DIR=$RTL BUILD=$W REP=$W/rep NETLIST=$W/map.v SDF=$W/map.sdf $*\"\r\nmake -s check $M > \"$W/check.out\" 2>&1; CHK=$(grep -c \"^ALL PASS\" \"$W/rep/check.log\" 2>/dev/null)\r\nmake -s synth $M > \"$W/synth.out\" 2>&1\r\nmake -s sim $M > \"$W/sim.out\" 2>&1;   SIM=$(grep -c \"^ALL PASS\" \"$W/rep/sim.log\" 2>/dev/null)\r\nmake -s power $M > \"$W/power.out\" 2>&1\r\nPER=$([ \"$RUN\" = 400 ] && echo 2.5 || echo 1.25)\r\ndocker run --rm -v \"$PWD:$PWD\" -w \"$PWD\" -e LIB=tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib -e NETLIST=\"$W/map.v\" \\\r\n  -e PERIOD=\"$PER\" --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta \\\r\n  openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a \\\r\n  -no_init -no_splash -exit submission/scripts/ranks.tcl > \"$W/rep/ranks.rpt\" 2>&1\r\nS=\"$W/rep/sta.rpt\"\r\nWNS=$(awk '/^worst slack max/{print $NF}' \"$S\"); WHS=$(awk '/^worst slack min/{print $NF}' \"$S\")\r\nAREA=$(grep \"^cell area\" \"$S\")\r\nTOT=$(echo \"$AREA\" | sed 's/cell area \\([0-9.]*\\).*/\\1/'); SEQ=$(echo \"$AREA\" | sed 's/.*sequential \\([0-9.]*\\).*/\\1/')\r\nFF=$(awk '/^cell DFF/{n+=$3} END{print n}' \"$S\")\r\nPV=$(awk '/^Total/{print $5*1e6; exit}' \"$S\")\r\nPS=$(awk 'NR>2{printf \"%s=%s \", $1, $NF}' \"$W/rep/power_summary.txt\" 2>/dev/null)\r\necho \"== $W RUN=$RUN\"\r\necho \"check=$([ \"$CHK\" = 1 ] && echo PASS || echo FAIL) sim=$([ \"$SIM\" = 1 ] && echo PASS || echo FAIL) wns=$WNS whs=$WHS\"\r\nprintf \"area=%s seq=%s comb=%.1f flops=%s vectorless_uW=%.1f\\n\" \"$TOT\" \"$SEQ\" \"$(echo \"$TOT - $SEQ\" | bc)\" \"$FF\" \"$PV\"\r\necho \"activity_uW: $PS\"\r\necho \"per register group (flops, worst slack):\"; cat \"$W/rep/ranks.rpt\" | grep -v \"^Warning\"\r\n"]
[20029.521, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat Makefile; ls submission/scripts; ls build/cand400/p1c4/rep\r\n# Makefile -- open-source flow for mkMultBuff (SPEC.md Section 7).\r\n# Usage: make <synth|check|sim|timing|power|all> RUN=<400|800>\r\n# Toolchain: bash submission/scripts/install.sh\r\n\r\nRUN      ?= 400\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 2.5\r\n  HALF    := 1.25\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 2200\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\n  # ABC mapping knobs (see notes/WORKLOG.md): no input-driver model, the SPEC\r\n  # output load on every ABC output, full cell library\r\n  ABC_DRIVER ?= none\r\n  ABC_LOAD   ?= 23.5\r\n  DONT_USE   ?=\r\nelse ifeq ($(RUN),800)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 1.25\r\n  HALF    := 0.625\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 1050\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\n  # ABC mapping knobs: BUF_X1 input driver, 1 fF load (ABC outputs are mostly\r\n  # flip-flop D pins), and no cells with 3- or 4-high stacks or MUX2 (slow at\r\n  # the slow corner) during mapping\r\n  ABC_DRIVER ?= BUF_X1\r\n  ABC_LOAD   ?= 1.0\r\n  DONT_USE   ?= OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_* MUX2_*\r\nelse\r\n  $(error RUN must be 400 or 800)\r\nendif\r\n\r\nROOT     := $(CURDIR)\r\nLIB      := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib\r\nCELLS    := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary.v\r\nRTL_DIR  ?= submission/rtl_$(RUN)\r\nRTL      := $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv)\r\nMEM      := starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv starter/rtl/registerArray.sv\r\nTB       := submission/testbench\r\nOUT      := submission/outputs\r\nREP      ?= submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)\r\nBUILD    ?= build/$(RUN)\r\nNETLIST  ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.v\r\nSDF      ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.sdf\r\nSEED     ?= 402\r\nSETUP_MARGIN ?= 0.15\r\n\r\nYOSYS_IMAGE := openroad/orfs@sha256:d3505fd5f930fcd20d3d25a41f3047230b7db7b7797e3448561c9e556cca3774\r\nSTA_IMAGE   := openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a\r\nDOCKER      := docker run --rm -v $(ROOT):$(ROOT) -w $(ROOT)\r\nYOSYS       := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e RTL_DIR=$(RTL_DIR) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e ABC_D=$(ABC_D) -e BOOTH=$(BOOTH) -e ADDER=$(ADDER) -e OUT=$(BUILD)/syn.v \\\r\n               -e ABC_DRIVER=$(ABC_DRIVER) -e ABC_LOAD=$(ABC_LOAD) -e MAPLIB=$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),$(BUILD)/maplib.lib,) \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/yosys\r\nOPENROAD    := $(DOCKER) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST_IN=$(BUILD)/syn.v -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               -e SETUP_MARGIN=$(SETUP_MARGIN) -e PDK_LEF_DIR=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/nangate45/lef \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/OpenROAD/bin/openroad -no_init -exit\r\nSTA         := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e SDF=$(SDF) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta $(STA_IMAGE) -no_init -no_splash -exit\r\n\r\n.PHONY: synth check sim timing power all clean timing_fail sta_only f14\r\n\r\n$(REP) $(BUILD) $(OUT):\r\n\tmkdir -p $@\r\n\r\n# ---- synthesis + static timing (netlist, SDF, area/timing/power-estimate reports)\r\nsynth: | $(REP) $(OUT) $(BUILD)\r\n\t$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),python3 submission/scripts/lib_dont_use.py $(LIB) $(BUILD)/maplib.lib $(foreach c,$(DONT_USE),'$(c)'),)\r\n\t$(YOSYS) -q -l $(REP)/synth.log -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl\r\n\tmv -f $(BUILD)/syn.stat.rpt $(REP)/yosys_area.rpt\r\n\t$(OPENROAD) submission/scripts/resize.tcl > $(REP)/resize.log 2>&1\r\n\t$(STA) submission/scripts/sta.tcl > $(REP)/sta.rpt 2>&1\r\n\tpython3 submission/scripts/sdf_typmax.py $(SDF).sta $(SDF) && rm -f $(SDF).sta\r\n\t@grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns|Total|cell area)\" $(REP)/sta.rpt\r\n\r\n# ---- RTL simulation with the RTL checker\r\ncheck: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=$(HALF) -o $(BUILD)/check.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/rtl_checker.sv $(MEM) $(RTL)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/check.vvp +seed=$(SEED) | tee $(REP)/check.log | tail -25\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/check.log || { echo \"check FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# simulation copy of the netlist: the harness instantiates mkMultBuff #(.N(32)),\r\n# so an (unused) parameter N is declared in the netlist module\r\n$(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v: $(NETLIST) | $(BUILD)\r\n\tsed -e '0,/^module mkMultBuff (/s//module mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (/' $< > $@\r\n\r\n# ---- gate-level simulation (zero delay, no back-annotation) with the RTL checker -> VCD\r\nsim: $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=$(HALF) -o $(BUILD)/sim.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/rtl_checker.sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/sim.vvp +seed=$(SEED) +vcd=$(BUILD)/gate.vcd | tee $(REP)/sim.log | tail -25\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/sim.log || { echo \"sim FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# ---- gate-level simulation with SDF back-annotation and the gate-level checker\r\ntiming: $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -gspecify -s mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_$(RUN) -o $(BUILD)/timing.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/sdf_checker_$(RUN).sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/timing.vvp +sdf_file=$(SDF) +seed=$(SEED) > $(REP)/timing.log 2>&1 ; true\r\n\t@grep -v -i \"sdf.*warning\" $(REP)/timing.log | tail -12\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/timing.log || { echo \"timing FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# ---- activity-based power from the gate-level VCD (whole run and the two 64-cycle windows)\r\npower: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tbash submission/scripts/power.sh $(REP) $(BUILD) $(NETLIST) $(PERIOD) $(LIB) $(STA_IMAGE)\r\n\r\n# ---- demonstration that the gate-level checker fails a netlist that violates timing\r\n#  RUN=400: the one-stage-multiplier variant in submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage,\r\n#           synthesized with the same flow at 2.5 ns (STA reports negative slack)\r\n#  RUN=800: the 400 MHz netlist, timed by STA and back-annotated at 1.25 ns\r\nFAIL_BUILD := build/fail_$(RUN)\r\nFAIL_REP   := submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)/timing_fail\r\ntiming_fail:\r\n\tmkdir -p $(FAIL_BUILD) $(FAIL_REP)\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n\t$(MAKE) synth RUN=400 RTL_DIR=submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n\t    NETLIST=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.v SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\nelse\r\n\t$(MAKE) sta_only RUN=800 BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n\t    NETLIST=$(OUT)/mkMultBuff_400_map.v SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\nendif\r\n\t-$(MAKE) timing RUN=$(RUN) BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) NETLIST=$(if $(filter 400,$(RUN)),$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.v,$(OUT)/mkMultBuff_400_map.v) SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\n\t@grep -q \"TIMING FAIL\" $(FAIL_REP)/timing.log && echo \"timing_fail: checker reported TIMING FAIL as expected\" \\\r\n\t    || { echo \"timing_fail: checker did NOT fail\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\nsta_only: | $(REP)\r\n\t$(STA) submission/scripts/sta.tcl > $(REP)/sta.rpt 2>&1\r\n\tpython3 submission/scripts/sdf_typmax.py $(SDF).sta $(SDF) && rm -f $(SDF).sta\r\n\t@grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns)\" $(REP)/sta.rpt\r\n\r\n# ---- SPEC F14: formal (SAT) proof that every flip-flop of the netlist is reset by RST_N\r\nf14: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tbash submission/scripts/f14_check.sh $(NETLIST) $(BUILD)/f14 | tee $(REP)/f14.log\r\n\r\nall: synth check sim timing power f14\r\n\r\nclean:\r\n\trm -rf build\r\nabc_speed.script\r\nbuild_report.sh\r\nconstraints.tcl\r\neval_candidate.sh\r\nf14_check.sh\r\nf14_check.tcl\r\nfresh_clone_rerun.sh\r\ninstall.sh\r\nlib_dont_use.py\r\nmutate.sh\r\npower.sh\r\npower.tcl\r\npower_summary.py\r\nranks.tcl\r\nresize.tcl\r\nsdf_typmax.py\r\nsta.tcl\r\nsynth.tcl\r\ntoken_usage.py\r\nwaves\r\ncheck.log\r\npower.rpt\r\npower_summary.txt\r\nranks.rpt\r\nresize.log\r\nsim.log\r\nsta.rpt\r\nsynth.log\r\nyosys_area.rpt\r\n"]
[20031.594, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat submission/scripts/synth.tcl submission/scripts/resize.tcl submission/scripts/sta.tcl submission/scripts/constraints.tcl submission/scripts/power.tcl submission/scripts/ranks.tcl\r\n# synth.tcl -- Yosys synthesis of submission/rtl_$RUN to Nangate45 (slow corner).\r\n# Invoked by the Makefile:  yosys -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl  with env\r\n#   RUN      400 | 800\r\n#   LIB      Liberty file (Nangate45 slow corner)\r\n#   ABC_D    ABC delay target in ps (may be shorter than the clock period)\r\n#   BOOTH    1 to let Yosys build a radix-4 Booth multiplier for '*'\r\n#   OUT      netlist path\r\nyosys -import\r\nset run   $::env(RUN)\r\nset lib   $::env(LIB)\r\nset abc_d $::env(ABC_D)\r\nset booth [expr {[info exists ::env(BOOTH)] ? $::env(BOOTH) : 0}]\r\nset out   $::env(OUT)\r\n# library used by ABC for mapping (may mark slow cells dont_use); everything\r\n# else (flip-flop mapping, area report) uses the original library\r\nset maplib [expr {[info exists ::env(MAPLIB)] && $::env(MAPLIB) ne \"\" ? $::env(MAPLIB) : $lib}]\r\n# final-adder architecture for $lcu (carry look-ahead unit): a Yosys parallel-prefix choice\r\nset adder [expr {[info exists ::env(ADDER)] ? $::env(ADDER) : \"sklansky\"}]\r\nset extra {}\r\nif {$adder ne \"ripple\"} { set extra [list -extra-map +/choices/${adder}.v] }\r\n\r\nread_liberty -lib $lib\r\n# read every .sv file of the source directory, in any order (SPEC Section 5)\r\nset rtl_dir [expr {[info exists ::env(RTL_DIR)] ? $::env(RTL_DIR) : \"submission/rtl_${run}\"}]\r\nforeach f [lsort [glob ${rtl_dir}/*.sv]] { read_verilog -sv $f }\r\nhierarchy -check -top mkMultBuff\r\nset sargs [list -top mkMultBuff -flatten {*}$extra]\r\nif {$booth} { lappend sargs -booth }\r\nsynth {*}$sargs\r\nopt -full\r\n# sequential mapping: Nangate has no synchronous-reset flop, so the reset is a\r\n# gate in front of D (dfflegalize keeps it synchronous)\r\ndfflibmap -liberty $lib\r\nopt\r\n# ABC: delay-oriented mapping followed by buffering and gate sizing; the\r\n# constraint file gives ABC the input drive and the output load of SPEC Section 6\r\nset cf [open [file rootname $out].abc.constr w]\r\nset drv  [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_DRIVER)] ? $::env(ABC_DRIVER) : \"BUF_X1\"}]\r\nset load [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_LOAD)] ? $::env(ABC_LOAD) : 1.0}]\r\nif {$drv ne \"\" && $drv ne \"none\"} { puts $cf \"set_driving_cell $drv\" }\r\nputs $cf \"set_load $load\"\r\nclose $cf\r\nset abc_script [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_SCRIPT)] ? $::env(ABC_SCRIPT) : \"submission/scripts/abc_speed.script\"}]\r\nif {$abc_script eq \"default\"} {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $maplib -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n} else {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $maplib -script $abc_script -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n}\r\nfile delete [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\nopt_clean\r\nsetundef -zero\r\nhilomap -singleton -hicell LOGIC1_X1 Z -locell LOGIC0_X1 Z\r\nopt_clean -purge\r\ncheck -assert\r\ntee -o [file rootname $out].stat.rpt stat -liberty $lib\r\nwrite_verilog -noattr -noexpr -nohex -nodec $out\r\n# resize.tcl -- OpenROAD Resizer on the Yosys netlist: fix slew/capacitance/fanout,\r\n# then gate sizing and buffering for setup and hold.\r\n# Timing inside the Resizer uses the library wire-load model, as the sign-off STA\r\n# does (no parasitics are estimated). A throw-away floorplan and global placement\r\n# are made only because the Resizer needs cell locations to insert buffers\r\n# (without them makeBufferedNet fails and high-fanout nets such as RST_N cannot\r\n# be buffered); the placement is not used for timing and is not an output.\r\n# env: LIB, NETLIST_IN, NETLIST, PERIOD, PDK_LEF_DIR, SETUP_MARGIN\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nset pdk $::env(PDK_LEF_DIR)/..\r\nread_lef $pdk/lef/NangateOpenCellLibrary.tech.lef\r\nread_lef $pdk/lef/NangateOpenCellLibrary.macro.mod.lef\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST_IN)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nsource $pdk/setRC.tcl\r\nset_dont_use {WELLTAP_X1 ANTENNA_X1 FILLCELL_* TBUF_* TINV_* CLKGATE* LOGIC* DLH_* DLL_* TLAT_*}\r\nputs \"== before: [format %.3f [expr {[sta::worst_slack_cmd max] * 1e9}]] ns\"\r\n\r\ninitialize_floorplan -utilization 40 -aspect_ratio 1 -core_space 2 \\\r\n    -site FreePDK45_38x28_10R_NP_162NW_34O\r\nsource $pdk/make_tracks.tcl\r\nplace_pins -hor_layers metal3 -ver_layers metal2 -random\r\nglobal_placement -density 0.6 -skip_io\r\n# timing stays on the wire-load model (no estimate_parasitics)\r\n\r\nset margin [expr {[info exists ::env(SETUP_MARGIN)] ? $::env(SETUP_MARGIN) : 0.15}]\r\nrepair_design\r\nrepair_timing -setup -repair_tns 100 -setup_margin $margin -effort high\r\nrepair_timing -hold -hold_margin 0.02\r\nreport_worst_slack -max\r\nreport_worst_slack -min\r\nreport_design_area\r\nwrite_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\n# sta.tcl -- OpenSTA timing at the target period; writes the SDF for gate-level sim.\r\n# env: RUN, LIB, NETLIST, SDF, PERIOD (ns)\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nputs \"== constraints: period $period ns, clock/input transition [expr {$period/8.0}] ns, output load [expr {4.0*$c_nand}] fF\"\r\nreport_checks -path_delay max -group_path_count 3 -format full_clock_expanded \\\r\n    -fields {slew cap input_pins fanout} -digits 3\r\nreport_checks -path_delay min -format full_clock_expanded -fields {slew cap input_pins} -digits 3\r\nputs \"== summary\"\r\nreport_worst_slack -max -digits 3\r\nreport_worst_slack -min -digits 3\r\nreport_tns -digits 3\r\nreport_check_types -max_slew -max_capacitance -max_fanout -violators\r\nreport_power -digits 4\r\n# cell area of the final netlist, from the Liberty areas\r\nset area 0.0\r\narray set hist {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n    set lc [get_property $inst ref_name]\r\n    set a [get_property [get_lib_cells */$lc] area]\r\n    set area [expr {$area + $a}]\r\n    if {[info exists hist($lc)]} { incr hist($lc) } else { set hist($lc) 1 }\r\n}\r\nset seq 0.0\r\nforeach lc [lsort [array names hist]] {\r\n    set a [get_property [get_lib_cells */$lc] area]\r\n    if {[string match DFF* $lc]} { set seq [expr {$seq + $a * $hist($lc)}] }\r\n    puts [format \"cell %-14s %5d  %9.3f um^2\" $lc $hist($lc) [expr {$a * $hist($lc)}]]\r\n}\r\nputs [format \"cell area %.3f um^2 (sequential %.3f um^2, %d instances)\" $area $seq [llength [get_cells *]]]\r\nwrite_sdf -include_typ -digits 4 -no_timestamp $::env(SDF).sta\r\nputs \"SDF written to $::env(SDF)\"\r\n# constraints.tcl -- SPEC.md Section 6 constraints for OpenSTA. Needs $period (ns).\r\nset clk_port [get_ports clk]\r\ncreate_clock -name clk -period $period $clk_port\r\nset_clock_transition [expr {$period / 8.0}] [get_clocks clk]\r\nset in_ports [lsearch -inline -all -not -exact [all_inputs] $clk_port]\r\nset_input_delay  0.0 -clock clk $in_ports\r\nset_output_delay 0.0 -clock clk [all_outputs]\r\n# input drive: output of the smallest D flip-flop (DFF_X1/Q), whose clock input\r\n# has a transition of one eighth of the clock period\r\nset_driving_cell -lib_cell DFF_X1 -pin Q -from_pin CK \\\r\n    -input_transition_rise [expr {$period / 8.0}] \\\r\n    -input_transition_fall [expr {$period / 8.0}] $in_ports\r\n# output load: 4 x input capacitance of NAND2_X4 (pin A1)\r\nset c_nand [get_property [get_lib_pins */NAND2_X4/A1] capacitance]\r\nset_load [expr {4.0 * $c_nand}] [all_outputs]\r\n# pre-layout wire estimate: the library's default wire-load model\r\nset_wire_load_model -name 5K_hvratio_1_1\r\n# power.tcl -- activity-based power with OpenSTA from the gate-level VCD.\r\n# env: LIB NETLIST PERIOD VCD TAG [BEGIN END] (VCD time units, ps)\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nset args [list -scope mkMultBuff_tb/DUT]\r\nset win \"whole run\"\r\nif {[info exists ::env(BEGIN)] && $::env(BEGIN) ne \"\"} {\r\n    lappend args -begin_time $::env(BEGIN) -end_time $::env(END)\r\n    set win \"$::env(BEGIN)..$::env(END) ps\"\r\n}\r\nread_vcd {*}$args $::env(VCD)\r\nputs \"== power $::env(TAG): window $win, VCD $::env(VCD)\"\r\nreport_power -digits 4\r\n# ranks.tcl -- flop count and worst setup slack at D per register group (Q-net name). env: LIB NETLIST PERIOD\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\narray set w {}; array set n {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n  if {![string match DFF* [get_property $inst ref_name]]} continue\r\n  set in [get_full_name $inst]\r\n  set q [get_full_name [get_nets -of_objects [get_pins $in/Q]]]\r\n  regsub {\\s*\\[[0-9]+\\]\\s*$} $q \"\" g\r\n  set s [get_property [get_pins $in/D] slack_max]\r\n  if {![info exists w($g)] || $s < $w($g)} { set w($g) $s }\r\n  if {[info exists n($g)]} { incr n($g) } else { set n($g) 1 }\r\n}\r\nforeach g [lsort [array names w]] { puts [format \"%-36s %4d %8.3f\" $g $n($g) $w($g)] }\r\n"]
[20035.18, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m R=build/cand400/p1c4/rep; grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns|Total|cell area)\" $R/sta.rpt; cat $R/power_summary.txt; cat $R/ranks.rpt | grep -v Warning; grep -E \"^cell \" $R/sta.rpt | head -60; cat submission/scripts/power.sh\r\nworst slack max 0.207\r\nworst slack min 0.061\r\ntns max 0.000\r\nTotal                4.5598e-04 1.6999e-04 3.7248e-05 6.6322e-04 100.0%\r\ncell area 2517.956 um^2 (sequential 673.778 um^2, 1592 instances)\r\ncase                                                internal switching   leakage  total uW\r\nsynthesis estimate (vectorless, activity 0.1)         455.98    169.99     37.25    663.22\r\nrun: window whole run                                 448.20    173.54     37.32    659.06\r\nfill: window 521250..681250 ps                        882.55    684.53     39.37   1606.50\r\ndrain: window 688750..848750 ps                       334.84     26.92     36.70    398.46\r\nEN_writeMem                             1    1.966\r\nRDY_blockRead                           1    0.989\r\nRDY_mult                                1    0.944\r\nVALID_memVal                            1    1.309\r\nacc_q                                   6    0.802\r\nreadMem_addr                            6    0.602\r\nu_mult.a17                             16    1.070\r\nu_mult.g_pre.neg_q                      8    1.263\r\nu_mult.g_pre.one_q                      8    1.274\r\nu_mult.g_pre.two_q                      8    1.174\r\nu_mult.l4q                             59    0.268\r\nv_q                                     2    1.162\r\nwriteMem_val                           32    0.207\r\ncell AND2_X1           54     57.456 um^2\r\ncell AND2_X2            2      2.660 um^2\r\ncell AND3_X1           22     29.260 um^2\r\ncell AND3_X2            2      3.192 um^2\r\ncell AOI21_X1         105    111.720 um^2\r\ncell AOI21_X2          11     20.482 um^2\r\ncell AOI22_X1          97    129.010 um^2\r\ncell AOI22_X2          24     57.456 um^2\r\ncell AOI22_X4           3     13.566 um^2\r\ncell BUF_X1            49     39.102 um^2\r\ncell BUF_X2            23     24.472 um^2\r\ncell BUF_X4            46     85.652 um^2\r\ncell BUF_X8             4     13.832 um^2\r\ncell CLKBUF_X1         24     19.152 um^2\r\ncell CLKBUF_X2          3      3.192 um^2\r\ncell CLKBUF_X3          3      3.990 um^2\r\ncell DFF_X1           149    673.778 um^2\r\ncell INV_X1            79     42.028 um^2\r\ncell INV_X2             1      0.798 um^2\r\ncell NAND2_X1         124     98.952 um^2\r\ncell NAND2_X2           1      1.330 um^2\r\ncell NAND3_X1          42     44.688 um^2\r\ncell NOR2_X1          198    158.004 um^2\r\ncell NOR2_X2            6      7.980 um^2\r\ncell NOR2_X4            2      4.788 um^2\r\ncell OAI21_X1          82     87.248 um^2\r\ncell OAI21_X2           3      5.586 um^2\r\ncell OAI21_X4           4     13.832 um^2\r\ncell OAI22_X1           4      5.320 um^2\r\ncell OAI22_X2           1      2.394 um^2\r\ncell OAI22_X4           1      4.522 um^2\r\ncell OR2_X1            22     23.408 um^2\r\ncell OR2_X2             1      1.330 um^2\r\ncell XNOR2_X1         244    389.424 um^2\r\ncell XNOR2_X2          75    199.500 um^2\r\ncell XOR2_X1           69    110.124 um^2\r\ncell XOR2_X2           12     28.728 um^2\r\ncell area 2517.956 um^2 (sequential 673.778 um^2, 1592 instances)\r\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n# power.sh REP BUILD NETLIST PERIOD LIB STA_IMAGE\r\n# Activity-based power from the gate-level VCD of `make sim`: the whole run and the\r\n# two 64-cycle windows announced by the RTL checker as \"PWR_WIN <fill|drain> <t0> <t1>\".\r\nset -euo pipefail\r\nREP=$1 BUILD=$2 NETLIST=$3 PERIOD=$4 LIB=$5 IMG=$6\r\nVCD=$BUILD/gate.vcd\r\n[ -f \"$VCD\" ] || { echo \"power.sh: $VCD missing, run make sim first\"; exit 1; }\r\nsta() {  # TAG [BEGIN END]\r\n  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD:$PWD\" -w \"$PWD\" -e LIB=\"$LIB\" -e NETLIST=\"$NETLIST\" \\\r\n    -e PERIOD=\"$PERIOD\" -e VCD=\"$VCD\" -e TAG=\"$1\" -e BEGIN=\"${2:-}\" -e END=\"${3:-}\" \\\r\n    --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta \"$IMG\" -no_init -no_splash -exit submission/scripts/power.tcl\r\n}\r\nsta run > \"$REP/power.rpt\" 2>&1\r\nfor w in fill drain; do\r\n  read -r _ _ t0 t1 < <(grep \"^PWR_WIN $w \" \"$REP/sim.log\" | head -1)\r\n  sta \"$w\" \"$t0\" \"$t1\" >> \"$REP/power.rpt\" 2>&1\r\ndone\r\npython3 submission/scripts/power_summary.py \"$REP\" | tee \"$REP/power_summary.txt\"\r\n"]
[20045.107, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 1,40p submission/rtl_400/mkMultBuff.sv; grep -n \"mult_pipe\\|LAT\\b\\|localparam\" submission/rtl_400/mkMultBuff.sv; diff <(sed -n '/^module/,$p' submission/rtl_400/mult_pipe.sv) <(sed -n '/^module/,$p' submission/rtl_800/mult_pipe.sv) | head -5; cat Makefile | grep -n \"ABC\\|DONT\\|RUN\" | head -30\r\n// mkMultBuff.sv -- 400 MHz implementation (2.5 ns clock), Nangate45 slow corner.\r\n//\r\n// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer (SPEC.md).\r\n// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, final adder), with\r\n// // three register ranks (LAT = 3):\r\n//   rank 1: operand register; the multiplier mult_input1 is Booth-recoded\r\n//           before it (one/two/neg digits), the multiplicand is stored as is\r\n//   rank 2: four carry-save rows after partial-product selection and two\r\n//           3:2 levels (9 -> 6 -> 4 rows)\r\n//   rank 3: product, after two more 3:2 levels (4 -> 3 -> 2) and a 32-bit\r\n//           Kogge-Stone adder; drives writeMem_val directly\r\n// Latency (accept -> EN_writeMem) = LAT cycles; a LAT-bit valid shift register\r\n// runs alongside the datapath and drives EN_writeMem (F4).\r\n//\r\n// Control: the two registered ready flags RDY_mult / RDY_blockRead are the\r\n// fill / drain state machine (states FILL = {1,0}, WAIT = {0,0}, DRAIN = {0,1});\r\n// acc_q counts operand pairs accepted in the fill phase, so pairs still in the\r\n// pipeline count against the capacity (F5); ptr_q is the memory address, shared\r\n// by the write pointer (fill) and the read pointer (drain), which never run in\r\n// the same cycle (F13). All outputs come from registers except EN_readMem\r\n// (= EN_blockRead & RDY_blockRead, F7) and memVal_data (= readMem_val, F8).\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (F14, F15).\r\nmodule mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (\r\n    input  logic         clk,\r\n    input  logic         RST_N,\r\n    input  logic         EN_mult,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input0,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input1,\r\n    output logic         RDY_mult,\r\n    input  logic         EN_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         RDY_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         VALID_memVal,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] memVal_data,\r\n    output logic         EN_writeMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   writeMem_addr,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] writeMem_val,\r\n    output logic         EN_readMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   readMem_addr,\r\n    input  logic [N-1:0] readMem_val\r\n);\r\n4:// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, final adder), with\r\n5:// // three register ranks (LAT = 3):\r\n12:// Latency (accept -> EN_writeMem) = LAT cycles; a LAT-bit valid shift register\r\n41:    // multiplier pipeline configuration (see mult_pipe.sv)\r\n42:    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n43:    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n44:    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b0100;\r\n45:    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n46:    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n51:    logic [LAT-1:0] v_q;                 // valid bit of each pipeline rank\r\n56:    wire wr  = v_q[LAT-1];\r\n63:            v_q <= {v_q[LAT-2:0], acc};\r\n77:    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\n5c5,9\r\n<     parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0\r\n---\r\n>     parameter bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n>     parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0,\r\n2:# Usage: make <synth|check|sim|timing|power|all> RUN=<400|800>\r\n5:RUN      ?= 400\r\n6:ifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n9:  ABC_D   ?= 2200\r\n12:  # ABC mapping knobs (see notes/WORKLOG.md): no input-driver model, the SPEC\r\n13:  # output load on every ABC output, full cell library\r\n14:  ABC_DRIVER ?= none\r\n15:  ABC_LOAD   ?= 23.5\r\n16:  DONT_USE   ?=\r\n17:else ifeq ($(RUN),800)\r\n20:  ABC_D   ?= 1050\r\n23:  # ABC mapping knobs: BUF_X1 input driver, 1 fF load (ABC outputs are mostly\r\n26:  ABC_DRIVER ?= BUF_X1\r\n27:  ABC_LOAD   ?= 1.0\r\n28:  DONT_USE   ?= OAI33_* NOR3_* NOR4_* OR3_* OR4_* AND4_* NAND4_* AOI211_* AOI221_* AOI222_* OAI211_* OAI221_* OAI222_* MUX2_*\r\n30:  $(error RUN must be 400 or 800)\r\n36:RTL_DIR  ?= submission/rtl_$(RUN)\r\n41:REP      ?= submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)\r\n42:BUILD    ?= build/$(RUN)\r\n43:NETLIST  ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.v\r\n44:SDF      ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.sdf\r\n51:YOSYS       := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e RTL_DIR=$(RTL_DIR) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e ABC_D=$(ABC_D) -e BOOTH=$(BOOTH) -e ADDER=$(ADDER) -e OUT=$(BUILD)/syn.v \\\r\n52:               -e ABC_DRIVER=$(ABC_DRIVER) -e ABC_LOAD=$(ABC_LOAD) -e MAPLIB=$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),$(BUILD)/maplib.lib,) \\\r\n57:STA         := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e SDF=$(SDF) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n67:\t$(if $(strip $(DONT_USE)),python3 submission/scripts/lib_dont_use.py $(LIB) $(BUILD)/maplib.lib $(foreach c,$(DONT_USE),'$(c)'),)\r\n96:\tiverilog -g2012 -gspecify -s mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_$(RUN) -o $(BUILD)/timing.vvp \\\r\n97:\t    $(TB)/sdf_checker_$(RUN).sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n107:#  RUN=400: the one-stage-multiplier variant in submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage,\r\n109:#  RUN=800: the 400 MHz netlist, timed by STA and back-annotated at 1.25 ns\r\n110:FAIL_BUILD := build/fail_$(RUN)\r\n"]
[20060.862, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m build/cand800a/mk.sh e2_1010_cinc CSA_REG=\"4'b1010\" ORD=\"1'b1\" GT=\"1'b1\" CPA=1 2>&1 | tail -4\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-0.118 whs=0.020\r\narea=4174.604 seq=2025.856 comb=2148.7 flops=448 vectorless_uW=2238.4\r\nactivity_uW: run:=2535.70 fill:=4658.10 drain:=1987.50 \r\nR1op:40(0.215) PP:144(0.156) L2:92(0.077) GP:60(0.088) ADD:38(0.189) PROD:32(-0.118) CTRL:42(0.130)\r\n"]
[20064.761, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m awk '/^Startpoint/{n++} n==1' build/cand800a/e2_1010_cinc/rep/sta.rpt | grep -E \"\\^|v \" | head -30\r\n                   0.156    0.000    0.000 ^ _4203_/CK (DFF_X1)\r\n     3    8.173    0.076    0.409    0.409 ^ _4203_/Q (DFF_X1)\r\n                   0.076    0.000    0.409 ^ _3317_/A2 (AND3_X4)\r\n     4   16.192    0.047    0.163    0.573 ^ _3317_/ZN (AND3_X4)\r\n                   0.047    0.000    0.573 ^ _3368_/A3 (NAND3_X4)\r\n     2    7.576    0.047    0.067    0.639 v _3368_/ZN (NAND3_X4)\r\n                   0.047    0.000    0.639 v _3370_/B1 (AOI21_X4)\r\n     3   12.964    0.108    0.138    0.777 ^ _3370_/ZN (AOI21_X4)\r\n                   0.108    0.000    0.778 ^ _3400_/B1 (AOI21_X2)\r\n     2    8.426    0.042    0.084    0.861 v _3400_/ZN (AOI21_X2)\r\n                   0.042    0.000    0.861 v _3401_/A1 (NOR2_X4)\r\n     3    6.910    0.059    0.094    0.956 ^ _3401_/ZN (NOR2_X4)\r\n                   0.059    0.000    0.956 ^ _3405_/A2 (NAND2_X1)\r\n     1    2.664    0.029    0.055    1.011 v _3405_/ZN (NAND2_X1)\r\n                   0.029    0.000    1.011 v _3406_/B (XOR2_X1)\r\n     1    3.350    0.037    0.211    1.222 v _3406_/Z (XOR2_X1)\r\n                   0.037    0.000    1.222 v _3407_/A2 (NOR2_X2)\r\n     1    1.419    0.043    0.092    1.314 ^ _3407_/ZN (NOR2_X2)\r\n                   0.043    0.000    1.314 ^ _4262_/D (DFF_X1)\r\n                                     1.250 ^ _4262_/CK (DFF_X1)\r\n"]
[20081.142, "o", "\u001b[2m# write /home/user/elec402-p2-open/notes/REFERENCES_CHECK.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20092.302, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800a/src && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\ns = open('mult_pipe.sv').read()\r\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"    parameter int       PFX       = 0      // CPA=2\"\"\", \"\"\"    parameter bit       CI1       = 1'b0,  // CPA=1: also register block carry-outs for carry-in 1\r\n    parameter int       PFX       = 0      // CPA=2\"\"\")\r\nold = s[s.index(\"        logic [31:0]   s0, s0q;\"):s.index(\"    end else if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\")]\r\nnew = \"\"\"        logic [31:0]   s0, s0q;\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] co0, co0q, co1, co1q, bpq, cin;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_blk\r\n            logic [CSW-1:0] G, P;\r\n            assign {G, P} = prefix(bg_[CSW*i +: CSW], bt_[CSW*i +: CSW]);\r\n            assign s0[CSW*i +: CSW] = bp_[CSW*i +: CSW] ^ {G[CSW-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n            assign co0[i] = G[CSW-1];\r\n            assign co1[i] = G[CSW-1] | P[CSW-1];\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin s0q <= '0; co0q <= '0; end\r\n            else        begin s0q <= s0; co0q <= co0; end\r\n        end\r\n        if (CI1) begin : g_ci1\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) co1q <= RST_N ? co1 : '0;\r\n            assign bpq = co1q;          // carry-out with carry-in 1 (generate | propagate)\r\n        end else begin : g_ci0\r\n            assign co1q = '0;\r\n            for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_bp\r\n                assign bpq[i] = &s0q[CSW*i +: CSW];\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        logic [NB-1:0] bgg;\r\n        logic [31:0]   inc, s0i;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_incb\r\n            for (k = 0; k < CSW; k++) begin : g_k\r\n                if (k == 0) begin : g_k0\r\n                    assign inc[CSW*i] = 1'b1;\r\n                end else begin : g_kn\r\n                    assign inc[CSW*i + k] = &s0q[CSW*i +: k];\r\n                end\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        // block carry: CI1 -> prefix over (co0, co1) as generate / transmit\r\n        assign bgg = bprefix(co0q, bpq);\r\n        assign cin = {bgg[NB-2:0], 1'b0};\r\n        // incremented block sums, reset folded into the early operands; the\r\n        // late block carry only selects\r\n        assign s0i = s0q ^ inc;\r\n        logic [31:0] psum;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < NB; i++) begin : g_inc\r\n            assign psum[CSW*i +: CSW] = ({CSW{cin[i]}} & s0i[CSW*i +: CSW] & {CSW{RST_N}})\r\n                                      | ({CSW{~cin[i]}} & s0q[CSW*i +: CSW] & {CSW{RST_N}});\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= psum;\r\n\"\"\"\r\ns = s.replace(old, new)\r\nopen('mult_pipe.sv','w').write(s)\r\nEOF\r\nsed -i \"s/    localparam int       PFX       = 0;/    localparam int       PFX       = 0;\\n    localparam bit       CI1       = 1'b0;/; s/.CPA(CPA), .PFX(PFX))/.CPA(CPA), .PFX(PFX), .CI1(CI1))/\" mkMultBuff.sv && grep -n \"CI1\" mkMultBuff.sv\r\n56:    localparam bit       CI1       = 1'b0;\r\n107:    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .SEL_REG(SEL_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT), .CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL), .CSW(CSW), .GP4(GP4), .GT(GT), .ORD(ORD), .CPA(CPA), .PFX(PFX), .CI1(CI1))\r\n"]
[20096.055, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m git log --oneline -1 && cat >> notes/WORKLOG.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n## Round 3: minimum flops (RTL optimisation)\r\n\r\n**Merge** of `origin/main` (e1b93d2), which changed SPEC Section 5 and CLAUDE Section 4:\r\n- the 5 % slack target must also hold in sign-off, and slack beyond it is worth nothing;\r\n- area and power are judged on the GPDK045 sign-off results (vectorless power);\r\n- candidates may be submitted to sign-off (about 3 min each, one at a time).\r\n\r\nConsequence: the cost to minimise is flops and cells in the RTL itself. Sign-off synthesises the RTL with its own tool, so our ABC/Resizer knobs only matter for meeting slack in our flow.\r\n\r\n**Tooling.**\r\n- `submission/scripts/eval_candidate.sh RUN RTL_DIR WORK` runs check, synth, sim and power on one candidate and prints slack, area seq/comb, flops, vectorless and activity power, and flops and slack per register group (`submission/scripts/ranks.tcl`). One run takes about 35 s.\r\n- Baseline 800 MHz per group:\r\n\r\n  | group | flops | slack |\r\n  |---|---:|---:|\r\n  | operand + digits | 40 | |\r\n  | PP | 144 | 0.166 |\r\n  | L1 | 117 | 0.368 |\r\n  | L2+3 | 76 | 0.075 |\r\n  | g/p | \u224860 | |\r\n  | csel A | \u224864 | |\r\n  | product | 32 | 0.079 |\r\n  | control | \u224844 | |\r\n\r\n**400 MHz experiments (mine)**, `build/cand400/`. 800 MHz mapping knobs (BUF_X1 driver, 1 fF load, dont-use list) unless noted.\r\n\r\n| candidate | ranks | flops | WNS ns | area (seq/comb) \u00b5m\u00b2 | vectorless \u00b5W | activity run/fill/drain \u00b5W |\r\n|---|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---|\r\n| current (Booth digits, CS after L2, product) | 3 | 166 | +0.224 | 2547 (751/1797) | 664.5 | 677/1566/434 |\r\n| digits, CS after L4 (2 rows, 59 b), product **(p1c4)** | 3 | 149 | +0.207 | 2518 (674/1844) | 663.2 | 659/1607/398 |\r\n| raw operands (recode after reg), CS after L4 (p0c4) | 3 | 141 | +0.110 (+0.073/+0.083 with other knobs) | 3165 (638/2528) | 746.9 | 765/2084/394 |\r\n| p1c4 / p0c4 with the old 400 knobs | 3 | 149 / 141 | \u22120.035 / \u22120.269 | 2341 / 3550 | | |\r\n| 2 ranks: no operand register, CS after L2 (r2c0100) | 2 | 125 | \u22120.314 | 2737 (566/2171) | 800.0 | 882/1629/349 |\r\n| 2 ranks: no operand register, CS after L3 | 2 | 139 | \u22121.100 | 2844 | | |\r\n\r\nNotes on these results:\r\n- 2 ranks with operands and product only is the one-stage multiplier: \u22121.469 ns (see the timing_fail variant).\r\n- The 2-rank designs with logic before the first register fail because the input port, modelled as a DFF_X1 driver, drives 37 loads (0.83 ns) and the product stage also misses (\u22120.155 ns).\r\n- Decision for 400: **p1c4**. The only internal cut is at the narrowest cutset that meets the target (2 carry-save rows, 59 bits), saving 17 flops. Recoding after the register would save another 8 but misses 125 ps in our flow. The 400 knobs in the Makefile change to the 800 knobs.\r\n\r\n**Parallel workers (subagents), one flow each:**\r\n- (a) 800 MHz cut placement and final-adder comparison on the row tree;\r\n- (b) 800 MHz bit-level Dadda/Wallace tree on the Booth PPs, plus 400;\r\n- (c) clock-gating feasibility on p1c4.\r\n\r\n**References** were checked before citing (`notes/REFERENCES_CHECK.md`). Harris's taxonomy page range could not be confirmed, so it is cited without pages.\r\nEOF\r\necho ok\r\n82a3a02 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i\r\nok\r\n"]
[20105.163, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m git add -A notes submission/scripts && git commit -q -m \"Round 3: candidate evaluation script, per-rank report, 400 MHz exploration log, reference check\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126GMUJKG14LrQMZ4a6y2it\" && git push -q origin claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i 2>&1 | tail -1; git status --short | wc -l\r\n0\r\n"]
[20114.681, "o", "\u001b[2m# --- end of turn ---\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20121.255, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cg/a/rtl && cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cg/a/rtl && cp ../../../cand400/p1c4/rtl/*.sv . && cat > clk_gate.sv <<'EOF'\r\n// clk_gate.sv -- technology-independent clock gate (latch + AND), written\r\n// behaviourally. The latch is transparent while clk is low, so 'en' is sampled\r\n// during the low phase and held while clk is high: gclk has no glitches as long\r\n// as 'en' settles before the rising edge (the usual latch-based ICG).\r\nmodule clk_gate (\r\n    input  logic clk,\r\n    input  logic en,     // enable for the NEXT rising edge of clk\r\n    output logic gclk\r\n);\r\n    logic en_l;\r\n    always_latch if (!clk) en_l = en;\r\n    assign gclk = clk & en_l;\r\nendmodule : clk_gate\r\nEOF\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\np='mkMultBuff.sv'; t=open(p).read()\r\nold=\"\"\"    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(clk),\"\"\"\r\nnew=\"\"\"    // clock gate for the multiplier datapath: an edge is needed when an operand\r\n    // pair is accepted, while a product is in ranks 1..LAT-1, and whenever\r\n    // RST_N = 0 (so the synchronous reset of the gated registers still acts, F14)\r\n    wire mclk;\r\n    clk_gate u_cg (.clk(clk), .en(!RST_N | acc | (|v_q[LAT-2:0])), .gclk(mclk));\r\n\r\n    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(mclk),\"\"\"\r\nassert old in t; t=t.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(t)\r\nPY\r\ngrep -n \"mclk\\|u_cg\" mkMultBuff.sv\r\n80:    wire mclk;\r\n81:    clk_gate u_cg (.clk(clk), .en(!RST_N | acc | (|v_q[LAT-2:0])), .gclk(mclk));\r\n84:        u_mult (.clk(mclk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n"]
[20121.942, "o", "\u001b[2m# write /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800b/gen_tree.py\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20124.325, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -i 's/        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= psum;/        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? psum : 32'\"'\"'d0;/' build/cand800a/src/mult_pipe.sv && grep -n \"p <= RST_N ? psum\" build/cand800a/src/mult_pipe.sv && build/cand800a/mk.sh e3_1010_cinc1 CSA_REG=\"4'b1010\" ORD=\"1'b1\" GT=\"1'b1\" CPA=1 CI1=\"1'b1\" 2>&1 | tail -4\r\n329:        always_ff @(posedge clk) p <= RST_N ? psum : 32'd0;\r\ncheck=PASS sim=PASS wns=-0.034 whs=0.020\r\narea=4289.516 seq=2048.466 comb=2241.1 flops=453 vectorless_uW=2277.3\r\nactivity_uW: run:=2586.30 fill:=4811.30 drain:=2012.00 \r\nR1op:40(0.222) PP:144(0.160) L2:92(0.152) GP:60(-0.034) ADD:43(0.271) PROD:32(0.095) CTRL:42(0.149)\r\n"]
