[20595.04, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800b && grep -n \"def fill_stage\" -A 50 gen_tree.py | grep -n \"return cols\" ; grep -n \"fill_stage(cols, b, tg, lo)\\|^pg = \\[\\]\\|pg.append\\|gs = \\[pg\\|BP\\[bi\\] = \\|ks(\\[g for\" gen_tree.py\r\n39:254-    return cols, nf, nh, lo\r\n348:        cols, nf, nh, lo = fill_stage(cols, b, tg, lo)\r\n369:pg = []\r\n372:    if len(bs) == 0: pg.append((ZERO, ZERO))\r\n373:    elif len(bs) == 1: pg.append((bs[0], ZERO))\r\n376:        pg.append((net.xor(x, y), net.and_(x, y) if c + 1 < W else ZERO))\r\n416:    G, P = ks([g for p, g in pg], [p for p, g in pg])\r\n423:        gs = [pg[c][1] for c in range(l, h)]; ps = [pg[c][0] for c in range(l, h)]\r\n430:        BP[bi] = net.or_(Gp[-1], Pp[-1]) if args.cpa == \"csel\" else Pp[-1]\r\n"]
[20599.064, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat >> notes/WORKLOG.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n**Clock gating (worker c, `build/cg/`): rejected.**\r\n- *Implementation:* a technology-independent latch-plus-AND gate in RTL. The enable includes `!RST_N`, so F14 still holds: the SAT check passes 149/149, and a separate SAT proof shows the latch input is 1 during reset. Yosys does not map latches with `dfflibmap`, so an extra mapping to DLL_X1 was needed.\r\n- *Results on p1c4, 400 MHz:*\r\n\r\n  | | baseline | gated |\r\n  |---|---|---|\r\n  | drain window | 398 \u00b5W | 109\u2013196 \u00b5W |\r\n  | whole run | 659 \u00b5W | 503\u2013534 \u00b5W |\r\n  | vectorless estimate (the judged metric) | 663 \u00b5W | 671\u2013842 \u00b5W |\r\n  | SDF check without a clock tree | pass | fails 384/384 |\r\n\r\n- *Why the vectorless estimate rises:* the gated clock net is charged but the port-driven clock is not, and default activities keep the enable mostly on.\r\n- *Why the SDF check fails:* the gating gate reaches the flops 1.4\u20132.0 ns after clk. That skew is invisible to ideal-clock STA, so every product is wrong in SDF simulation.\r\n- *What it would take:* a clock tree (TritonCTS), propagated clocks and hold buffers (variant d3, operand register ungated). Sign-off builds no clock tree, so it would see the failing case.\r\n- *800 MHz:* the same and worse; a tree delay of 0.35\u20130.5 ns is 30\u201340 % of the period.\r\n- *Decision:* no clock gating. The only gain is activity-based, the judged metric gets worse, and sign-off SDF is at risk.\r\nEOF\r\necho ok\r\nok\r\n"]
[20606.585, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800b && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\ns = open(\"gen_tree.py\").read()\r\n# 1. final-stage fill\r\nold = \"# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef emit_stage_comment\"\r\nnew = '''def fill_final(cols):\r\n    \"\"\"last tree stage: every column to <= 2 bits (Dadda rule: half adder when one bit\r\n    over, else full adder), earliest bits into the adders, the latest bit passes\"\"\"\r\n    cols = [list(c) for c in cols]\r\n    nf = nh = 0\r\n    for c in range(W):\r\n        while len(cols[c]) > 2:\r\n            bs = sorted(cols[c], key=lambda b: (b[1], not is_const(b[0])))\r\n            if sum(is_const(b[0]) for b in bs[:2]) == 2:\r\n                cols[c].remove(bs[0]); cols[c].remove(bs[1])\r\n                if c + 1 < W: cols[c + 1].append((ONE, CONST_T))\r\n                continue\r\n            if len(bs) == 3:\r\n                x, y = bs[0], bs[1]\r\n                cols[c].remove(x); cols[c].remove(y)\r\n                s_, cy = ha(x, y); nh += 1\r\n            else:\r\n                x, y, z = bs[0], bs[1], bs[2]\r\n                if is_const(z[0]) and is_const(y[0]):\r\n                    x, y, z = bs[0], bs[1], bs[3]\r\n                for b_ in (x, y, z): cols[c].remove(b_)\r\n                s_, cy = fa(x, y, z); nf += 1\r\n            cols[c].append(s_)\r\n            if c + 1 < W: cols[c + 1].append(cy)\r\n    return cols, nf, nh\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\ndef emit_stage_comment'''\r\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\r\n\r\nold = \"\"\"        cols, nf, nh, lo = fill_stage(cols, b, tg, lo)\"\"\"\r\nnew = \"\"\"        if tg == 0:\r\n            cols, nf, nh = fill_final(cols)\r\n        else:\r\n            cols, nf, nh, lo = fill_stage(cols, b, tg, lo)\"\"\"\r\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\r\n# 2. transmit propagate\r\nold = \"\"\"        pg.append((net.xor(x, y), net.and_(x, y) if c + 1 < W else ZERO))\r\n\"\"\"\r\nnew = \"\"\"        pg.append((net.xor(x, y), net.and_(x, y) if c + 1 < W else ZERO))\r\n        tp[c] = net.or_(x, y)   # transmit (x | y): propagate for the carry prefix\r\n\"\"\"\r\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\r\ns = s.replace(\"pg = []\\n\", \"pg = []\\ntp = {}\\n\", 1)\r\nold = \"\"\"    pg = [(mg[p_], mg[g_]) for p_, g_ in pg]\r\n\"\"\"\r\nnew = \"\"\"    pg = [(mg[p_], mg[g_]) for p_, g_ in pg]\r\n    tp = {}\r\n\"\"\"\r\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\r\nold = \"\"\"lo_c = 0\r\nwhile lo_c\"\"\"\r\nnew = \"\"\"tpr = [tp.get(c, pg[c][0]) for c in range(W)]   # registered p/g: p itself\r\nlo_c = 0\r\nwhile lo_c\"\"\"\r\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\r\ns = s.replace(\"G, P = ks([g for p, g in pg], [p for p, g in pg])\", \"G, P = ks([g for p, g in pg], tpr)\")\r\ns = s.replace(\"gs = [pg[c][1] for c in range(l, h)]; ps = [pg[c][0] for c in range(l, h)]\\n        Gp, Pp = ks(gs, ps)\",\r\n              \"gs = [pg[c][1] for c in range(l, h)]; ps = [pg[c][0] for c in range(l, h)]\\n        Gp, Pp = ks(gs, [tpr[c] for c in range(l, h)])\")\r\nopen(\"gen_tree.py\",\"w\").write(s)\r\nEOF\r\ngrep -n \"Gp, Pp = ks\\|s1\\[c\\] = \" gen_tree.py\r\n457:        Gp, Pp = ks(gs, [tpr[c] for c in range(l, h)])\r\n461:                s1[c] = inv(ps[kk]) if kk == 0 else net.xor(ps[kk], net.or_(Gp[kk - 1], Pp[kk - 1]))\r\n"]
[20612.147, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cd /home/user/elec402-p2-open/build/cand800b && for b in 0.54 0.60 0.66 0.72 0.78; do echo \"== b=$b\"; python3 gen_tree.py /dev/null --mode fill --budgets $b,9 --target 2,0 --gp cpa --k 4 | grep \"R3\\|R4\\|LAT\"; done; for m in wallace dadda; do python3 gen_tree.py /dev/null --mode $m --cuts 2,4 --gp cpa --k 4 | grep \"R3\\|R4\\|LAT\"; done\r\n== b=0.54\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 98, 58, 45, 32] datapath flops=417 FA=94 HA=19\r\n  R3 after fill stage: 54 FA 0 HA, max height 6, model arrival 0.54, 98 flops\r\n  R4 after fill stage: 40 FA 19 HA, max height 2, model arrival 1.02, 58 flops\r\n== b=0.60\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 98, 58, 45, 32] datapath flops=417 FA=94 HA=19\r\n  R3 after fill stage: 54 FA 0 HA, max height 6, model arrival 0.54, 98 flops\r\n  R4 after fill stage: 40 FA 19 HA, max height 2, model arrival 1.02, 58 flops\r\n== b=0.66\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 89, 58, 45, 32] datapath flops=408 FA=94 HA=19\r\n  R3 after fill stage: 63 FA 0 HA, max height 6, model arrival 0.66, 89 flops\r\n  R4 after fill stage: 31 FA 19 HA, max height 2, model arrival 1.02, 58 flops\r\n== b=0.72\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 78, 57, 45, 32] datapath flops=396 FA=95 HA=18\r\n  R3 after fill stage: 74 FA 0 HA, max height 5, model arrival 0.72, 78 flops\r\n  R4 after fill stage: 21 FA 18 HA, max height 2, model arrival 0.84, 57 flops\r\n== b=0.78\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 77, 57, 45, 32] datapath flops=395 FA=95 HA=18\r\n  R3 after fill stage: 75 FA 0 HA, max height 5, model arrival 0.78, 77 flops\r\n  R4 after fill stage: 20 FA 18 HA, max height 2, model arrival 0.84, 57 flops\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 86, 59, 43, 32] datapath flops=404 FA=92 HA=55\r\n  R3 after level 2: 66 FA 24 HA, model arrival 0.72, 86 flops\r\n  R4 after level 4: 26 FA 31 HA, model arrival 0.66, 59 flops\r\nLAT=6 ranks=[40, 144, 104, 60, 45, 32] datapath flops=425 FA=91 HA=22\r\n  R3 after level 2: 45 FA 16 HA, model arrival 0.72, 104 flops\r\n  R4 after level 4: 46 FA 6 HA, model arrival 0.66, 60 flops\r\n"]
[20612.154, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m SP=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca/scratchpad && git worktree add -q $SP/wt_c400 -b cand/c400-p1c4 HEAD 2>&1 | tail -1; cp build/cand400/p1c4/rtl/*.sv $SP/wt_c400/submission/rtl_400/ && cd $SP/wt_c400 && git add submission/rtl_400 && git commit -q -m \"Sign-off candidate: 400 MHz p1c4 (3 ranks, 149 flops); 800 MHz unchanged\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126GMUJKG14LrQMZ4a6y2it\" && git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/check/c400-p1c4 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1; date -u +%H:%M\r\nremote: \r\n0fbf037 Sign-off candidate: 400 MHz p1c4 (3 ranks, 149 flops); 800 MHz unchanged\r\n08:17\r\nShell cwd was reset to /home/user/elec402-p2-open\r\n"]
