[23553.796, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-elec402-p2-open/6503db16-82a0-5ee1-9a2e-83eb2b44d2ca/tasks/bc1a1t1w8.output\r\n# Sign-off check check/final\r\n\r\nCommit `efbfecdf64f2`, checked 2026-11-08 09:06 UTC.\r\n\r\nEach implementation is synthesized with the GPDK045 library under the constraints of SPEC.md Section 6. The resulting netlists are simulated with SDF back-annotation against an independent testbench that samples outputs at the rising edge.\r\n\r\n| Check | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| GPDK045 static timing, 400 MHz at 2.5 ns | WNS 203 ps, meets the slack target (target 125 ps) |\r\n| GPDK045 cell area, 400 MHz | 2660.8 \u00b5m\u00b2, within budget (limit 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2) |\r\n| GPDK045 power estimate, 400 MHz | 215.2 \u00b5W (vectorless) |\r\n| GPDK045 static timing, 800 MHz at 1.25 ns | WNS 158 ps, meets the slack target (target 62 ps) |\r\n| GPDK045 cell area, 800 MHz | 4416.2 \u00b5m\u00b2, within budget (limit 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2) |\r\n| GPDK045 power estimate, 800 MHz | 829.7 \u00b5W (vectorless) |\r\n| Gate-level simulation with SDF, 400 MHz at 2.5 ns | Pass, 1204/1204 products, 0 timing-check messages |\r\n| Gate-level simulation with SDF, 800 MHz at 1.25 ns | Pass, 1162/1162 products, 0 timing-check messages |\r\n| 400 MHz netlist at 1.25 ns (informational: normally fails, which shows that violations are detected) | Fail, 0/0 products, 3754 timing-check messages; violated F1 F2 F4 F5 F6 F8 F9 STALL |\r\n\r\n[exited with code 0]\r\n"]
[23564.204, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m python3 - <<'EOF'\r\nvals={'S4A':'2660.8','S4P':'215.2','S4W':'203','S4N':'1204 of 1204','S8A':'4416.2','S8P':'829.7','S8W':'158','S8N':'1162 of 1162'}\r\nfor p in ['submission/pdf_report/src/report.md','submission/pdf_report/src/signoff.md']:\r\n    s=open(p).read()\r\n    if p.endswith('signoff.md'):\r\n        a=s.index('Both flows meet the slack target, but the margins differ.')\r\n        s=s[:a]+'''Both flows meet the slack target with different margins: at 400 MHz, 203 ps in sign-off against 263 ps in our flow, and at 800 MHz, 158 against 140 ps. The scorecard does not state its corner. A commercial synthesis tool closes timing to the constraint and then recovers area with the slack it has left, so its margin says little about raw speed. GPDK045 area is 8.6 % (400 MHz) and 9.9 % (800 MHz) larger than ours. Its vectorless power is 2.9 and 2.6 times lower, which reflects the different library, supply voltage and default activity rather than the designs. Both flows ranked every flip-flop reduction the same way. The one disagreement was the Wallace tree at 800 MHz, where our flow showed 1.8 % less area and sign-off showed 11.2 % more power. The judged sign-off result decided that choice.\r\n'''\r\n    for k,v in vals.items(): s=s.replace(k,v)\r\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\r\nEOF\r\ngrep -c \"S[48][APWNRQ]\" submission/pdf_report/src/report.md submission/pdf_report/src/signoff.md; grep -n \"Since the last revision\" submission/pdf_report/src/report.md | cut -c1-80\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/src/report.md:0\r\nsubmission/pdf_report/src/signoff.md:0\r\n12:Two implementations of `mkMultBuff` were built, one for a 2.5 ns clock and on\r\n"]
[23587.393, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -i 's/both flows return no product; the sign-off simulator also reports its timing-check violations directly./both flows return no product. The sign-off simulator also reports its timing-check violations directly./' submission/pdf_report/src/signoff.md && cat >> notes/WORKLOG.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n**Final sign-off** (`check/final`, efbfecd, checked 09:06 UTC). Results are identical to the candidate checks.\r\n\r\n| | area | vectorless power | WNS | SDF simulation |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 400 MHz | 2660.8 \u00b5m\u00b2 | 215.2 \u00b5W | 203 ps | 1204/1204 |\r\n| 800 MHz | 4416.2 \u00b5m\u00b2 | 829.7 \u00b5W | 158 ps | 1162/1162 |\r\n\r\nThe informational check (the 400 MHz netlist at 1.25 ns) fails, as it should.\r\n\r\nAgainst the previous designs this is \u22123.3 % area and \u22124.2 % power at 400 MHz, and \u221222.2 % area and \u221226.0 % power at 800 MHz.\r\n\r\n**Report** rewritten for round 3 at the same length. New sections:\r\n- the cost model (cutset width, retiming and initial states);\r\n- the 400 MHz rank analysis and Wallace cutsets;\r\n- the 800 MHz rank and adder decisions;\r\n- a candidate table with the sign-off decision;\r\n- clock gating;\r\n- new datapath figures.\r\n\r\nNew references (Parhi, Leiserson-Saxe, Touati-Brayton, Townsend et al., Harris, Han-Carlson, Sklansky, Brent-Kung) were checked first (`notes/REFERENCES_CHECK.md`).\r\nEOF\r\ngit add -A submission notes && git commit -q -m \"Report: final sign-off numbers and comparison\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126GMUJKG14LrQMZ4a6y2it\" && git push -q origin claude/focused-dijkstra-3f079i 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1\r\n8067f90 Report: final sign-off numbers and comparison\r\n"]
